  "raw": {
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0202-JW-Nicholson-Hall/Grants-Manager----Manager-of-Grant-and-Travel-administration-_R00120246": {
      "title": "Grants Manager - (Manager of Grant and Travel administration)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Grants Manager - (Manager of Grant and Travel administration)     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM Science - PA - Administration (Laurie Rea (00003523))     Work Location: 0202 J.W. Nicholson Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The Department of Physics & Astronomy administrative team is seeking a full-time grant and travel manager. The Grant & Travel Manager is responsible for the post‑award administration of all departmental grants and contracts, as well as comprehensive oversight of departmental travel administration. This role ensures accurate financial management, compliance with university and sponsor regulations, and efficient coordination of grant and travel processes. The position supervises and trains staff, manages financial workflows, and serves as a key liaison between faculty, department leadership, and central administrative offices. Strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage complex financial and administrative tasks are essential. Responsibilities: Grant & Contract Management (50% effort) • Manages the department post award administration of grants and contracts. • Reconciles grant accounts and ensures accuracy of financial data. • Monitors financial activity on grant, contract, and cost share accounts for compliance. • Conducts long range financial planning and provides forecasting support to faculty. • Analyzes and audits daily business expenditures to ensure compliance with sponsor and university standards. • Prepares and processes account corrections. Faculty Support & Compliance • Informs and advises faculty on allowable costs, budgetary elements, and sponsor guidelines. • Provides guidance on proposal budgeting related to overhead, fringe benefits, fees, and university financial requirements. • Interprets sponsor regulations and ensures that all expenditures align with award terms and conditions. • Offers proactive financial consultations regarding budget status, spending rates, and compliance issues. Liaison & Coordination • Serves as departmental liaison with: Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP); Sponsored Program Accounting (SPA); and Other university administrative units • Communicates policy updates, reporting requirements, and procedural changes. Travel Administration (30% effort) • Responsible for managing all aspects of the department’s travel administration. • Oversees, supervises, and trains direct reports involved in coordinating travel arrangements and reimbursements. • Serves as the backup travel coordinator for the department. • Ensures travel requests, approvals, and reimbursements comply with university, state, and sponsor policies. Audit & Quality Control • Conducts annual audits of travel arrangement and reimbursement processes. • Identifies opportunities to improve efficiency, accuracy, and compliance. • Implements improvements to streamline workflows and enhance service quality. Policy Communication & Training • Keeps faculty and staff informed of changes to travel systems, policies, and procedures. • Provides ongoing training and support related to travel platforms, documentation, and compliance requirements. Supervision (15% effort) • Directly supervises a full-time Grant/Travel Coordinator. • Provides mentorship, performance feedback, and workflow direction. • Promotes professional effectiveness and fosters a collaborative, service-oriented work environment. Other Duties as Assigned (5% effort ) Minimum qualifications: Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance or a related field with 3 years of related experience. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply--a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred qualifications: 6-10 years of experience in the following: Experience in higher education, research administration, or sponsored programs. Knowledge of university financial systems and travel software. Experience making travel arrangements and financial reconciling. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast‑paced environment. Required Skills Strong understanding of post‑award grant administration and sponsored research regulations. Demonstrated financial management abilities, including reconciliation, forecasting, and auditing. Experience managing travel processes and reimbursement workflows. Excellent supervisory and training skills. High attention to detail; strong analytical and problem‑solving abilities. Ability to interpret complex sponsor guidelines and university policies. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously. Proficiency with financial/accounting systems, spreadsheets, and travel management platforms.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. Please provide letter of application, resume, and three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire (if applicable). For questions regarding pay or the status of your application, please reach out to Laurie Rea at lrea@lsu.edu     Skills Needed: Conflict Management, Financial Acumen, Precise Decision Making, Process Improvements, Resource Management, Stakeholder Management, Strategic Thinking, Training People     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 9, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): N     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Veterinary-Medicine/Veterinary-Technician-1--2--or-3-Food-Animal_R00120050-1": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician 1, 2, or 3-Food Animal",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Veterinary Technician 1, 2, or 3-Food Animal     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM VetMed - VTH - Admin - Nursing - Food Animal (Dawn Lou-Wese Kelley (00001329))     Work Location: Veterinary Medicine     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The Large Animal Hospital provides patient care 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. This position provides technical veterinary support to faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students in the Food Animal department and throughout the Large Animal Hospital. The individual must possess extensive experience in the safe handling and restraint of livestock and be capable of instructing veterinary students in proper animal handling techniques while promoting a safe learning environment for both personnel and patients. This position supports the care and management of emergency and critical care cases during both regular business hours and after-hours operations. The individual is expected to consistently adhere to hospital infection prevention and biosecurity protocols to maintain a safe environment for patients, clients, students, and staff. Patient care responsibilities include, but are not limited to, providing technical support in the Food Animal Department, Isolation Unit, Large Animal Intensive Care Unit (LAICU), resident teaching herd, as well as equine services. The position requires flexibility to assist throughout the hospital as needed to ensure the delivery of high-quality patient care and support the hospital's teaching, clinical, and service missions. Veterinary Technician 1: 30%-Assist with the day-to-day operations of the Food Animal Department and  Large Animal Hospital, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with appointments, emergency cases, medical procedures, and inpatient treatments. Assist with providing proper patient handling, restraint, inpatient monitoring, hourly patient assessments, and treatment administration. Safely unload, load, admit, transfer, and discharge large animal patients, and prepare examination and treatment areas before and after procedures by setting up, cleaning, disinfecting, and restocking equipment and supplies. Complete all duties with minimal supervision while adhering to established hospital policies, safety procedures, and biosecurity protocols. 20%-Assist with client communication, ensuring effective communication and accurate collection of patient information. Monitor patients throughout the hospital; assist with treatments as prescribed by clinicians; maintain accurate and complete medical records; and enter and track charges for large animal inpatients and outpatients. Assist veterinary students and student workers with clinical procedures and treatments while promoting proper techniques and quality patient care. 20%-Assist with clinical teaching and training of veterinary students and newly hired  veterinary technicians, assistants, and student workers. Assist clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, including bandaging, sample collection, blood transfusions, ultrasonography, joint injections, intravenous catheter placement, and other clinical treatments. 15%-Assist with the routine maintenance and cleaning of technical equipment, including endoscopes, ultrasound machines, ECG equipment, oxygen tanks, and other clinical instruments. Maintain hospital readiness by stocking and cleaning examination rooms, treatment areas, carts, and supplies. Assist in training veterinary students and new staff on hospital protocols, including biosecurity and infection prevention procedures.  10%-Participate in holiday, weekend, and on-call emergency coverage as required. 5%-Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician.   Preferred: Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and one year of related experience.  Veterinary Technician 2: 30%-Perform the day-to-day operations of the Food Animal Department and Large Animal Hospital, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with appointments, emergency cases, medical procedures, and inpatient treatments. Provide proper patient handling, restraint, inpatient monitoring, hourly patient assessments, and treatment administration. Safely unload, load, admit, transfer, and discharge large animal patients, and prepare examination and treatment areas before and after procedures by setting up, cleaning, disinfecting, and restocking equipment and supplies. Complete all duties with minimal supervision while adhering to established hospital policies, safety procedures, and biosecurity protocols. 20%-Perform client communication, ensuring effective communication and accurate collection of patient information. Monitor patients throughout the hospital; assist with treatments as prescribed by clinicians; maintain accurate and complete medical records; and enter and track charges for large animal inpatients and outpatients. Support veterinary students and student workers with clinical procedures and treatments while promoting proper techniques and quality patient care. 20%-Participate in clinical teaching and training of veterinary students and newly hired  veterinary technicians, assistants, and student workers. Support clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, including bandaging, sample collection, blood transfusions, ultrasonography, joint injections, intravenous catheter placement, and other clinical treatments. 15%-Perform the routine maintenance and cleaning of technical equipment, including endoscopes, ultrasound machines, ECG equipment, oxygen tanks, and other clinical instruments. Maintain hospital readiness by stocking and cleaning examination rooms, treatment areas, carts, and supplies. Support the training of veterinary students and new staff on hospital protocols, including biosecurity and infection prevention procedures.  10%-Participate in holiday, weekend, and on-call emergency coverage as required. 5%-Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and have two years of related experience.   Preferred:  Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and three years of related experience.  Veterinary Technician 3: 30%-Perform and teach the day-to-day operations of the Food Animal Department and  Large Animal Hospital, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with appointments, emergency cases, medical procedures, and inpatient treatments. Provide proper patient handling, restraint, inpatient monitoring, hourly patient assessments, and treatment administration. Safely unload, load, admit, transfer, and discharge large animal patients, and prepare examination and treatment areas before and after procedures by setting up, cleaning, disinfecting, and restocking equipment and supplies. Complete all duties with minimal supervision while adhering to established hospital policies, safety procedures, and biosecurity protocols. 20%-Perform and teach client communication, ensuring effective communication and accurate collection of patient information. Monitor patients throughout the hospital; assist with treatments as prescribed by clinicians; maintain accurate and complete medical records; and enter and track charges for large animal inpatients and outpatients. Instruct and support veterinary students and student workers with clinical procedures and treatments while promoting proper techniques and quality patient care. 20%-Instruct and participate in clinical teaching and training of veterinary students and newly hired  veterinary technicians, assistants, and student workers. Teach and support clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, including bandaging, sample collection, blood transfusions, ultrasonography, joint injections, intravenous catheter placement, and other clinical treatments. 15%-Perform and teach the routine maintenance and cleaning of technical equipment, including endoscopes, ultrasound machines, ECG equipment, oxygen tanks, and other clinical instruments. Maintain hospital readiness by stocking and cleaning examination rooms, treatment areas, carts, and supplies. Instruct veterinary students and new staff on hospital protocols, including biosecurity and infection prevention procedures.  10%-Participate in holiday, weekend, and on-call emergency coverage as required. 5%-Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and have four years of related experience.    Preferred : Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and five years of related experience.  Job Skills Needed for All Levels: Is comfortable working around and safely handling cattle, swine, and small ruminants Math skills; including drug calculations (dosage & conversions)  Has a working knowledge of large animal husbandry Has working knowledge of common large animal disease processes, injuries, and ailments. Is able to read and understand patient treatment flow sheets and carry out orders. Is able to work in the large animal hospital to carry out treatments with minimum supervision Knowledge of medical terminology, basic anatomy, and abbreviations Proper administration of oral, sub-cutaneous, intramuscular, and intra venous medications Basic computer skills, problem-solving and communication skills    Knowledge of proper medical record keeping (paper and electronic)     Additional Job Description: Required to work a variety of shifts including nights, weekends, holidays, on-call, and emergency response.  Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the general public, or cause significant damage to University property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. Essential Personnel - This position may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. Physical Demands- This position requires frequent and constant physical activities such as: standing, sitting, walking, bending, reach above and below shoulders, twisting, pushing/pulling, grasping, squatting, and ability to lift >50+lbs. Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if applicable). Please provide your resume and three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. Questions can be directed to Dawn Kelley, prplrein@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 3, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Veterinary-Medicine/Veterinary-Technician-1--2--or-3-Anesthesia_R00120009": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician 1, 2, or 3-Anesthesia",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Veterinary Technician 1, 2, or 3-Anesthesia     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM VetMed - VTH - Admin - Nursing - Anesthesia (Torri Rae Collins (00006295))     Work Location: Veterinary Medicine     Pay Grade:     Job Description: This position provides anesthesia and anesthetic support for all clinical service areas, including Small Animal Internal Medicine, Small Animal Surgery, specialty small animal services, and all Large Animal clinical services. Responsibilities include preparing and monitoring patients before, during, and after anesthesia; assisting faculty clinicians and house officers with anesthetic procedures; and ensuring the safe delivery of anesthesia in accordance with established hospital protocols. The individual must possess expertise in the safe handling and restraint of small animals and be able to provide instruction and guidance to veterinary students in anesthesia techniques, patient monitoring, and proper animal handling while fostering a safe and effective clinical learning environment.   Veterinary Technician 1: 35%-Assist with all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Assist with providing technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Assist with the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Assist with the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Assist with routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Assist with ensuring immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Participate in providing emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician.   Preferred: Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and one year of related experience.  Veterinary Technician 2: 35%-Perform and demonstrate all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Provide technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Perform and demonstrate the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Participate in the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Perform and demonstrate routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Ensure immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Perform and demonstrate emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned.   Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and have two years of related experience.   Preferred: Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and three years of related experience.  Veterinary Technician 3: 35%-Perform and teach all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Provide technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Perform and teach the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Participate in the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Perform and teach routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Ensure immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Perform and teach emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned.  Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology AND must be actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and have four years of related experience.    Preferred: Actively licensed with the Louisiana Board of Veterinary Medicine as a Registered Veterinary Technician and five years of related experience.  Job Skills Needed for All Levels: Knowledge of basic animal care and handling including restraint   Knowledge of medical terminology, basic anatomy, and abbreviations Basic computer skills, problem-solving and communication skills    Knowledge of proper medical record keeping (paper and electronic) Math skills; including drug calculations (dosage & conversions)  Operation of equipment, diagnostic tests and hand held analyzers  Ability to work independently with minimal supervision  Ability to collect blood from  a number of different sites by venipuncture Proper administration of oral, sub-cutaneous, intra muscular, and intra venous medications Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignment simultaneously     Additional Job Description: Essential Personnel - Required to work a variety of shifts including nights, weekends, holidays, on-call, and emergency response.  Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the general public, or cause significant damage to University property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. Physical Requirements - Required to be capable of more than 50 pounds, standing or walking for prolonged periods, able to reach above and below the shoulder, vision (near sight), vision (far sight), kneel or sit on the floor, push/pulling, grasping, crawling, twisting, squatting, climbing, sitting, and/or bending Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if applicable). Please provide your resume and three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. Questions can be directed to Torri Collins, tcollins@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 3, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-St-Tammany-Parish-Extension-Office/Assistant-Associate-Extension-Agent--Nutrition-_R00120176": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAG PL4 - Southeast - Parish - Washington (Amy Marie Varnado (00082119))     Work Location: 0101 St. Tammany Parish Extension Office     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Work Location:  This position serves stakeholders in St. Tammany and Washington Parishes in Southeast Louisiana. Fifty percent of the employee’s time and Extension educational efforts will be dedicated to programming and service delivery in St. Tammany Parish and 50 percent will support Extension educational efforts in St. Washington Parish. The assigned domicile office is located in Covington, LA. Together, the two parishes encompass a combined population of 323,844 residents. The LSU AgCenter’s Healthy Communities Program is designed to reach citizens within their communities with health, wellness, and nutrition information and food buying and preparation skills with the goal of achieving increased knowledge and behavioral change leading to healthier lifestyles to impact the trend of increased obesity and related chronic diseases such as Type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, heart disease, and stroke. Job Description:  The Assistant/Associate Nutrition & Community Health (NCH) Extension Agent is responsible for delivering community-based nutrition education with a focus on healthy eating, physical activity, weight management, general health and wellness, and chronic disease prevention. The agent will conduct nutrition education programs throughout the year, primarily targeting Louisiana’s adult population, with youth programming offered as time and requests allow. Most programming will include an interactive educational session and food demonstration and/or tasting to engage participants and reinforce healthy eating practices. The agent will lead efforts in planning, implementing, conducting, evaluating, and reporting interventions that involve food, nutrition, physical activity, and general health. Additional responsibilities include participating in participant recruitment, community outreach, health expos, health fairs, and Ag Extension events. Agents are expected to highlight NCH programs in the assigned parish(es) and distribute nutrition education through in-person sessions, print media, local public media, mass media, social media, and other communication platforms. The agent will be comfortable working with diverse audiences and delivering education to groups with various learning styles. Agents will be aware of community, city/town, parish, and regional partnerships, resources, and contacts which can help support local and parish NCH programming. The agent will organize and maintain an advisory committee composed of local government officials, volunteers, health professionals, and community residents to identify and address local nutrition-related needs. As an AgCenter Extension employee, the agent must be committed to ongoing professional development, staying abreast of current trends in nutrition, and sharing evidence-based nutrition information related to specific program topics with the public. This position requires occasional overnight travel and availability to work evenings and weekends to meet community needs. The agent will serve under the supervision and guidance of the parish chair, regional director, NCH regional coordinator, and NCH state office staff.   The agent may be assigned other tasks by supervisors and is expected to collaborate with other Extension faculty at parish, regional, and state levels. Qualification Requirements:    A baccalaureate degree in nutrition, family and consumer sciences, human sciences, vocational education or a closely related field from an accredited college or university is required. A registered dietician with community experience is preferred. Persons with only an undergraduate degree must have a minimum 2.5 overall grade-point average based on a 4-point grading system. If the applicant has pursued any graduate courses, the grade-point average of all graduate work must be at least 3.0 on a 4.0 system. The applicant must demonstrate effective oral and written communication skills. Experience in recruiting, training and supervising adults and volunteers and experience in teaching and applying principles of leadership development to both youth and adult audiences is also desired. Knowledge of public relations and the ability to cope with change are highly desirable characteristics. Ability to work with and through others is essential as is the ability to function with minimum supervision. The successful candidate will exemplify a positive attitude and a passion to improve the lives of others. Some overnight, weekend and evening work may be required. Salary and Benefits:  Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Conditions of Employment:  A personal automobile and appropriate insurance coverage is required (travel allowance provided).  Satisfactory completion of one specific graduate level extension courses (3 credit hours) is required in year two or three of employment, prior to promotion eligibility to associate agent.  Additionally, a faculty member who does not have a related master’s degree must complete an additional 12 hours of related graduate level coursework in order to be promoted to associate agent and such promotion must occur in the first seven years of employment.  An exception is that additional agent experience may be substituted for 12 hours of coursework, but not for the required course.  Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline:  October 4, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure:  Apply online at  https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU  (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching cover letter with resume including a statement of professional interest and goals, official university transcripts, and two letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Dr. Vadel Shivers Nutrition and Community Health Regional Coordinator 9050 Airline Highway Suite 120 Baton Rouge, LA  70815 Email: vshivers@agcenter.lsu.edu   Ph: (225) 963-6344 Website: www.lsuagcenter.com   The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment. An Equal Opportunity Employer.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions:     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Campbell-B-Hodges-Hall/Professional-in-Residence--Public-Relations-_R00120174-1": {
      "title": "Professional-in-Residence (Public Relations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Professional-in-Residence (Public Relations)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Manship School of Mass Communication (Kim Bissell (00082011))     Work Location: Campbell B. Hodges Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The LSU Manship School of Mass Communication invites applications for a nine-month, non-tenure track position as a Professional-In-Residence for the Public Relations area to begin in Spring 2027. We seek a distinguished communication practitioner to teach four courses per semester in the Manship School undergraduate core curriculum and/or courses in public relations, strategic communication, corporate communication, crisis communications and courses related to their areas of expertise. Job Responsibilities: Teach four undergraduate courses per semester in the Manship School of Mass Communication and develop a portfolio of service activities. The PIR may assist with supervision of undergraduate research and creative work in lieu of a fourth course. 100% Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in public relations, mass communication, or related field; 7 years of experience. Degree Substitute : Bachelor's degree in public relations, mass communication, or related field with professional work-related experience that clearly documents the qualifications to teach the course; 10 or more years of industry-related professional experience. Additional Requirements: FERPA -As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide cover letter, resume, (3) professional references and transcripts. Official transcripts, if needed are required prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. Chun Yang at cyang10@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): October 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0112-Audubon-Sugar-Institute-Building/Compliance-and-Event-Coordinator_R00120162": {
      "title": "Compliance and Event Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Compliance and Event Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM FA - CSPER - PTS - PS - Event Services (Bruce Tate (00067971) (Inherited))     Work Location: 0112 Audubon Sugar Institute Building     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: The Compliance and Event Coordinator supports the planning and execution of parking and transportation operations for campus events and provides operational support for parking compliance activities. Reporting to the Compliance and Event Manager, the coordinator organizes routine event logistics, staffing information, maps, post orders, equipment, and records. The Compliance and Event Coordinator assist with compliance deployment and quality review and maintains accurate operational data and documentation. The position works across PTS teams and with campus partners to ensure event plans and compliance procedures are communicated and carried out consistently. Job Responsibilities Coordinate routing parking and transportation logistics for campus events under the direction of the Compliance and Event Manager. Gather event requirements, including anticipated attendance, parking demand, traffic flow, access, staffing, signage, barricades, reserved parking, ADA accommodations, shuttle needs, equipment, and customer communications considerations. Prepare and maintain event operating materials such as maps, timelines, staffing rosters, post orders, contact lists, setup instructions, checklists, and contingency information. Coordinate event setup, equipment distribution, staff check-in, post assignments, real-time updates, and demobilization as assigned Communicate approved event plans and changes to PTS employees, event organizers, vendors, and campus partners. (35%) Support daily parking compliance operations through deployment coordination, coverage tracking, field communication, and documentation. Monitor assigned areas for compliance concerns and communicate emerging patterns, safety issues, or resource needs to the manager. Assist with citation quality review, activity reporting, complaint research, documentation gathering, and trend analysis while referring policy decisions and complex cases to the manager. Reinforce approved enforcement procedures, customer service standards, safety practices, and event-specific instructions in the field. Provide coverage or operational assistance during peak periods, major events, construction impacts, closures, and other special circumstances as assigned. (30%) Prepare draft schedules, event staffing requests, assignments, and coverage plans for manager approval; track attendance, call-outs, substitutions, and overtime information. Maintain organized event and compliance records, including plans, rosters, reports, permits or reservations, partner requests, equipment logs, and after-action materials. Track event supplies and operational equipment such as signs, cones, barricades, radios, vests, handheld devices, and credentials; coordinate availability and report repair or replacement needs. Support cost estimates, purchase documentation, vendor coordination, invoices, event billing records, and internal reconciliation as assigned. (15%) Enter, maintain, and validate information in relevant parking, event, scheduling, payment, citation, mapping, and recordkeeping systems. Prepare routine reports and dashboards on event activity, staffing, citations, incidents, resource use, service concerns, and other operational measures. Identify data-quality or process issues and recommend practical improvements to forms, checklists, workflows, reports, and recurring event plans. Provide basic operational support for T2, ParkMobile, MPS Safety Sticks, Offstreet, handheld devices, radios, and related platforms within assigned access and training. (10%) Respond to routine event and compliance questions and provide accurate information in a professional, timely, and service-oriented manner. Maintain productive working relationships with campus departments and event partners, document requests and commitments, and ensure follow-up items are completed. Refer exceptions, policy interpretations, sensitive complaints, personnel matters, and significant operational conflicts to the Compliance and Event Manager. (5%) Other duties as assigned. (5%) Additional Requirements This position requires a valid driver's license, will require an MVR, and is subject to drug screens per PM-33/PS-67/FASOP HR-04. This position is considered emergency essential and may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree with related experience LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Minimum Certifications/Licenses LA Class E Driver's License or equivalent     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Sherry Blattenberger at sblatt2@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Artistic Vision, Audience Engagement, Brand Stewardship, Collaboration, Communication, Content Development, Detail-Oriented, Project Coordination     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 4, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 4, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
