    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0123-University-Administration/Financial-Accountant_R00120157": {
      "title": "Financial Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Financial Accountant     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSU System Chief Financial Officer - Business Office (Brandi Lopez (00080219))     Work Location: 0123 University Administration     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The LSU System office Financial Accountant reports to the Business Manager, LSU System Office of the President. This position is responsible for the compilation, preparation, review, and submission of accounting transactions and reports on the LSU System. A successful candidate must exhibit a high level of confidentiality and professionalism. Job Responsibilities: 40%- Governmental and Institutional Reporting - Assists in preparing responses to requests from various stakeholders including but not limited to: 1) monitoring and compiling fiscal note requests to report potential financial impact to all LSU System campuses of bills proposed during legislative session; 2) coordination and compilation of the Quarterly Receivable & Bad Debt Report to the Louisiana OSRSP; 3) coordination and compilation of the annual Accounts Receivable Write-off Report for BOS approval; 4) coordination and compilation of the System Investment Report; 5) coordination and preparation of the Semi-Annual Financial Report to the BOS; 6) Affiliated Entities Report; and 7) ad hoc reports. 30%- Departmental Accounting– Completes accounting and business transactions in LSU’s Workday Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system including deposits of checks, creation of journal entries, creation of procurement requisitions, and invoice processing. Monitors and reconciles ledgers for the LSU System departmental and LSU Foundation accounts 15%-Assists with Budget Preparation – Reviews, coordinates, and compiles all LSU system campuses’ budget request forms for submission to the Board of Regents and the Louisiana Office of Planning and Budget. 10%-Serves as Asset Custodian for the LSU System Office of the President and Health Affairs; orders supplies, and processes vendor payments for departmental operations and events. 5%- Assists with special projects as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting or related field with at least one year of relevant experience in higher education.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary range, please contact Brandi Lopez at blope16@lsu.edu. This position has access to/directly handles cash/funds. Financial history/credit check required per FASOP HR-04.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Adaptability, Analytical Reasoning, Budget Forecasting, Collaboration, Detail-Oriented, Ethics, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): January 1, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1144-Ruffin-G-Pleasant-Hall/Financial-Aid-Counselor--Online_R00120154": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor/ Online",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Financial Aid Counselor/ Online     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - EM - Rec - FAS - FA - LSU Online (Abby Spires (00314883))     Work Location: 1144 Ruffin G. Pleasant Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description:   The Online Financial Aid Counselor position within Louisiana State University’s Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships will play a key collaborative role in advancing the university and meeting the student access objectives.  The individual, with general oversight from the Senior Online Financial Aid Coordinator, will be responsible for maintaining financial aid communication with current and prospective students and families.   Financial Aid Counseling (60%)   Counsels and advises prospective and enrolled students in all matters pertaining to federal and state financial aid programs, including but not limited to Federal Pell Grants, Federal Supplemental Educational Opportunity Grants, TEACH Grants, Federal Work-Study, and Direct Loan Programs.  This interaction may include phone, in-person, virtual or written contacts.  The employee must be accurate in describing financial aid policies, criteria and procedures. Individual must be responsive to prospective students’ concerns and needs by providing excellent customer service. Performs detailed and personalized outreach to prospective and continuing students such as: phone calling, emailing, and other communications as needed.  Responsible for assisting students in resolving problems associated with the application processes for federal and state programs, the electronic loan transmission process and the correction process.  Evaluates and processes requests for “special circumstances” and “petitions for independent status” presented by students in determining eligibility for the federal programs.   Financial Aid Operations (30%) Resolves overaward situations, which involves reducing one or more aid programs because of receipt of additional resources or conflicting financial information.  Must inform students, contact appropriate agencies, and return proceeds. Serves as a rotating member of the satisfactory academic progress appeals committee. Assist with the examination, review and certification of direct plus loan request. Reviews daily correspondence and award letters in their respective alphabetical breakdown to ensure accuracy and perform quality assurance.  Aid in the retention of students through direct outreach to at risk populations, providing students with a thorough understanding of resources and polices.    Special projects as assigned (10%) Serves as the secondary liaison to Digital and Continuing Education, responding to all inquiries student’s needs are met in a timely manner. Including, but not limited to assigned committees and outreach projects.  Represent LSU and the Office of Enrollment Management at professional functions and recruiting events.    Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Meets eligibility to obtain National Student Loan Database System access and must not be in default on a student loan.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in financial aid or equivalent student service setting higher education.  Our ideal candidate possesses the following qualities: Knowledge of best practices in financial aid Strong team orientation, effective interpersonal skills, and superior written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated commitment to data-driven decision-making, including effective analytical skills and proven results in achieving objectives and goals. As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The location of this position is LSU-BR and is not eligible for remote work. To be considered, qualified candidates will submit a complete application which includes a cover letter explaining their specific interest in the position and how their skills and experiences prepare them for success in this role, a resume, and three professional references. Please provide resume and transcripts, if applicable. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Abby Spires at aspire5@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Communication, Confidentiality, Critical Thinking, Customer-Focused, Decision Making, Policy Knowledge, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): January 1, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Student-Health-Center-Cl-Infirmary-Building/Assistant-Medical-Director_R00120151": {
      "title": "Assistant Medical Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Medical Director     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - H&WB - SHC - Medical and Ancillary Services (Amy R Ordeneaux (00007157))     Work Location: Student Health Center (C&l Infirmary) Building     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Louisiana State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Medical Director. Located in the Student Health Center (SHC) and reporting to the Medical Director, the Assistant Medical Director is responsible for providing student-focused leadership and serves as a lead clinical member in the primary care clinic, the specialty clinics, and the supporting ancillary services as well as providing direct patient care. The Assistant Director must possess a deep appreciation for a collaborative care model and a commitment to advancing the divisional priorities and cultivating a working relationship with Our Lady of the Lake Health.   GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES FOR THIS POSITION:   Delivers high-quality, evidence-based medical care to the student population, with a focus on preventive, maintenance, and restorative health services. Provides direct primary care for students, including assessment, testing, diagnosis, treatment and referral, performs minor surgical procedures and documents care in the electronic health record, employing care protocols and proper coding. Provides essential support to the Medical Director in key clinical and administrative functions and assumes the role of acting clinical lead during their absence, overseeing clinical decision-making, staff coordination, and response to urgent operational issues. Identifies and evaluates strategic opportunities and provide consultative recommendations to the Medical Director and senior leadership. Supports Medical Director for medical quality improvement efforts, coordinating peer review and credentialing, facilitating studies, updating policies and procedures based on standards and/or best practice, and supporting accreditation activities. OPPORTUNITIES FOR LEADERSHIP: Working under the direction of and in close partnership with the Medical Director, the Assistant Medical Director will have opportunities to contribute clinical expertise, support departmental priorities, and help carry forward initiatives across the following areas: Support Provider Development and Clinical Education The Student Health Center is committed to maintaining a clinical team that is prepared to respond to the evolving health needs of the student population. The Assistant Medical Director will have the opportunity to support provider development through mentorship, clinical education, and shared learning. Working together with the Medical Director, the Assistant Medical Director will need to identify educational needs, assist with clinical in-services, and reinforce the consistent use of current evidence-based practices. Enhance Quality and Safety Providing safe, reliable, and high-quality care requires an ongoing commitment to evaluation, learning, and improvement. The Assistant Medical Director will contribute to quality and safety efforts through the review of clinical outcomes, patient feedback, and peer review findings. There is an opportunity to help identify areas for improvement and assist with implementing and sustaining agreed-upon changes in practice. Improve Access and Clinical Operations As the student population and demand for services continue to evolve, the Student Health Center must regularly assess how students access and move through care. The Assistant Medical Director has the opportunity to provide clinical insight into scheduling and patient flow, and the use of primary care, specialty, nursing, and ancillary services in order to support timely access, continuity of care, and effective student experience. Increase Interdisciplinary Collaboration The Student Health Center’s collaborative care model depends on strong communication and coordination across SHC units, university departments, and external partners. The Assistant Medical Director will help foster productive working relationships, support shared approaches to student care, and address barriers that affect coordination, referrals, and continuity of services.   ATTRIBUTES OF THE SUCCESSFUL CANDIDATE:   Strong leader who is able to identify and advance departmental goals while fostering meaningful staff engagement and buy-in. Proactively elevates and scales programs effectively leveraging available resources and navigating constraints. Shows determination and strategic vision needed to build out effective models of practice, with a commitment to advancing and scaling coaching to maximize impact. Engages as a leader beyond the department and the SHC, playing an active role in the Division of Student Affairs and broader campus-wide initiatives. Demonstrates strong relationship-building and partnerships skills, utilizing thoughtful and effective approaches to engage stakeholders, cultivate collaboration, and achieve shared outcomes with those whom you have no positional authority. Dedicated to being part of a SHC team invested in integrating all aspects of health to better serve students. ABOUT THE DIVISION OF STUDENT AFFAIRS PRIORITIES: Three priorities guide our work in the Division of Student Affairs. Foremost, we maintain a commitment to quality which is rooted in the belief that LSU students deserve our best effort. Every interaction we have with students should communicate care, relevance, polish, and attention to detail. We work to ensure every space, place, and staff-to-student interaction communicates a sense of home to students. Finally, we design programs, services, events, and experiences with everyone in mind .   RESPONSIBILITIES:   Direct Student Care: 60% Provides direct primary care for students, including assessment, testing, diagnosis, treatment and referral; performs minor surgical procedures; documents care in the electronic health record, employing care protocols and proper coding; provides consultation on complex or high-risk cases in the absence of the Medical Director. Leadership & Administration: 25% Provides essential support to the Medical Director in key clinical and administrative functions and assumes the role of acting clinical lead during their absence, overseeing clinical decision-making, staff coordination, and response to urgent operational issues. Provides training, guidance, and supervision of designated providers. Identify and evaluate strategic opportunities and provide consultative recommendations to the Medical Director and senior leadership. Assists with other administrative and workflow matters as needed to optimize quality, efficiency and access.   Quality Control & Compliance: 10% Supports Medical Director for medical quality improvement efforts, coordinating peer review and credentialing, facilitating studies, updating policies and procedures based on standards and/or best practice, and supporting accreditation activities. Works closely with FMOL's Quality Team, sharing data and recommendations that benefit both institutions. Other Duties: 5% Performs other duties as assigned by the Executive Director and Medical Director. This includes but is not limited to efforts that support broad division/institution efforts including engaging in in-service opportunities for the division, and other special projects.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:   Unencumbered Louisiana MD or DO License Current ABMS Board Certification in Primary Care or Emergency Medicine Current DEA and CDS Certificates Three years of clinical medical experience. Some experience in maintaining nationally recognized accreditation standards such as Joint Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations or Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care and some experience on process improvement and health care systems/ models. DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Five years of clinical medical experience. Experience in a college health setting; experience supervising and evaluating other clinicians.   ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS: Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to drug/alcohol testing in accordance with University Policy Statement 67.   This position may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18.   Ability and willingness to work some evening and weekend hours.   NOMINATIONS, APPLICATIONS, AND INQUIRIES:   Applications will be accepted online on the LSU Careers website. Please direct all nominations and inquiries for the position to Kelsi Taylor, Administrative Services Manager, at ktay126@lsu.edu . The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue to accept applications and nominations until the position is filled. Requested application materials include a letter of interest or cover letter; resume or curriculum vitae; and the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least five professional references, and a copy of license to practice. All applications, nominations, and inquiries will remain confidential. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Requested application materials include a letter of interest or cover letter; resume or curriculum vitae; the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references; and a copy of license to practice. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Kelsi Taylor at 225-578-2308.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): January 1, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU-Student-Union/Custodian-2_R00120149": {
      "title": "Custodian 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Custodian 2     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM AUX - EP - Ops - BldSvc - Union (Stacie Broadway (00003745))     Work Location: LSU Student Union     Pay Grade: Classified Technician and Skilled Trades     Job Description: This position is responsible for cleaning and maintaining the LSU Student Union facility.  This person must be capable of moving about in a 305,000 square foot building multiple times daily to clean and prepare ballrooms, meeting/conference rooms, lobbies, office space, and exterior sidewalks, patios, and balconies. The person must also be able to ascend and descend the stairs of a 4 story building multiple times daily and stand for extended periods during cleaning processes. They must also be capable to stoop, kneel, and crouch to pick up litter, retrieve equipment, and clean restrooms, offices, lobbies, and maintain floors.  This person should be capable of moving furniture that weighs 20 to 40 pounds or more and transport tables and chairs weighing 60-80 pounds to set-up for events throughout the building.  Will use arms/hands to operate floor/power equipment used in preparing and maintaining floors.  In accordance with University Policy Statement 18, this position is considered essential and may be required to report or stay on campus in the event of emergency or closure. Job Description Cleans lobbies, bathrooms, hallways, meeting rooms, billiards area, and administrative area of the union by sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, dusting, and polishing. Mixes or blends cleaning solutions to proper concentrations as necessary - 30% Responsible for set-ups and break downs associated with daily events in meeting rooms, lobbies, ballrooms, and exterior grounds - 25% Cleans, strips, waxes and polishes floors using industrial size mops and commercial type floor machines. Fills commercial floor machines with cleaning solutions of proper concentration, empties unused solution into appropriate container - 20% Cleans floor machines and checks and recharges batteries. Washes, rinses and dries industrial size wet mops, dust mops, and commercial floor pads. Operates wet dry vacuuming carpet extraction equipment and other commercial equipment as requires for cleaning and shampooing carpets - 10% Empties (exterior and interior ) trash and recycling containers, transports waste material to outdoor refuse containers or recycling containers as needed. Cleans, decontaminates, and deodorizes waste containers using proper materials according to label directions - 10% Performs other duties as may be assigned by Building Services supervisors, Managers, or other administrative personnel within the department - 5% Minimum Qualifications: No Test Score Required Six months of experience in custodial, housekeeping, groundskeeping, or food service work. apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=100270       Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number, and email address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Jasiah Arceneaux at 225-578-7481 and jarce24@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 13, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1112-Ruffin-G-Pleasant-Hall/Financial-Aid-Coordinator--Verification_R00120143": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Coordinator/ Verification",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Financial Aid Coordinator/ Verification     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - EM - Rec - FAS - FA - Operations (Morgan Trapen Tannehill (00001127))     Work Location: 1112 Ruffin G. Pleasant Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The Verification Coordinator position within Louisiana State University’s Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships will play a key collaborative role in advancing the university and meeting the student access objectives.  The individual, with general oversight from the Senior Coordinator of Operations, will be responsible assisting with interpreting and entering verification documents, communicating conflicts identified in the verification process, and performing calculations for Return of Title IV funds.    Interpret and enter verification action items to admitted and continuing students. Identify and resolve discrepancies in self-reported information against actual documentation for the pool selected for verification. Communicate conflicts identified in the verification process and information needed for resolution. Interpret subsequent transactions of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA) that may be received for a student to determine if conflicts exist. If conflicts exist, request the appropriate verification action item on the student’s account and communicate the conflict. Review the transfer monitoring report provided to us by the U.S. Department of Education for mid-year transfer students. This report is utilized to help determine the amount of aid that a mid-year transfer student may be eligible to receive. Perform calculations in accordance with the regulations for the returning of Title IV funds to the appropriate programs within the time frame allotted by the Department of Education. Responsible for monitoring posting of refunds for any Title IV funds returned to the Department of Education by a student officially or unofficially resigning and have received federal student aid.   Special projects as assigned (10%) Serves as a rotating member of the satisfactory academic progress appeals committee. Represent LSU and the Office of Enrollment Management & Student Success at professional functions and recruiting events.   Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree Meets eligibility to obtain National Student Loan Database System access and must not be in default on a student loan. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Our ideal candidate possesses the following qualities: Experience working in financial aid or equivalent student services setting in higher education. High level of fluency in Spanish, written and verbal, preferred. Knowledge of best practices in financial aid Strong team orientation, effective interpersonal skills, and superior written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated commitment to data-driven decision-making, including effective analytical skills and proven results in achieving objectives and goals. Special Qualifications:   As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The location of this position is LSU-BR and is not eligible for remote work. To be considered, qualified candidates will submit a complete application which includes a cover letter explaining their specific interest in the position and how their skills and experiences prepare them for success in this role, a resume, and three professional references. Please provide resume and transcripts, if applicable. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Morgan Tannehill at mtrape1@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Communication, Confidentiality, Critical Thinking, Customer-Focused, Decision Making, Policy Knowledge, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): January 1, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0110A-WC-Stubbs-Hall/Assistant-Professor---Environment-and-Community-Studies_R00120137": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Environment and Community Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor - Environment and Community Studies     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM HSS - School of Sociology (Edward S Shihadeh (00008174))     Work Location: 0110A W.C. Stubbs Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Start Date: August 2027   Job Position/Rank: Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track). Department of Sociology Louisiana State University Academic Positions: Assistant Professor Salary Range: Negotiable Job Description: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (Position/Tenure-Track) Department of Sociology. College of Humanities and Social Sciences  Louisiana State University Specialization Area: Environment and Community The Department of Sociology at Louisiana State University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2027. We seek applicants with a specialization in Environment and Community who want to join a vibrant academic community at a R1 university. Required Qualifications: Applicants should show promise of developing a strong record of publications. Potential for research funding is critical. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in sociology or anticipate completion of the degree by August of 2027. Screening of applicants will begin Sept 30, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents, including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; sick leave; paid holidays; wellness benefits; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more. The LSU Department of Sociology is one of the oldest in the South and has awarded doctoral degrees for over 80 years. LSU is Louisiana's flagship research university and is the only public Carnegie designated Research Extensive University in the state. For more information about the department, please see www.lsu.edu/sociology. LSU is an equal opportunity employer.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applications should include a letter of application and curriculum vitae. In addition, please have three letters of recommendation sent to: Kegan Reid, Job Search, 126 Stubbs Hall, Louisiana State University, Baton Rouge, LA 70803 or via email to Kegan Reid at kreid@lsu.edu. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, contact Edward Shihadeh, Department Chair, at edsoc@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): March 2, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
