    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0100-Athletic-Physical-Plant-Office/Custodian-2-OR-Custodian-3_R00120105": {
      "title": "Custodian 2 OR Custodian 3",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Custodian 2 OR Custodian 3     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM Athletics - FG - Ops - Grounds - Custodial - PMAC Night Shift (Reshawn Bell (00335435))     Work Location: 0100 Athletic Physical Plant Office     Pay Grade: Classified Technician and Skilled Trades     Job Description: The Core Values of LSU Athletics define who we are and what we do. They are: Excellence, Integrity, Authenticity, Perseverance, Respect, Fairness, Growth, and Service. They are the support system that sustains our success. These values work together, constantly collaborating and combining to secure our future and drive our unending work to create transformational change – for our student-athletes, for our athletics community, and for the millions across the world who know and love these three letters.  Forever LSU. This position is a state Civil Service position that is responsible for all housekeeping duties for Athletic facilities and buildings. 95% Incumbent will be responsible for all housekeeping duties in Athletic Facilities.  Housekeeping duties include vacuuming and cleaning spots on carpets, dusting and polishing furniture, cleaning windows and window sills, mopping and waxing floors.  Clean and sanitize restrooms and locker rooms.  Clean the water fountains and elevator doors, being careful to use appropriate cleaner (a stainless steel polish).  Dust and polish all furniture in the area.  Remove any litter in and around the buildings on a daily basis. For Custodian 3's train/mentor entry-level custodians.  Help triage questions and provide additional support to the Custodian Supervisor A. 5%       Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Custodian 2: Six months of experience in custodial, housekeeping, grounds keeping, or food service work.   http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=100270 Custodian 3: One year of experience in custodial, housekeeping, groundskeeping, or food service work. http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=175910 Special/Physical Qualifications Capable of moving about in a 58,000 sq. ft. bldg. multiple times daily to clean and prepare locker rooms, office space, training rooms, spectator seating and exterior sidewalks, playing surfaces and common area. Able to stand for extended periods during cleaning processes. Must also be capable to stoop, kneel, and crouch to pick up litter, retrieve equipment, and clean restrooms, offices, lobbies, and maintain floors. Should be capable of moving furniture that weighs 20 to 40 lbs.  Will use arms/hands to operate floor/power equipment used in preparing and maintaining floors.  Will work with and be exposed to common cleaning products.  Ability to work extended days, weekends and holidays. In accordance with University PS 18, this position is considered essential and may be required to report or stay on campus in the event of an emergency or closure. Pre-employment physical required.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary range, please contact Jaden Rogers at jadenr@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 9, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0359-JW-Nicholson-Hall/Assistant-Research-Scientist--High-Energy-Astrophysics-and-Space-Weather-Projects-_R00120104": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Scientist (High-Energy Astrophysics and Space Weather Projects)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Research Scientist (High-Energy Astrophysics and Space Weather Projects)     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAM Science - PA - Multimessenger (Michela Negro (00082539)) (SO005767)     Work Location: 0359 J.W. Nicholson Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Job responsibilities: 50% - Research on high-energy astrophysics and space weather: Conduct independent and collaborative research on CALET data from the International Space Station, continuing and extending the analysis of geomagnetic storm effects on Earth's radiation belts, including a systematic search of the full-mission (10-year) CALET dataset. The position will manage the group's simulation efforts, including running, validating, and documenting simulation campaigns and maintaining the associated analysis pipelines and software for use by other group members. Responsibilities also include preparing results for publication in peer-reviewed journals, presenting at collaboration meetings and scientific conferences, mentoring and training graduate and undergraduate students joining the group, participating in group and CALET collaboration meetings, and delivering periodic updates on research progress, simulation status, and student projects. 40% - Scientific Balloon Program: Support the Balloon Program Manager for the statewide student ballooning program (LaACES) and the HASP PI for the national ballooning program, which includes supporting the implementation of ballooning curriculum, producing training materials, delivering lectures, guiding hands-on activities, and serving as an advisor to participating student teams developing experiments related to space weather, heliophysics, and/or other astrophysics areas of research. The position will also provide technical support for flight hardware maintenance and refurbishment, testing and development of flight software, development of operations documentation, and overall support for payload integration and flight launch operations. 10% - Outreach: Support the Outreach Program Manager at community organizations and K-12 school events. Deliver space weather, heliophysics, or other astrophysics lectures and content at community and school-based events. Deliver scientific demonstrations at outreach events. Provide logistics support for events. And other duties as assigned. Minimum requirements: Bachelor's degree in physics or related field with seven years of related experience. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply – a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred qualifications: PhD in physics or related field with three years of related experience. Additional Information: This position requires a valid driver's license, will require an MVR, and will be subject to drug screenings per PS-67. This position and/or position's responsibilities require work directly with minors. Finger printing and National Sex Offender Registry check required per FASOP HR-04.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach ALL documents under the Resume/CV section of your application. Provide a cover letter and CV. Provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire (if applicable). For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Michela Negro at 225-578-1488 or michelanegro@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 9, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/S-Knapp-Hall/Extension-Associate--4-H-Shooting-Sports-and-Livestock-_R00120101": {
      "title": "Extension Associate (4-H Shooting Sports and Livestock)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Extension Associate (4-H Shooting Sports and Livestock)     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG PL4 - 4H Youth Development Programs (Kimberly Jones Williams (00010820))     Work Location: S. Knapp Hall     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: Work Location: LSU Main Campus, Baton Rouge, Louisiana (Statewide Responsibilities)   Position Description: The LSU AgCenter seeks a highly motivated and dynamic individual to serve as the 4-H Shooting Sports and Livestock Extension Associate within the Louisiana 4-H Youth Development Program. This position provides statewide leadership, coordination, and support for youth educational programs focused on livestock, shooting sports, ATV safety, and related workforce development opportunities. The candidate will work closely with the State Shooting Sports Coordinator, State 4-H Animal Science Specialist, parish extension agents (ANR and 4-H), certified volunteers, industry leaders, commodity organizations, and university faculty to strengthen and expand program opportunities for Louisiana youth. This position plays a critical role in ensuring high-quality educational experiences that promote positive youth development, leadership, responsibility, life skills, sportsmanship, animal welfare, and safe participation practices. About Louisiana 4-H: Louisiana 4-H reaches thousands of youth annually through programs focused on leadership, citizenship, healthy living, STEM, agriculture, animal science, natural resources, and workforce development. Through hands-on learning experiences and dedicated volunteers, Louisiana 4-H prepares young people to become responsible, productive, and engaged citizens that are Beyond Ready for life. Qualification Requirements : Bachelor’s degree in animal science, agricultural education, wildlife management, natural resources, youth development, agricultural leadership, extension education, or a closely related field. Bachelor's degree in Animal Science, Agricultural Education, Wildlife Management, Natural Resources, Youth Development, Agricultural Leadership, Extension Education, or a closely related field.      Experience working with youth in educational, agricultural, outdoor, or volunteer-based programs. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with youth, volunteers, extension personnel, and external stakeholders. Ability to travel extensively throughout Louisiana and occasionally out of state. Ability to work evenings and weekends as required by program needs. LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications.  If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (per La. RS 42:36). Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with: • Experience in 4-H, FFA, shooting sports, livestock, outdoor education, or youth development programs. • Shooting Sports instructor certification or willingness to obtain certification. • Knowledge of livestock production systems and animal science principles. • Experience coordinating educational events, contests, trainings, or volunteer programs. • Experience with program evaluation, event management, and educational curriculum development. • Demonstrated leadership ability and experience working with diverse audiences. • Strong technology and communication skills, including experience with Microsoft Office, online registration platform (4-HOnline), and social media outreach. Salary and Benefits : Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available : Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline : September 30, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Qualified candidates must apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching file(s) containing a curriculum vita, a letter of application, official university transcripts, and three letters of professional references. Questions about the online application system should be directed to the HRM Office at 225/578-0324. (Paper, faxed, or emailed application materials will not be accepted.) In lieu of attaching the letters of reference, they may be sent directly to: Dr. Todd A. Tarifa Department Head, Louisiana 4-H Youth Development Program Associate Director for Youth Development (4-H/FFA) LSU AgCenter 102 Efferson Hall Baton Rouge, LA 70803 Phone: 225-578-2196 Email: tatarifa@agcenter.lsu.edu Website:  www.lsuagcenter.com The Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and applications will be accepted without regard to race, religion, color, sex, national origin, age, or disability. Information on Equal Employment can be obtained from the EEO and Civil Rights Coordinator, 103 J. Norman Efferson Hall, LSU AgCenter, Baton Rouge, LA 70803. Phone 225.578.2258. It is the policy of the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service to employ only United States citizens or aliens lawfully authorized to work in the United States. The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Extension Associate (4-H Shooting Sports and Livestock)     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0135-Human-Ecology-Building/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Textiles--Apparel-Design---Merchandising_R00111215": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Textiles, Apparel Design & Merchandising",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Textiles, Apparel Design & Merchandising     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COA - Department of Textiles Apparel Design and Merchandising (Bruce Cameron (00054395))     Work Location: 0135 Human Ecology Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The LSU College of Agriculture is seeking to fill a tenure-track assistant/associate professor position in the Department of Textiles, Apparel Design, and Merchandising (TAM). The individual will hold 100% appointment with LSU State University A&M (College of Agriculture.) 65% Teaching : Teach undergraduate and graduate courses that may include but are not limited to draping, collection development, Optitex Pattern Software, Adobe Creative Suites, Clo-3D, Digital Textile Design and Computerized Knitting systems.  30% Research : Develop research in areas of Textiles, Apparel Design & Merchandising with an emphasis in apparel design technology in the apparel industry. Develop an independent and collaborative research program related to their field, acquire external funding for scholarship with the expectation that they will disseminate their research findings as well as participate in juried exhibitions. 5% Service : Contribute to advising and recruitment of both undergraduate and graduate students. Professional involvement in community; membership in appropriate professional and/or academic organizations; ability to develop industry partnerships. FERPA -As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Additional Information: This position is considered a research or research-related support position and must undergo screenings per RS 17:1826. Minimum Qualifications: Earned PhD in Textile, Apparel Design & Merchandising or related area. Established college-level teaching record as graduate student, instructor or above; demonstrated record of scholarship, participation in juried exhibitions, and ability to obtain external funding; evidence of teaching excellence, graduate and undergraduate level advising, and service consistent with appointment.  Preferred Qualifications: Earned PhD in Textile, Apparel Design & Merchandising or related area. For consideration at the Associate Professor rank, 3 years of service preferred. Demonstrated ability to teach a variety of courses within the Textile, Apparel Design and Merchandising curriculum (e.g., draping, fashion illustration, collection development, research methods); proficiency with  current industry software and technologies (such as Adobe Creative Suite, Optitex, Computerized knitting systems [Shima Seiki] and Clo-3D); industry experience; professional involvement in community; membership in appropriate professional and/or academic organizations; ability to develop industry partnerships. SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, a Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year along with a week off between Christmas Day and New Years Day), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. APPLICATION DEADLINE: Until a suitable candidate is identified. APPLICATION PROCEDURE: Must apply online at https://lsusystemcareers.lsu.edu/ by attaching a cover letter with statement of professional interest and goals, resume, university transcripts, and the names and contact information for three professional references. For more information contact the hiring manager below: Dr. Casey Stannard (stannard@lsu.edu) Chair of Search Committee     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please upload cover letter, CV, references, and official transcript(s) under the Resume/CV header in Workday (multiple documents may be uploaded under this header). Official transcript(s) are not required at time of application but are required at time of hire. A portfolio needs to be included as part of the application. Questions about the position (not application materials) should be emailed to: Dr. Casey Stannard (stannard@lsu.edu) Chair of Search Committee.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 27, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-University-Public-Safety-Building/Police-Officer-1--2--or-3_R00120047": {
      "title": "Police Officer 1, 2, or 3",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Police Officer 1, 2, or 3     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM FA - CSPER - Police - Spprt - Title IX/CARE (Sarah McBride Drake (00010129))     Work Location: 0101 University Public Safety Building     Pay Grade:     Job Description: This position is a commissioned law enforcement position in which the incumbent serves as a uniformed or plainclothes member of the LSU Police Department assigned to various departmental units and/or details. This position description describes the typical duties/work setting of the job. The actual duties and percentage effort/duty for a position listed on the position description may vary slightly, and the incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as assigned. Job distinctions: Police Officer 1 - Entry Level; Police Officer 2 - Experienced; Police Officer 3 - Advanced. The physical area covered by the department includes the campus with over 500 principal buildings located on more than 1200 acres, and additional facilities (Innovation Park, FETA, Rural Life Museum, Hilltop Arboretum, and AgResearch, totaling nearly 4000 additional acres) located off campus in Baton Rouge. Work shifts are designed to best supplement the department in its mission to provide safety to the campus population. Job Responsibilities Provides proactive patrols to protect lives/property and responds to calls for service from the community. Detects suspicious activities and watches for criminal acts, incidents, accidents, and suspicious persons. Prepares incident reports for supervisor review and approval. Testifies in court to present evidence or act as a witness in criminal cases. May be asked to perform administrative duties, such as but not limited to attending meetings, attending events/protests, conducting witness interviews, performing duties associated with the courts, performing daily operations-style duties, and conducting general investigative activities. (35%) Enforces state motor vehicle traffic laws. Investigates traffic crashes to determine causes, including gathering evidence and data from the crash scene. Prepares traffic crash reports and supplements as required. Sets up barricades and other traffic controls to assist various Facilities projects and arranges for the towing of vehicles out of restricted areas. (30%) Reports directly to the Police Sergeant or supervisor of higher rank. Attends shift briefings related to patrol activities and attends law enforcement training as required. Drives police vehicles in the execution of duties. Obeys the general orders of the department and university policy and procedures. (10%) Works assignments involving large crowds and special events control operations. Operates and maintains security access systems throughout LSU administrative and academic buildings. (10%) Works assignments involving fire safety, environmental safety, hazardous materials, building security, and selective enforcement programs. Works emergency response assignments as they relate to medical incidents, hurricanes, floods, bomb threats, and/or any other catastrophic situations as required. (5%) Communications Center - answers both routine and emergency telephone calls. (5%) Other duties as assigned. (5%) Additional Requirements This position requires a valid driver's license, will require an MVR, and is subject to drug screens per PM-33/PS-67/FASOP HR-04. This position is classified as a safety and security-sensitive position. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. This position is considered emergency essential and may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. Additional Information Ability to work in all weather conditions. Overtime and weekend work. Ability to lift 50 pounds. Must be able to operate a computer, telephone, and other office equipment. Physically strenuous activity relative to the nature of law enforcement is required. This position will require a physical evaluation based on the required physical demands. Applicants must have Civil Service test scores for 2100 — Protective Services Exam (PSE) in order to be considered for this vacancy unless exempted by Civil Service rule or policy. If you do not have a score prior to applying to this posting, it may result in your application not being considered. Applicants  without  a current test score can apply to take the test  here . Testing locations and schedules for State Civil Service test centers can be found here . Minimum Qualifications An applicant who meets the Minimum Qualifications and has a Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) certification from a Louisiana-accredited training academy may be appointed by probational appointment or job appointment to a job that requires the Protective Services Exam without a test score. The applicant’s POST certification shall not be under suspension or pending a revocation hearing. Police Officer 1 MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: No experience or training is required. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Possession of a current Louisiana driver's license. Willingness and ability to attain a Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) certification. An applicant who has been convicted of a felony or who is under indictment on a felony charge will be disqualified until relief from the disabilities imposed by state and federal laws is granted. Police Officer 2 MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: One year of law enforcement experience. EXPERIENCE SUBSTITUTION: Every 30 semester hours earned from an accredited college or university will substitute for one year of the required experience. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Possession of a current Louisiana driver's license. Possession of an active Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) certification may be required. An applicant who has been convicted of a felony or who is under indictment on a felony charge will be disqualified until relief from the disabilities imposed by state and federal laws is granted. Police Officer 3 MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Two years of law enforcement experience. EXPERIENCE SUBSTITUTION: Every 30 semester hours earned from an accredited college or university will substitute for one year of the required experience. The maximum substitution allowed is 60 semester hours which substitutes for two years of experience. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Possession of a current Louisiana driver's license. Possession of an active Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) certification may be required. An applicant who has been convicted of a felony or who is under indictment on a felony charge will be disqualified until relief from the disabilities imposed by state and federal laws is granted. Minimum Certifications/Licenses Valid driver's license Louisiana State Civil Service Job Specifications Police Officer 1: http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=169660 Police Officer 2: http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=169680 Police Officer 3: http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=169700     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Sgt. Sarah Drake at sdrake1@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: September 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 10, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
