    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0330-Thomas-D-Boyd-Hall/HRIS-Analyst-Time---Absence_R00119845": {
      "title": "HRIS Analyst-Time & Absence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: HRIS Analyst-Time & Absence     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM FA - HRM - OO - HRIS - Time & Absence (Karen Mixon Magee (00010273))     Work Location: 0330 Thomas D. Boyd Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Job Summary: The Time & Absence section of the Office of Human Resource Management is responsible for administering the University leave policy and Workday time tracking and absence modules. Provides expert guidance and direction to university and campus administration on time and absence best practice and Workday module capabilities. Collaborates with management to ensure that strategy, functionality and programs support LSU’s business objectives, meeting all legal and policy requirements. Job Responsibilities: 35%- Assisting with managing Time Tracking and Absence Workday functionality and administers the campus leave policy. Provides expert guidance and direction to university and campus administration on time and absence best practice and Workday module capabilities. Responsible for assigned Workday module including, but not limited to: fixes, testing, data integrity, updates, participate in user groups, stay abreast of functionality, work with ITS to develop and maintain reports. Develop and maintain system documentation and processes including third party time tracking solutions. Act as security module administrator. Works closely with compensation consultants to define, establish, maintain, modify and streamline special time types and compensation policy (i.e. premium pay, on call pay, shift differentials, etc.) 35%- Responsible for all leave/time off functions in Workday, including but not limited to: entering and reviewing all continuous leave transactions, ensuring all leave events in Workday reflect all related approved leave documents; supporting the manager in responding to emergency-related leave processes, closures, and actions according to state and federal policies; processing terminations in Workday, ensuring the accuracy of terminal leave transactions for former workers; reviewing accuracy of adjustments to service dates and overriding balances for transfers and new employees with prior state service; administering leave related functions such as workers compensation adjustments, leave without pay accruals, etc. Understand and interpret LSU leave policies in order to advise and guide departments to ensure compliance. Responsible for supporting audit functions, including but not limited to: monitoring the use of special leaves, emergency related time entry, premium pay/shift differential quarterly audits, and annual leave certification audit. 20%-Identifies advanced reporting needs and requirements to satisfy auditor and policy compliance. Works with the manager and assigned business analyst(s) to create, modify, and establish a robust reporting portfolio to support users in tracking and maintaining data for adherence to policy and procedure. Provides advisement and guidance to internal and external customers on university leave policies and Workday leave module functionality and reports. Monitors and maintains leave related policy statements and policy memorandums for updates as required by changes to state or federal mandates. 5%- Training and other duties as assigned – Identifies campus community training needs and works with the manager to develop and deliver various trainings on Time Tracking and Absence functionality. Create, review and revise necessary job aides as needed. 5%- Back-up HR Assistant on HR phone and email, and front desk coverage. Other duties as assigned by the manager. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with 1-year of related experience in HR processes, systems or related field. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply – a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in data analysis, audit, and information systems or similar fields.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application, please contact Karen Magee at kmagee@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Aquatic-Germplasm--Genetic-Resources-Ctr/Research-Associate-Specialist_R00120079": {
      "title": "Research Associate Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate Specialist     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG Chancellor - LAES - Aquatic Germplasm & Genetic Resources Center (Terrence R Tiersch (00011984))     Work Location: Aquatic Germplasm & Genetic Resources Ctr     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: (This is a grant-funded, non-tenure track position through 10/1/2027.  Funding must be available for any continuation of appointment) Work Location: Aquatic Germplasm and Genetic Resources Center, Baton Rouge, Louisiana (www.aggrc.com) Position Description: This position’s primary purpose is to support the successful execution of research programs through grant compliance monitoring, grant spend plan development, budget tracking, animal husbandry, and technical research support. This position will assist investigators and program staff in maintaing compliance with sponsor requirements, tracking project expenditures, monitoring grant balances, and ensuring research activities align with approved budgets and project objectives. Work after hours including weekends may be required periodically. Familiarity with aquatic species and reproductive biology is strongly preferred. Experience with CAD, 3-D printing, and open hardware is preferred including a strong desire for intersectoral collaboration. Qualification Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Bioengineering or a related field. Applicants with a degree in another agricultural or basic science field will be considered qualified provided they possess significant work experience in an area. Experience in the public sector and/or a university setting is desirable. Must have excellent interpersonal, administrative, and organizational skills, along with strong computer skills. Understanding of accounting principles  Knowledge of sponsored research administration, grant compliance requirements, and project management principles  Proficiency in Workday, Microsoft Office applications  Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with federally funded grants (USDA, NSF, NOAA, USFWS, or similar sponsors).  Comfortability working in a collaborative and evolving environment  Experience with budget forecasting, cost analysis, and financial planning.  Familiarity with research compliance requirements, including animal care and use protocols.  Experience developing dashboards, reports, or automated tracking systems using Excel or similar tools.  Experience supporting multi-investigator or multi-institutional research projects LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications.  If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (La RS 42:36). Salary and Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with education and experience.  The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline: September 16, 2026 or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Chris Toepfer Unit: AGGRC LSU AgCenter Mailing Address: 2288 Gourrier Ave. BR, La 70820 Phone : 2255786257 E-mail: ctoepfor@agcenter.lsu.edu   Website: www.lsuagcenter.com The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions:     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-Assumption-Parish-Extension-Office/Assistant-Associate-Extension-Agent--Nutrition-and-Community-Health-_R00120077-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition and Community Health)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition and Community Health)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAG PL3 - Southwest - Assumption (Margo Lynn Castro (00003296))     Work Location: 0101 Assumption Parish Extension Office     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Work Location:   The area to be served includes Assumption, St. Mary and St. Martin parishes.  While this position will have responsibilities in the Southwest region, the proposed domicile for this position is Assumption Parish Extension Office.  The NCH agent will also have Point of Contact responsibilities in Lower St. Martin Parish and St. Mary parishes. Position Description: This is a non-tenure track, agent level position (100% Extension NCH appointment). The Nutrition & Community Health (NCH) Extension Agent will work under the supervision and direction of the Parish Chair, NCH Regional Coordinator, Regional Director, and NCH state office faculty.  This position includes a seventy percent (70%) Flavors of Health (FOH) appointment and a thirty percent (30%) Centers for Disease Control High Obesity Program (CDC-HOP) appointment.   For the seventy percent (70%) Flavors of Health (FOH) appointment, the Agent will develop and maintain a plan of work for general nutrition education programming based on current FOH expectations and for serving as a primary point of contact for nutrition programming in Assumption parish.  This will include recruiting clientele for nutrition programs; implementing core curricula; preparing nutrition education materials, communications, and activities that respond to local needs or requests; and facilitating a community advisory committee to provide programmatic direction to strengthen outreach efforts. Flavors of Health programming include delivering programs on chronic disease prevention and management through healthy lifestyle changes.  Additionally, the incumbent will be expected to disseminate research-based information, identify educational opportunities, and participate in other educational meetings aimed at serving stakeholders in Assumption parish. The Agent is expected to use a variety of delivery methods to deliver information and provide educational opportunities, which could include newsletters, social media posts, workshops and other educational events, and contributing to parish websites.  Additionally, thirty percent (30%) of the Agent’s time will be dedicated to facilitating the Healthy Communities program and will work under the supervision and direction of the Parish Chairs, Regional Director, NCH Regional Coordinator, and NCH state office faculty.  The Agent will implement NCH Healthy Communities projects in Assumption Parish designed to promote a broad initiative to increase healthy food access and physical activity in the parish by addressing the food system and built environment. The agent will organize community-based advisory committees involving stakeholders, local government, volunteers, other health professionals and community residents to identify the most critical needs in the communities served, strategies to address those needs, ways to overcome barriers to good nutrition and health in communities and build community advocacy. Following those needs identified by the advisory committees, the Agent will work with advisory committees and community groups to promote healthy behaviors in the parish. The Agent will provide primary leadership in planning, implementing, evaluating and reporting food and physical activity policy, environmental and systems interventions as well as implementing health and nutrition education programming for adult and youth in the parish leading up to and as a result of these efforts.  Additionally, the incumbent will be the catalyst to educate existing and potential community and programming partners about the importance of nutrition education and complementary policy, systems and environmental strategies for audiences that address nutrition, physical activity, food safety and food security needs.  The agent will work under the administrative supervision and direction of the parish chair, NCH Regional Coordinator, NCH State office staff, and regional director.  To attend and conduct training to meet the needs of the clientele, this position requires some overnight travel and work on evenings and weekends. Qualification Requirements: A baccalaureate degree in dietetics, community and family nutrition, human ecology, public health, wellness and health , family and consumer sciences, food science, kinesiology, hospitality management , or closely related areas. Must have an undergraduate degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 2.5 (all GPA requirements based on a 4.0 system) and a 3.0 for graduate work attempted, if any, or master’s degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 3.0 or a current grade-point average of at least 3.0 on at least 12 hours of graduate credit. The applicant must demonstrate effective oral and written communication skills. A master’s degree in the field listed above is desired. Experience in recruiting, training and supervising volunteers and experience in teaching and applying principles of leadership development to both youth and adults is also desired.  Knowledge of public relations and the ability to cope with change are highly desirable characteristics.  Ability to work with and through others is essential as is the ability to function with minimum supervision.  Salary and Benefits:   Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Conditions of Employment: A personal automobile and appropriate insurance coverage is required (travel allowance provided).  Satisfactory completion of one specific graduate level extension course (3 credit hours) is required in year two or three of employment, prior to promotion eligibility to associate agent.  Additionally, a faculty member who does not have a related master’s degree must complete an additional 12 hours of related graduate level coursework in order to be promoted to associate agent and such promotion must occur in the first seven years of employment.  An exception is that additional agent experience may be substituted for 12 hours of coursework, but not for the required course.  Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline:   October 2, 2026 or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Qualified candidates must apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU   (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching file(s) containing a curriculum vita, a letter of application, official university transcripts, and two letters of reference. Questions about the online application system should be directed to the HRM Office at 225/578-0324. (Paper, faxed, or emailed application materials will not be accepted.)  In lieu of attaching the letters of reference, they may be sent directly to: Mandy Armentor NCH Regional Coordinator, Southwest Region Office 1373 Caffey Road Rayne, LA, 70578 Email: marmentor@agcenter.lsu.edu   Phone: 337-788-7547; Fax 337-788-7553 Website:  www.lsuagcenter.com The Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and applications will be accepted without regard to race, religion, color, sex, national origin, age, or disability. Information on Equal Employment can be obtained from the EEO and Civil Rights Coordinator, 103 J. Norman Efferson Hall, LSU AgCenter, Baton Rouge, LA 70803. Phone 225.578.2258.  It is the policy of the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service to employ only United States citizens or aliens lawfully authorized to work in the United States. The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition and Community Health)     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-West-Baton-Rouge-Parish-Extension-Office/Assistant-Associate-Extension-Agent--Nutrition---Community-Health-_R00120068": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition & Community Health)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition & Community Health)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAG PL3 - Southwest Region - Jefferson Davis (James Todd Fontenot (00002417))     Work Location: 0101 West Baton Rouge Parish Extension Office     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Work Location: The area to be served includes West Baton Rouge (WBR) and Iberville parishes. While this position will have responsibilities in the Southwest region, the proposed domicile for this position is either WBR or Iberville Parish Extension Office. The NCH agent will also have Point of Contact responsibilities in the non-domicile parish (either WBR or Iberville) and Upper St. Martin parishes. Position Description: This is a non-tenure track, agent level position (100% Extension NCH). The Nutrition & Community Health (NCH) Extension Agent will work under the supervision and direction of the Parish Chair, NCH Regional Coordinator, Regional Director, and NCH state office faculty. This position includes a one hundred percent (100%) Flavors of Health (FOH) appointment. The Agent will develop and maintain a plan of work for general nutrition education programming based on current FOH expectations and for serving as a primary point of contact for nutrition programming in West Baton Rouge and Iberville parishes. This will include recruiting clientele for nutrition programs; implementing core curricula; preparing nutrition education materials, communications, and activities that respond to local needs or requests; and facilitating a community advisory committee to provide programmatic direction to strengthen outreach efforts. Flavors of Health programming include delivering programs on chronic disease prevention and management through healthy lifestyle changes. Additionally, the incumbent will be expected to disseminate research-based information, identify educational opportunities, and participate in other educational meetings aimed at serving stakeholders in WBR and Iberville parishes. The Agent is expected to use a variety of delivery methods to deliver information and provide educational opportunities, which could include newsletters, social media posts, workshops and other educational events, and contributing to parish websites. The agent will organize community-based advisory committees involving stakeholders, local government, volunteers, other health professionals and community residents to identify the most critical needs in the communities served, strategies to address those needs, ways to overcome barriers to good nutrition and health in communities and build community advocacy. Following those needs identified by the advisory committees, the Agent will work with advisory committees and community groups to promote healthy behaviors in the parish(es). The Agent provides primary leadership in planning, implementing, evaluating and reporting food and physical activity policy, environmental and systems interventions as well as implementing health and nutrition education programming for adult and youth in the parish leading up to and because of these efforts. Additionally, the incumbent will be the catalyst to educate existing and potential community and programming partners about the importance of nutrition education and complementary policy, systems and environmental strategies for audiences that address nutrition, physical activity, food safety and food security needs. The agent will work under the administrative supervision and direction of the parish chair, NCH Regional Coordinator, NCH State office staff, and regional director. To attend and conduct training to meet the needs of the clientele, this position requires some overnight travel and work on evenings and weekends. Qualification Requirements: A baccalaureate degree in dietetics, community and family nutrition, human ecology, public health, wellness and health , family and consumer sciences, food science, kinesiology, hospitality management , or closely related areas. Must have an undergraduate degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 2.5 (all GPA requirements based on a 4.0 system) and a 3.0 for graduate work attempted, if any, or master’s degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 3.0 or a current grade-point average of at least 3.0 on at least 12 hours of graduate credit. The applicant must demonstrate effective oral and written communication skills. A master’s degree in the field listed above is desired. Experience in recruiting, training and supervising volunteers and experience in teaching and applying principles of leadership development to both youth and adults is also desired. Knowledge of public relations and the ability to cope with change are highly desirable characteristics. Ability to work with and through others is essential as is the ability to function with minimum supervision. Salary and Benefits:   Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Conditions of Employment: A personal automobile and appropriate insurance coverage is required (travel allowance provided). Satisfactory completion of one specific graduate level extension course (3 credit hours) is required in year two or three of employment, prior to promotion eligibility to associate agent. Additionally, a faculty member who does not have a related master’s degree must complete an additional 12 hours of related graduate level coursework in order to be promoted to associate agent and such promotion must occur in the first seven years of employment. An exception is that additional agent experience may be substituted for 12 hours of coursework, but not for the required course. Date Available :  Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline : October 2, 2026 or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure:   Qualified candidates must apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching file(s) containing a letter of application, resume, university transcripts, and two letters of reference. Questions about the online application system should be directed to the HRM Office at 225/578-0324. (Paper, faxed, or emailed application materials will not be accepted.)  In lieu of attaching the letters of reference, they may be sent directly to:                                 Mandy Armentor, NCH Regional Coordinator Southwest Region Office 1373 Caffey Road Rayne, LA 70578 Email:   marmentor@agcenter.lsu.edu   Phone: 337-788-7547; Fax 337-788-7553 Website:  www.lsuagcenter.com The Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and applications will be accepted without regard to race, religion, color, sex, national origin, age or disability.  Information on Equal Employment can be obtained from the EEO and Civil Rights Coordinator, 103 J. Norman Efferson Hall, 110 LSU Union Square, LSU AgCenter, Baton Rouge, LA 70803.  Phone 225.578.2258.  It is the policy of the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service to employ only United States citizens or aliens lawfully authorized to work in the United States. The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (Nutrition & Community Health)     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
