    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L0100-Hebert-Law-Center/Law-Library-Director_R00118487": {
      "title": "Law Library Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Law Library Director     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Law - Law Library and Information Services (Caprice L. Roberts (00076655) (Inherited))     Work Location: L0100 Hebert Law Center     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The LSU Paul M. Hebert Law Center seeks an innovative and experienced leader to serve as its next Director of the Law Library. The Director will advance the mission of the Law Center by ensuring that the library dynamically supports the instructional, scholarly, and research needs of the faculty and students. Reporting directly to the Dean, the Director holds responsibility for all facets of library management and operations, including budgeting, financial oversight, purchasing, hiring, supervision, personnel management, provision of library services and research instruction, collection development and maintenance, and physical plant operations. This role demands a team-oriented leader who can champion strategic planning and implementation while fostering a cooperative environment. The Director ensures that the collection and resources adequately support teaching, learning, research, and service while maintaining institutional compliance with ABA and AALS accreditation standards. The Law Library collection consists of over 1.1 million volume and volume equivalents (including over 400,000 in print), featuring a premier collection in foreign and comparative law. Supported by an annual budget of approximately $1.8 million, the library is currently undergoing an extensive multi-million dollar renovation project and employs a dedicated team of 6 librarians and 1 professional staff member. The Law Library coordinates and instructs Law Center’s legal research curriculum, delivered via traditional and hybrid methods. The Director is a member of the full-time faculty and expected to teach courses in the legal research and writing curriculum, with the possibility of teaching additional doctrinal courses. Applicants must possess a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school and a master’s degree in library and information science from an ALA-accredited institution and demonstrate superior academic credentials, a commitment to outstanding teaching, and strong administrative, communication, and interpersonal leadership skills. We welcome applications from candidates seeking either a tenure-track or professional practice-track position; tenure-track candidates must demonstrate a record of or strong potential for sustained scholarly achievement.    Beyond the Law Center, the library serves the broader university, the bar, and the public as a Federal and State depository. While independent, the Law Library routinely collaborates and partners with the main LSU campus library on joint initiatives. The Director will also champion cooperative resource sharing and technology procurement through the statewide LOUIS consortium, reinforcing a highly team-oriented approach to library services. Job Responsibilities: Library Administration (50%) Serves as the chief administrator of the Law Library, providing comprehensive oversight of all aspects of library management and operations. Core responsibilities include budgeting, financial management, procurement, personnel administration—including recruitment and supervision—collection development and maintenance, delivery of reference and research services, legal research instruction, management of physical facilities, and active participation in strategic planning and implementation. The administrator ensures that the Law Library's collections and resources effectively support the instructional, research, and service missions of the Law Center community. This role also encompasses ensuring ongoing compliance with accreditation standards and membership requirements set by the ABA and AALS within designated areas of responsibility. Personnel Management (20%) Provides supervision for all faculty and staff within the Law Library, overseeing daily activities and library operations. Collaborates with law faculty, staff, and the Dean to foster a collaborative and inclusive workplace aligned with the mission of the LSU Law Center. Research Instruction, Coordination, and Scholarship (15%) Oversees a range of advanced and specialized legal research courses, providing instruction within the legal research program alongside other dual-degreed library faculty. Maintains ongoing professional and scholarly engagement through the development of library and information science scholarship and active participation in conferences and other academic or peer settings. Strategic Planning and Implementation (10%) Works collaboratively with the Dean and other members of the Law Center and LSU community to help determine the overall course and direction of the Law Center. Other Duties (5%) Perform additional responsibilities as required by the Dean of the Law Center as necessary. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school (foreign equivalents considered on a case-by-case basis) and a master’s degree in library and information science from an ALA-accredited institution, superior academic credentials, a commitment to outstanding teaching, and strong administrative, communication, and leadership skills. We welcome applications from candidates seeking either a tenure-track or professional practice-track position. Tenure-track candidates must demonstrate a record of or strong potential for sustained scholarly achievement.      Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach current CV/resume, 3 references, and official transcripts of both JD and MLS degrees. Questions may be directed to Bill Corbett, Chair of the Library Director Search Committee, at lawhrm@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Financial Management, Hiring, Leadership, Library Administration, Researching, Strategic Planning     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 29, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0400-Hebert-Law-Center/Law-Center-Director-of-Bar-Success_R00119923": {
      "title": "Law Center Director of Bar Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Law Center Director of Bar Success     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Paul M Hebert Law Center (Caprice L. Roberts (00076655))     Work Location: 0400 Hebert Law Center     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Summary: The LSU Paul M. Hebert Law Center seeks to hire a non-tenure-track Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor of Professional Practice to serve as its Director of Bar Success. The Director reports to the Dean and serves in a full-time, 12-month position. The LSU Paul M. Hebert Law Center is one of the few law schools in the United States that operates within a mixed legal system of civil and common law, reflecting Louisiana's unique legal tradition. Located at the heart of one of the most beautiful campuses in America, the Law Center is a collegial and intellectually vibrant community that has recently experienced significant momentum. The Director of Bar Success will design, implement, and manage bar preparation programming to assist students in preparing for and passing the Louisiana and out-of-state bar exams, including the NextGen Bar Exam. Job Responsibilities: Bar Success Program Leadership and Administration – 25% Design, implement, manage, and assess comprehensive bar success programs and initiatives to support student and graduate preparation for the Louisiana, out-of-state, and NextGen Bar Exams. Collaborate with commercial bar preparation vendors to enhance program effectiveness and student outcomes. Teaching and Instruction – 25% Develop and teach credit-bearing bar preparation courses and related instructional programming. Create and update course content to align with current bar examination requirements and best practices. Student Advising, Coaching, and Academic Support – 30% Provide individualized advising, coaching, and academic support to students and graduates preparing for bar examinations. Develop personalized study plans and intervention strategies to promote bar readiness and success. Assessment, Data Analysis, and Curriculum Collaboration – 15% Track, analyze, and report bar passage outcomes and related performance data across jurisdictions. Partner with faculty to integrate bar-tested competencies, skills development, and NextGen Bar Exam considerations throughout the curriculum. Other Duties as Assigned – 5% Perform additional responsibilities, special projects, committee service, and other duties in support of the law school's academic success, accreditation, assessment, and student services objectives. Qualifications: Required qualifications include a Juris Doctor (JD) degree from an ABA-accredited law school (or international equivalent), bar membership in any U.S. jurisdiction (active or inactive), and a minimum of two years of experience in law practice, law teaching, or academic support programs. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred qualifications include experience in bar success program coordination or administration, experience with data collection and analysis, and familiarity with the Louisiana bar exam.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Questions may be directed to Missy Lonegrass, Chair of the Faculty Appointments Committee, at lawhrm@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 29, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Manship-School-Research-Facility/Transient---PPRL-Outbound-Phone-Survey-Researcher_R00119754": {
      "title": "Transient - PPRL Outbound Phone Survey Researcher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Transient - PPRL Outbound Phone Survey Researcher     Position Type: Transient (Fixed Term) (Seasonal)     Department: LSUAM MC - Reilly Center - Ops - PPRL Call Center (Dyrel Treadwell (00001392))     Work Location: Manship School Research Facility     Pay Grade: Temporary     Job Description: The PPRL Outbound Phone Survey Researcher position involves interviewing people via telephone and accurately entering responses into a computer-based data collection system. The questions typically involve a variety of business, health, political and economic issues. This job is relatively low stress, as it requires sitting, dialing phone numbers, data entry, and interacting with people on the phone. This is a remote job. You will perform this job entirely off-site at your home. This job posting is for an out-bound call center. We do not receive any incoming calls. Personal Requirements for this job include: Basic computer knowledge Basic typing skills Must have acceptable reading and pronunciation skills Must be friendly, outgoing and have a conversational tone of voice You must have a clear speaking voice and be able to communicate well over the phone Must be able to follow set procedures including the ability to read scripts verbatim Must have some previous retail or customer service experience All applicants must include a resume. Home Requirements for this job include: A relatively up-to-date home computer A strong Ethernet/broadband internet connection at home A headset w/ microphone that can plug into your home computer A quiet homework environment with minimal interruptions The hours available are Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday 5pm-9pm, Saturdays & Sundays 10am to 9pm. You do not have to work every day listed above, or every hour listed above, but the minimum shift length is 3 hours. As a reminder, the job pays $12.50/hr. You can work as little as you want as long as your shift length is at least 3 hours. The position requires a minimum commitment of at least 12 hours per week, with a maximum of no more than 20 hours per week.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a current resume. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dyrel Treadwell at dtread2@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0100-Administrative-Support-Building/Custodian-3_R00119769": {
      "title": "Custodian 3",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Custodian 3     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM FA - FPO - FS - BldSvc - DayMgmt2 - D&W - Supv (Shawn Cordell Brown Jr. (00089766))     Work Location: 0100 Administrative Support Building     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Serve as a Lead worker under the direction of a Custodian Supervisor A as part of a crew, providing custodian care to academic and administrative buildings. May be assigned to specific facilities with a variety of functions as required. Will have supervisory responsibilities in the absence of Custodian Supervisor A.  Job Duties: 50%- Serve as lead worker amongst the custodian staff. Support Supervisors in the day-to day which may include but is not limited to inspections and job follow-up. Assist Custodian Supervisor As with time and attendance records, distribution of keys, supplies and materials. Stands in for Custodian Supervisor A's in their absence. May assist with other supervisory task such as hiring, discipline and training.  40%- Performing housekeeping task, manual labor and other activities necessary for the efficient operation of the campus.  Performs the same tasks and duties assigned to Custodian 2s. Inspects and ensures that all equipment to be used is safe and fully functional.  10%- Performs any other miscellaneous related duties necessary to maintain the cleanliness and sanitary conditions of the University as well as the efficient and safe operation of the department. Performs any other miscellaneous related duties necessary to maintain the cleanliness and sanitary conditions of the University, as well as the efficient and safe operation of the department.  Minimum Qualifications: One year of experience in custodial, housekeeping, groundskeeping, or food service work.   Special or Physical Qualifications: This position is considered emergency essential and may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. This position will require a physical evaluation based on the physical demands required. Louisiana State Civil Service Job Details: https://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=175910     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Shawn Brown at sbrown16@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 7, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
