    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0100-Administrative-Support-Building/Custodian-2_R00119623": {
      "title": "Custodian 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Custodian 2     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM FA - FPO - FS - BldSvc - NightMgmt2 (Winkeyssa Genese Robertson (00047719))     Work Location: 0100 Administrative Support Building     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Job Description Serves on custodial crew to maintain the cleanliness and sanitary conditions of the University and grounds. Will work in various facilities with a variety of functions as required.  Job Duties: 30%- Performs housekeeping tasks, manual labor, and other activities necessary for the efficient operation of the campus and could include the following areas: offices, classrooms, laboratories, residence hall lobbies, bathrooms, stairwells, elevators, hallways, and other assigned areas. Cleaning includes sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, scrubbing, dusting, and polishing. Mixes or blends routine cleaning solutions to proper concentration.  30%- Empties trash and recycling containers, transports waste material to outdoor refuse or recycling containers as appropriate. May be required to work around and/or handle hazardous materials including but not limited to, transporting bio-hazardous waste boxes to storage for pickup. Determined by visual inspection if material is acceptable or unacceptable for recycling, according to written standards. Cleans, decontaminates and deodorizes waste containers.  10%- Performs floor maintenance and other special cleaning tasks, such as cleaning, stripping, waxing, and polishing floors, and carpet cleaning using industrial grade machines. Stain removal on carpets and resilient floors. Strips floors using chemical strippers, scrubs, spray buffs or burnishes resilient floors. Operates wet/dry vacuum, carpet extraction equipment or other commercial equipment as required for cleaning and shampooing carpets or cleaning water leaks. Cleans and removes stains from upholstered furniture. Uses equipment according to label direction for correct dilution & application. Operating a flood pump or other equipment to remove flood waters from buildings.  10%- Moves/rearranges office furniture, fixtures, and lab equipment as well as sets up tables, chairs, partitions, sign stanchions and other related equipment used for special events including but not limited to, programs, registrations, Spring Testing, Commencement, seminars, Open House, meetings, or any other scheduled event 10%- Washes building exteriors, windows, walls, fixtures, steps and sidewalks using power washers, pressure sprayers, commercial window washing equipment, cleaning solutions, ladders, scaffolds, hydraulic man-lifts, or other related equipment or materials. Service related equipment, such as checking fuel, oil, solution tanks and filling as needed  5%- Unlocks/locks campus buildings, labs, offices, or rooms utilizing assigned building, room, or master keys. Has responsibility for security of all keys issued as part of daily assignment 5%- May perform a variety of other tasks including but not limited to: maintain and clean equipment used in performance of assigned duties, wear safety equipment or clothing as instructed by supervisor - such as gloves, goggles, dust masks, etc., report maintenance or safety hazards to supervisor, and report the need for equipment and supplies for the area to your supervisor. Perform other duties as necessary to maintain the cleanliness and sanitary conditions of the University, as well as the efficient and safe operation of the department.  Minimum Qualifications: Six months of experience in custodial, housekeeping, groundskeeping, or food service work. Additional Information: This position is considered emergency essential and may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. This position will require a physical evaluation based on the physical demands required. Louisiana State Civil Service Job Details: http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=100270         Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Winkeyssa Robertson at wrobertson1@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 7, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0100-River-Road-Annex-Building/Mobile-Equipment-Operator-2--Truck-Driver-Moving-Specialist-_R00119622": {
      "title": "Mobile Equipment Operator 2 (Truck Driver Moving Specialist)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Mobile Equipment Operator 2 (Truck Driver Moving Specialist)     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM FA - FPO - FS - BldSvc - Moving - Operations (Thomas Michael Wilcox (00071985))     Work Location: 0100 River Road Annex Building     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Works on a Special Events and Moving crew which provides logistical and labor support for the moving of University Departments, assists individuals, academic departments and other University groups with logistical support for special events, programs and other activities within major State University, with over 30,000 students and 4,500 full time faculty and staff. Hours are 7:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m., Monday through Friday, however, extended hours and weekends may be required in order to meet the needs of the University. Job Responsibilities Operates stakes body or flat bed trucks with a GVW rating of 10,000 to 26,000 pounds to transport various material, equipment, office furnishing, chemical drums and other materials as required for the operation of the university. On occasion may also operate smaller vehicles such as van, pick up trucks or enclosed trucks. - 30% Directs and oversees the loading and unloading of vehicles, material handling, moving office furnishings and performs all the same functions as Laboring personnel involved these services.- 25% Exercise functional supervision over Laborers, Helpers, Mobile Equipment Operator 1 's and Custodians 1's and 2's involved in providing moving and hauling services, setting up for special events, moving University Department, moving heavy research and laboratory equipment. Must have a working knowledge material handling and related moving equipment, handling heavy loads, handling office furnishings and computer and other materials and equipment found on a large University, May also supervise student workers in this capacity.- 15% Operates a boom truck with a boom rating 8,000 pounds and GVW rating 22,000 pounds. Operates forklifts and scissors lifts with lifting capacity over 10,000 pounds or lift height of 12 feet. Uses safety cages, forklift extender as necessary. Will do power washing. -10% Pick-up, loads and delivers surplus property to the University Property warehouse and the State Property Control warehouse. Verifies the correctness of delivers and pick-ups by checking University equipment tag numbers against the property control forms and paperworks. Checks work done by laboring personnel to ensure correctness and maintain inventory control. -5% Make recommendation to supervision and management regarding rigging of loads, moving material, including technique, man-power and special equipment required -5% Sets up and assembles multi-sectional staging from 1O\" to 42\" high and risers by doing the actual work or directing the efforts of laboring personnel. Inspects completed work to ensure that it is safe, functional and capable of supporting the intended personnel or activity -5% Exercise functional supervision over laboring personnel performing a wide variety if miscellaneous physical labor functions as required to maintain the efficient operation of the University. Assists as required and performs all the same functions as laboring personnel. Assembles furniture, special events set up, Modular Office systems, shelving and other items using hand tools. Make minor repairs on special events furniture. Other duties as assigned .-5% Additional Information This position requires a valid driver's license, will require an MVR, and is subject to drug screens per PM-33/PS-67/FASOP HR-04. This position is considered emergency essential and may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. This position is classified as a safety and security-sensitive position. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04 This position will require a physical evaluation based on the physical demands required. Minimum Qualifications One year of experience in mobile equipment operations. Minimum Certifications/Licenses Class D Driver's License Louisiana State Civil Service Job Details http://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=103440     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Thomas Wilcox at twilco4@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 14, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0100-Landscape-Services-Building/Horticultural-Attendant-Superintendent_R00119872": {
      "title": "Horticultural Attendant-Superintendent",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Horticultural Attendant-Superintendent     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM FA - FPO - FS - Land - Turf Supervision (James C Ransom III (00012369))     Work Location: 0100 Landscape Services Building     Pay Grade: Classified Technician and Skilled Trades     Job Description: This position supervises and works on grounds maintenance, special grounds and landscape installation projects including but not limited to irrigation, drainage, concrete, arbor, etc. This position also installs and maintains turf, landscape beds and irrigation systems. Emergency and/or routine work includes but is not limited to concrete/asphalt removal/repair, tree/limb removal, planting/bracing, grounds projects and special functions/events. This position supervises grounds and construction employees, inmate crews and contract labor. This position requires the ability to complete any necessary administrative responsibilities. Job Duties 65%- Supervise and support direct reports. assigned crews, inmate labor, and contract labor to perform daily landscape maintenance and installation tasks such as but not limited to mowing. string trimming, chemical application. agriculture services, concrete maintenance and installation, irrigation maintenance & installation, landscape installation, bed and soil preparation work. hardscape layout and installation. planting, sodding, etc. on both regular maintenance and new projects. 10%- Plan, schedule, and procure materials and equipment for maintenance and project related tasks. 10%- Perform all Human Resource related tasks such as but not limited to time keeping, performance reviews, accident reports, disciplinary work, etc. Assure that all machinery and equipment used is cleaned and maintained properly and communicate repair needs to the shop foreman. Perform safety meetings on a monthly basis. 5%- Supervise and perform preventative maintenance, repair and daily cleaning of assigned equipment; campus irrigation inspections; system commissioning and follow up repair tasks to ensure proper operation. 5%- Perform other duties as directed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Four years of experience or training in farming, the care and maintenance of trees and shrubs, or groundskeeping; OR Twenty-four semester hours in a plant science or landscape field of study. Special or Physical Qualifications: Due to the nature of this position and/or position responsibilities this position shall be subject to drug/alcohol testing in accordance with University Policy Statement 67.  In accordance with PS-18 this position maybe required to report to or stay on campus in the event of emergency or closure.  Must be able to lift 50 lbs, be capable of stooping, kneeling, balancing, or crouching; able to reach and/or climb a ladder. Position is subject to outside environmental conditions.  Due to the position's physical requirements, a pre-employment physical examination will be required per FASOP: HR-04. Certifications/Licenses: Valid Driver's License Louisiana State Civil Service Job Details: https://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=105980     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact James Ransom at jranso1@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 7, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Louise-Garig-Hall/Custodian-1-or-2_R00119642": {
      "title": "Custodian 1 or 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Custodian 1 or 2     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - ResLife - Housing - Operations (Jace Owens Sr. (00075635))     Work Location: Louise Garig Hall     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Serves on a custodian crew providing services for the Department of Residential Life maintaining over 1,900,000 square feet in residence halls and apartments housing over 5,000 students at the state's only comprehensive, Class 1 Research University with over 25,000 students and 4,500 full time faculty and staff. High degrees of public contact and interaction with staff and students. Frequent contacts with general public through support provided for continuing education programs, seminars, institutes, workshops and conferences. 30% Cleans residence hall lobbies, bathrooms, hallways and other assigned areas by sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, dusting and polishing.  Works in areas requiring a higher degree of knowledge and skill related to that specific area.  May be required to work around or handle hazardous materials.  Mixes or blends routine cleaning solutions to proper concentration. 20% Empties trash and recycling containers, transports waste material to outdoor refuse containers or recycling containers as appropriate.  May be responsible for removing and disposing of bio-hazardous waste.  Determines by visual inspection if material is acceptable for recycling, according to written standards.  Clean, decontaminate and deodorize waste containers. 10% Cleans, strips, waxes and polishes floors using industrial size mops and/or commercial type floor machines.  Uses commercial stripper, waxes, floor sealers, cleaners and pads according to label direction for correct dilution and application. 10% Operates wet/dry vacuum, carpet extraction equipment, other commercial equipment as required for cleaning and shampooing carpets or cleaning up after water leaks or floods.  Operate a flood pump or other equipment to remove flood waters from buildings. 10% Washes building exteriors, windows, walls, fixtures, steps and sidewalks using power washers, pressure sprayers, commercial window washing equipment, cleaning solutions or other related equipment and materials. 10% Unlocks/locks campus buildings utilizing assigned building, room and master keys. Has responsibility for security of all keys issued as part of daily assignment. Moves and sets up tables, chairs, partitions, sign stanchions and other related equipment used for special events such as programs, registration, Spring Testing, etc. May be required to move or rearrange office furniture and fixtures . 5% May perform a variety of other tasks including one or more of the following: maintain and clean equipment; wear safety equipment or clothing as instructed per supervisor; report safety hazards to supervisor; carry a note pad and pencil to record maintenance problems found in buildings; report maintenance needs of building and equipment daily, 5% Perform any other miscellaneous custodial related duties necessary to maintain the cleanliness and sanitary conditions of buildings and grounds.   Custodian 1 Minimum Qualifications: No experience or training required.   https://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=100300   *Test Score Not Required Custodian 2 Minimum Qualifications: Six months of experience in custodial, housekeeping, grounds keeping or food service work.   https://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=100270   * Test Score Not Required Special or Physical Qualifications (BOTH LEVELS):   Must be capable of walking around a 10,000 square foot building multiple times daily and be able to ascend and descend the stairs of a 5 story building multiple times daily and stand for extended period of time. Be capable to stoop, kneel, and crouch.   Capable of moving furniture that weighs 20 to 40 lbs or more and transport cleaning carts and various equipment to different parts of the building on occasion In accordance with University Policy Statement 18, this position is considered essential and may be required to report or stay on campus in the event of emergency or closure. Due to the position's physical requirements, a pre-employment physical examination will be required per FASOP: HR-04.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please fully complete the Experience section of the application, listing out job duties and average weekly hours worked. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Jace Owens, Jace.owens@lsu.edu or 225-578-5580     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 8, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU---Pennington-Biomedical/Assistant-to-the-Asociate-Executive-Director-of-Clinical-Science_R00119832": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Asociate Executive Director of Clinical Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: At the forefront of medical discovery as it relates to understanding the causes of obesity, diabetes, cardiovascular disease, cancer and dementia, Pennington Biomedical Research Center is a campus of Louisiana State University and conducts basic, clinical and population research. The Center includes Basic Science, Clinical Research, and Population and Public Health, enabling both focused research and translational science. Research at Pennington Biomedical is supported broadly by multiple NIH Research Centers , and includes approximately 65 faculty and 20 postdoctoral fellows who comprise a network of 44 laboratories and 13 highly specialized core service facilities.  Pennington Biomedical is located within state-of-the-art research facilities on a 222-acre campus in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant to the Asociate Executive Director of Clinical Science     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUPBRC ExD - Clinical Science (Juan Lertora (00057945))     Work Location: LSU - Pennington Biomedical     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Pennington Biomedical Research Center , a world-renowned academic research institute of Louisiana State University, is seeking an Assistant to the Associate Executive Director of Clinical Science. The Assistant to the Associate Executive Director (AED) of Clinical Science provides high-level executive administrative and operational support to the Associate Executive Director's office. This position serves as a key administrative liaison for the AED, coordinating complex schedules, meetings, travel, communications, documentation, special projects, and departmental activities. The executive assistant works independently and exercises sound judgment, discretion, and confidentiality when managing sensitive information and competing priorities. The position also coordinates administrative activities associated with the NIDDK NORC grant and supports communication and collaboration among leadership, faculty, staff, internal departments, and external stakeholders. This role requires exceptional organizational, communication, time-management, and problem-solving skills and the ability to anticipate needs, manage multiple priorities, and effectively support an executive-level leader in a complex clinical science and research environment.   Major Responsibilities Provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Associate Executive Director (AED) of Clinical Science by coordinating daily priorities, managing administrative needs, exercising independent judgment, and ensuring timely follow-through on executive priorities and initiatives. Manage the AED's calendar, schedule, and travel, including prioritizing appointments and meetings, coordinating travel arrangements and itineraries, processing leave and expense reports, and managing other administrative requirements. Plan and coordinate meetings, events, and executive activities, including developing agendas, preparing materials and presentations, coordinating participants and logistics, documenting meetings, and tracking decisions, action items, and deadlines. Prepare and manage executive-level communications and documents, including reports, correspondence, presentations, briefing materials, and documents requiring review, approval, or signature; gather, organize, and summarize information as needed. Coordinate administrative and operational activities for the NORC grant, including serving as a liaison among NORC members and leadership; monitoring grant activities, funding, publications, timelines, and deliverables; coordinating committee and advisory board meetings; maintaining the NORC website; supporting Pilot & Feasibility programs; and coordinating annual progress reports and competitive renewal activities. Provide administrative and logistical support to Clinical Science departments reporting to the AED, including coordinating requests, facilitating communication, preparing materials, organizing meetings, and supporting departmental operations and initiatives. Coordinate special projects and strategic initiatives on behalf of the AED by researching and gathering information, monitoring progress, coordinating activities across departments, and preparing updates to support timely completion of objectives. Manage the day-to-day operations of the AED's office, including responding to inquiries, coordinating communications, maintaining confidential records, and serving as a professional point of contact for internal and external stakeholders. Perform other duties and special projects assigned in support of Clinical Science and organizational objectives. Occasional work outside normal business hours may be required to support executive schedules, events, and deadlines. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business administration, healthcare administration, public administration, communications, management, or a related field.* Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience providing executive-level administrative, program, or operational support in a complex organizational environment; an equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Three (3) years of experience supporting an executive, senior leader, director, physician, researcher, or comparable professional-level position. Two (2) years of experience coordinating complex projects, programs, grants, or organizational initiatives, including responsibility for timelines, documentation, deliverables, and follow-up. Two (2) years of experience coordinating executive-level meetings, conferences, events, or multi-stakeholder activities. Proficiency in Microsoft Office 365, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Demonstrated proficiency in preparing and editing professional correspondence, reports, presentations, and other executive-level documents with a high degree of accuracy. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple concurrent priorities and deadlines while maintaining a high level of accuracy, organization, and confidentiality. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to interact effectively with individuals at all organizational levels, including executive leadership and external stakeholders. Ability to exercise independent judgment, maintain confidentiality, prioritize competing demands, and represent executive leadership in a professional manner. Ability to work occasional evenings or outside normal business hours to support executive activities, meetings, events, or time-sensitive deadlines. * Pennington Biomedical is committed to creating an inclusive space where our employees feel valued for their skills and uniqueness. If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications as listed, but has significant experience within the major job responsibilities, we welcome their application. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a clinical, healthcare, biomedical research, academic, or higher education environment. Experience providing administrative coordination for federal, state, foundation, or other sponsored research grants. Experience supporting senior leadership within a research, academic medical, or healthcare organization. Experience with enterprise systems used for scheduling, financial management, electronic document management, or project coordination. ​ Pennington Biomedical Research Center seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce with a broad range of backgrounds and perspectives and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Interested candidates should include a resume and a list of three (3) professional references to the online application. Professional references should be the name, title, company, and contact information from past employers. Professional references should include current or previous supervisors and/or coworkers. Personal references should not be considered for the reference check process. We will respect the request that we not contact a current employer. However, we will need to contact a prior supervisor if such a request is made. A letter of application/cover letter is recommended but not required. Official transcripts are required prior to hire and are not required at the time of application.     Posting Date: August 28, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 28, 2026    Additional Position Information: Pennington Biomedical is located within state-of-the-art research facilities on a 222-acre campus in Baton Rouge, Louisiana . For more information, visit PBRC . Questions regarding career opportunities at Pennington Biomedical should be sent to hrm@pbrc.edu . Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - Pennington Biomedical Research Center offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     Pennington Biomedical Research Center/LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to PBRC Human Resources at 225-763-2776 or hrm@pbrc.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Student-Health-Center-Cl-Infirmary-Building/Medical-Laboratory-Technologist-2_R00119796": {
      "title": "Medical Laboratory Technologist 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Medical Laboratory Technologist 2     Position Type: Classified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - H&WB - SHC - MAS - Laboratory (Suzanne Elizabeth Mouch (00009166))     Work Location: Student Health Center (C&l Infirmary) Building     Pay Grade: Classified Medical     Job Description: The Medical Technologist (MT) is a member of a multi-disciplinary team in the Medical Clinic, including primary care, gynecology and specialty care. The MT performs a variety of clinical diagnostic tests with an emphasis on recognizing and resolving problems and applying interpretive judgment. The MT is responsible for employing practice standards and supporting quality improvement efforts. The MT should have a deep appreciation for a collaborative care model, partnering with all areas of the SHC, and be committed to advancing the divisional priorities of commitment to quality, communicating a sense of home, and designing with everyone in mind, and cultivating a working relationship with Our Lady of the Lake Health. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES 30% - Calibrate and operate equipment and conduct performance checks with appropriate documentation. Establish and monitor quality improvement programs to ensure data accuracy and reliability. Identify and investigate problems with testing, instruments and results, documenting appropriately. Serve as a technical consultant. 25% - Interpret, verify and report test results, utilizing the lab information system and the clinic management system/electronic health record. Consult with the laboratory team if testing and reporting concerns arise. Notify medical providers of critical values according to procedure. Perform inventory management, quality monitoring, data analysis, peer competency and prepare reports for quality assessment. 20% - Perform venipunctures and specimen collection. Follow appropriate safety protocols. Label and prepare specimens for analysis, storage and transport to reference laboratories. Prepare lab requests for specimen collection and processing. Maintain working knowledge of all lab tests and associated fees and inform patients accordingly. Collect immunization forms and assist students with related questions. 20% - Assist with data entry and distribution of laboratory, insurance and billing information, correspondence and medical reports, maintaining strict patient confidentiality and compliance with the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA). Complete required trainings as assigned by the university and the Student Health Center. Support quality improvement and accreditation efforts. 5% - Performs other duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Possession of a current Louisiana Clinical Laboratory Scientist-Generalist or Clinical Laboratory Scientist-Specialist license plus one of the following: A bachelor's degree in medical technology or clinical laboratory science plus one year of experience as a medical technologist; OR A bachelor's degree in a biological, physical, or chemical science plus two years of experience as a medical technologist. SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to drug/alcohol testing in accordance with University Policy Statement 67. In accordance with University Policy Statement 18, this position is considered essential and may be required to report or stay on campus in the event of an emergency or closure. May be required to work occasional nights and weekends. LOUISIANA STATE CIVIL SERVICE JOB DETAILS https://apps01.civilservice.louisiana.gov/onestopjobinfo/DisplayJobSpec.aspx?JobCode=117270     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please provide a resume and three references, official transcripts, a copy of license to practice, and board certification - ASCP or AMT. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Kelsi Taylor at 225-578-2308.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     A permanent or probationary internal employee who is appointed to another position following certification from an open competitive eligible list is considered a new employee in the new position and shall serve a probationary period of six months.      Posting Date: August 28, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 11, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!   Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Business-Education-Rotunda/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Entrepreneurship_R00110910": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COB - Stephenson Department of Entrepreneurship and Information Systems (Edward Fisk Watson III (00001317))     Work Location: Business Education Rotunda     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Summary: The Stephenson Department of Entrepreneurship & Information Systems invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Entrepreneurship at the Assistant / Associate Professor rank to begin in Fall 2027. The Associate Professor rank may come with tenure.  Associate Professors and senior Assistant Professors are highly encouraged to apply. Senior applicants must have a strong research record and junior candidates must show promise for the development of a solid research agenda. This position requires the Assistant/Associate Professor to teach entrepreneurship courses at the undergraduate and graduate-level and to conduct research and publish in top entrepreneurship and closely related journals. Job Responsibilities: 45% - Teach undergraduate and graduate-level Entrepreneurship courses.  Normal teaching load is two courses or sections per semester for a total of four courses or sections per academic year. 45% - Engage in academic research and publish in academic journals. 10% - Provide service to the department, College, and university. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Ph.D./ DBA in Entrepreneurship, Management or related field; For Assistant Professor level, ABD candidates will be considered. Years of Experience: Assistant Professor: 0-5 years Associate Professor: 6+ years Demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching or demonstrated potential for excellence. Job Competencies: Course Instruction - Proficient Research - Proficient Communication - Advanced     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide cover letter, CV, available teaching evaluations, and three professional references including name, title, phone number, and email address. A copy of your transcript may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire. Candidates are encouraged to apply by October 1, 2026, but applications will continue to be considered until the position is filled. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis. The search committee hopes to begin interviewing candidates during the Fall 2026 semester. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. Ed Watson, ewatson@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 28, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 17, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
