    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/3325-Patrick-F-Taylor-Hall/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Professor-of-Research_R00119770": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Engineering - School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Shuangqing Wei (00007502))     Work Location: 3325 Patrick F. Taylor Hall     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Assistant Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, quality control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Work under the general direction of senior investigators while demonstrating increasing independence in research design and execution. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Provide day-to-day technical guidance to students and postdoctoral researchers in coordination with project principal investigators. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Contribute technical ideas, preliminary results, and written materials to collaborative proposal development. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Specific Experience: Demonstrated research accomplishments through peer-reviewed publications. Evidence of the ability and potential to conduct high-quality independent and collaborative research. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Specific Experience: Postdoctoral or industrial research experience. Experience participating in federally sponsored research. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Experience contributing to research proposal development. Associate Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Lead substantial research tasks or projects and coordinate technical activities across multidisciplinary teams. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Supervise graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research personnel, and mentor junior researchers in scholarly publication and professional development. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Develop and lead proposal sections or complete proposals and serve, as appropriate, as Principal Investigator, Co-Principle Investigator, or key personnel on externally funded projects. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 5 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Strong and sustained record of peer-reviewed publications demonstrating research excellence. Demonstrated success in obtaining or making significant contributions to externally funded research. Experience supervising graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, or research personnel. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 5 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Experience serving as Principal Investigator, Co-Principal Investigator, or key personnel on externally funded research. Experience leading multidisciplinary research projects. Established national reputation in one or more relevant research areas. Experience managing project schedules, milestones, personnel, and sponsor deliverables. Professor of Research 40% Sponsored Research: Conduct innovative research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, machine learning, distributed optimization, and intelligent autonomous systems for distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. Design and develop mathematical models, algorithms, engineering simulations, software tools, experiments, and testing methodologies for distributed multi-agent systems, resilient communications, intelligent sensing, autonomous decision-making, and cooperative autonomous operations. Manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments, and tests, and collect and analyze data while ensuring data integrity, control, and research reproducibility. Maintain currency with relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, communications and networking methods, and machine learning techniques. Publish research findings in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Provide senior scientific and technical leadership for major sponsored research activities and coordinate research across multiple investigators, disciplines, and partner organizations. 35% Supervise Graduate Students and Postdoctoral Researchers: Provide research supervision and technical mentoring to graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research associates, and other research personnel. Guide research planning, technical development, experimental and simulation activities, publication preparation, sponsor deliverables, and professional development while fostering a collaborative and inclusive research environment. Lead and mentor multidisciplinary teams of graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, research faculty, research associates, and technical staff. 25% Research Program Development and External Funding: Identify funding opportunities and participate in developing competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Initiate and develop contacts and collaborations with grant and contract agencies, faculty members, industry partners, and other academic institutions to support the growth of externally funded research programs. Contribute to proposal preparation, technical planning, budgeting, project reporting, sponsor communications, and the preparation of technical reports and other research-related documentation. Lead the development of major multidisciplinary proposals, cultivate sponsor and industry relationships, and provide management leadership for research portfolios, budgets, schedules, deliverables, personnel, and sponsor reporting. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 10 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Internationally recognized record of scholarly achievement and high-impact peer-reviewed publications. Sustained record of externally funded research as Principal Investigator, Co-Principal Investigator, or equivalent research leader. Demonstrated experience leading multidisciplinary research programs and managing sponsored research projects. Proven record of mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research personnel. Demonstrated record of project management and proposal development. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline with 10 years of post Ph.D. research experience. Specific Experience: Experience leading large multidisciplinary research initiatives involving universities, industry, and government agencies. Experience developing long-term research partnerships and strategic sponsored research programs. Professional leadership through editorial service, conference organization, or leadership roles in professional societies. Record of technology transition, patents, software dissemination, or other research impact.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The Division of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) in the School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) at Louisiana State University invites applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Research position. The successful candidate will conduct innovative sponsored research in data-driven modeling, communications, networking, artificial intelligence, machine learning, intelligent autonomous systems, and distributed maritime operations involving both surface and underwater autonomous vehicles. The successful candidate will join a vibrant and collaborative interdisciplinary research team consisting of faculty, research scientists, postdoctoral researchers, and graduate students from Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, and Mathematics. The team conducts cutting-edge research, supported by federal agencies and industry partners, in distributed multi-agent systems, autonomous maritime operations, communications, networking, machine learning, and intelligent autonomous systems. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, contribute to large multidisciplinary research projects, and help develop innovative technologies with real-world applications. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the growth of externally funded research programs through high-quality research, scholarly publications, mentoring of graduate students and postdocs, and the development of competitive research proposals. Questions regarding this position can be directed to Shuangqing Wei at swei@lsu.edu. Due to sponsor requirements associated with federally funded research, applicants must be U.S. citizens or lawful permanent residents (Green Card holders). Applications from individuals who do not meet this requirement will not be considered.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 27, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 23, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Veterinary-Medicine/Veterinary-Assistant-1--2--or-3-Anesthesia_R00119705": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistant 1, 2, or 3-Anesthesia",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Veterinary Assistant 1, 2, or 3-Anesthesia     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM VetMed - VTH - Admin - Nursing - Anesthesia (Torri Rae Collins (00006295))     Work Location: Veterinary Medicine     Pay Grade:     Job Description: This position provides anesthesia and anesthetic support for all clinical service areas, including Small Animal Internal Medicine, Small Animal Surgery, specialty small animal services, and all Large Animal clinical services. Responsibilities include preparing and monitoring patients before, during, and after anesthesia; assisting faculty clinicians and house officers with anesthetic procedures; and ensuring the safe delivery of anesthesia in accordance with established hospital protocols. The individual must possess expertise in the safe handling and restraint of small animals and be able to provide instruction and guidance to veterinary students in anesthesia techniques, patient monitoring, and proper animal handling while fostering a safe and effective clinical learning environment.   Veterinary Assistant 1: 35%-Assist with all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Assist with providing technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Assist with the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Assist with the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Assist with routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Assist with ensuring immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Participate in providing emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology OR credentials as a vet tech or equivalent OR 3 years of experience in a working environment with similar duties Veterinary Assistant 2: 35%-Perform and demonstrate all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Provide technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Perform and demonstrate the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Participate in the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Perform and demonstrate routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Ensure immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Perform and demonstrate emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned.   Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology with 2 years' experience OR credentials as a vet tech or equivalent with 2 years' experience OR 5 years of experience in a working environment with similar duties.  Veterinary Assistant 3: 35%-Perform and teach all aspects of anesthetic induction and patient preparation, including assisting with the placement and maintenance of peripheral intravenous, central venous, and arterial catheters. Assist with endotracheal intubation, including verification of placement, aspiration prevention, and troubleshooting airway complications. Provide technical support for epidural injections, regional nerve blocks, and other anesthesia-related procedures. Develop and maintain working knowledge of sedatives, injectable and inhalant anesthetic agents, anesthetic equipment, and multi-modal patient monitoring to ensure the safe administration and recovery of anesthetized patients. 30%-Perform and teach the day-to-day operations of the Anesthesia Service, including assisting faculty clinicians, house officers, and veterinary students with anesthetic procedures, patient monitoring, and emergency cases. Develop and apply working knowledge of patient care, anesthesia monitoring, diagnostic techniques, and treatment protocols in accordance with established hospital standards. Participate in the clinical instruction of veterinary and veterinary technician students by assisting clinical veterinary students, house officers, and faculty clinicians with anesthesia procedures, patient care, and treatments while promoting safety. 15%-Perform and teach routine maintenance, cleaning, and quality control of anesthesia equipment, while ensuring anesthesia work areas are clean, organized, and adequately stocked with supplies. Maintain the Anesthesia Service in a constant state of readiness by preparing equipment, medications, and emergency supplies for scheduled procedures and urgent cases. Ensure immediate availability of equipment and materials required for cardiopulmonary cerebral resuscitation (CPCR) and other emergency anesthetic interventions. 15%-Perform and teach emergency anesthesia support by assisting in the assessment, stabilization, and anesthetic management of patients presenting emergency service requiring surgical intervention. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to after-hours emergencies as assigned, including serving as essential personnel during emergency response and ride-out operations. 5%-Other duties as assigned.  Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; OR associate's degree in veterinary technology with 4 years' experience OR credentials as a vet tech or equivalent with 4 years' experience OR 7 years of experience in a working environment with similar duties.  Job Skills Needed for All Levels: Knowledge of basic animal care and handling including restraint   Knowledge of medical terminology, basic anatomy, and abbreviations Basic computer skills, problem-solving and communication skills    Knowledge of proper medical record keeping (paper and electronic) Math skills; including drug calculations (dosage & conversions)  Operation of equipment, diagnostic tests and hand held analyzers  Ability to work independently with minimal supervision  Ability to collect blood from  a number of different sites by venipuncture Proper administration of oral, sub-cutaneous, intra muscular, and intra venous medications Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignment simultaneously     Additional Job Description: Essential Personnel - Required to work a variety of shifts including nights, weekends, holidays, on-call, and emergency response.  Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the general public, or cause significant damage to University property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. Physical Requirements - Required to be capable of more than 50 pounds, standing or walking for prolonged periods, able to reach above and below the shoulder, vision (near sight), vision (far sight), kneel or sit on the floor, push/pulling, grasping, crawling, twisting, squatting, climbing, sitting, and/or bending Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if applicable). Please provide your resume and three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. Questions can be directed to Jose Juarez, jjuarez@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 27, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 26, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
