    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/3196-Energy-Coast-and-Environment-Building/Research-Associate-2_R00119124": {
      "title": "Research Associate 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate 2     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAM CCE - DOCS - Wetland Biogeochemistry (John R White (00008640))     Work Location: 3196 Energy, Coast, and Environment Building     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: The Research Associate 2 will support the Wetland Biogeochemistry Analytical Services (WBAS) laboratory by assisting with sample intake, sample preparation, routine analytical procedures, data entry, and laboratory maintenance activities. This position is designed to provide hands-on experience in environmental analytical techniques while supporting the timely processing of environmental samples submitted by LSU researchers and external clients. Job Responsibilities: Sample Intake and Project Tracking: Receive environmental samples submitted by internal and external clients. Verify sample IDs, chain-of-custody forms, preservation requirements, holding times, and sample integrity. Enter project information into laboratory tracking databases and communicate any discrepancies to laboratory management. 15% Sample Preparation and Laboratory Analysis: Perform routine sample preparation procedures including drying, grinding, weighing, filtration, digestion, extraction, and preservation according to established SOPs and EPA-approved methods. Assist with the preparation of environmental samples including water, sediment, soil, plant, and biological materials. 30% Instrument Operation: Operate routine analytical instrumentation following training and established SOPs, including elemental analyzers (CHN), ICP-OES, TOC analyzers, Seal nutrient analyzers (AA500), and other laboratory equipment. Perform routine calibrations and daily startup/shutdown procedures. 30% Data Management and Quality Control Documentation: Maintain accurate laboratory records and perform data entry into electronic databases and Excel spreadsheets. Assist with quality assurance and quality control documentation, including calibration logs, laboratory control samples, duplicates, blanks, and standard recoveries. Prepare preliminary data summaries for review by senior laboratory staff. 15% Laboratory Maintenance: Prepare stock solutions, calibration standards, and quality control materials. 5% Other duties as assigned. 5% Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's Degree One-year related experience Specific Experience: Familiar with auto pipettes for making calibration standards and quality control standards. Familiar with the proper use of hydrochloric acid, nitric acid and sulfuric acid for cleaning plastic-ware and glassware. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow SOPs. Basic experience with Microsoft Excel. Experience in chemical laboratory procedures and using proper SOP protocol for cleaning laboratory materials. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree Specific Experience: Experience with environmental sample preparation. Experience using analytical instrumentation. Familiarity with EPA methods and laboratory QA/QC procedures. Job Competencies: The use of automatic pipettes for making standards. Proficient Be able to work with others in a laboratory setting. Proficient Strong attention to detail and ability to follow SOPS. Proficient Experience with Microsoft Excel. Proficient Know the rules and regulations for dealing with common acids. Proficient         Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three (3) professional references including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required before hiring. Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to pre-employment screenings in accordance with University Policy as required and RS:17 screenings (https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?p=y&d=1297548). For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Sharon Butler at sbutler@lsu.edu. For questions or concerns about updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 17, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-St-James-Parish-Extension-Office/Assistant-Associate-Extension-Agent--4-H-Youth-Development-_R00119121": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (4-H Youth Development)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (4-H Youth Development)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAG PL4 - Southeast - Parish - St James (Dr. Renee C Naquin (00001094))     Work Location: 0101 St. James Parish Extension Office     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: (This is a grant-funded, non-tenure track position through 06/30/2028. Funding must be available for any continuation of appointment.) Work Location:   The extension office is in Lutcher, Louisiana. The area to be served is St. James Parish, which is in southeast Louisiana with a population of approximately 20,000 residents. The parish has 8 public schools and 1 parochial school. The parish has a potential youth audience of 2000 youth. In addition to school clubs, the parish 4-H program oversees four project clubs: Livestock, Shooting Sports, Junior Leader, and Sewing. The largest programs are Livestock (50-60 youth), Shooting Sports (40-50 youth), and Junior Leader Club (30-40 youth). This position will assist with the oversight of the Shooting Sports program and support Junior Leader Club meetings, activities, and events throughout the year. The program works with over 80 adult and youth volunteers and other non-profit organizations that help support youth programs. The goals of the 4-H Youth Development Program include increasing youth leadership development and community service learning; strengthening the partnership between 4-H and formal education; and expanding volunteer involvement to increase contact hours per youth. Agriculture commodities are sugarcane, soybean, perique tobacco, horticultural crops, and crawfish production.  Position Description : The LSU AgCenter is actively seeking applicants who can contribute to such an environment through their scholarship, teaching, mentoring, and professional service. 4-H Youth Development: The LSU AgCenter St. James Parish Office seeks a 4-H Agent to lead the parish-wide 4-H youth development program. You must demonstrate the ability to work effectively with cultural, ethnically, and socioeconomically diverse audiences. Applicants must have abilities to build and maintain effective working relationships with 4-H adult volunteers, the St. James Parish 4-H Advisory Committee and Foundation, community-based and grassroots organizations, and peers in the LSU AgCenter organization. You will also provide strong leadership in the development of the adult volunteer system and youth-focused life skills educational content that is engaging and relevant to the audience. You will be part of a team that works together in support of initiatives designed to promote and support agriculture and strong families. As a LSU AgCenter faculty member, you will also: work with agencies and organizations to assist or lead cooperative and interdisciplinary projects, both in the parish and through multi-parish efforts; provide service to schools outside of 4-H programming; develop creative works in support of programming, including presentations, professional posters, and web-based education; write scholarly publications related to the field of expertise; and participate in professional associations and service activities for the LSU AgCenter. You will document efforts through an annual plan of work (POW) and report of accomplishment. For those being hired as an Assistant/Associate agent you will be expected to attain promotion and tenure per LSU AgCenter guidelines. What you will do: Plan, develop, teach, evaluate, and report on youth educational programs that meet the needs of the parish’s diverse population in coordination with the St. James Parish 4-H Program and in alignment with the strategic direction of the Louisiana 4-H Youth Development program. Deliver youth development programming through 4-H community clubs, special interest clubs/groups, school enrichment, day camps, after school programs, and other events and activities, emphasizing leadership, community service, and workforce development to name a few. Coordinate youth and volunteer involvement in multi-parish, state, regional, and the national 4-H program and events. Build and lead a strong volunteer base through recruitment, screening, training, and managing adult volunteers, including competency building using state and national 4-H research-based methods. Teach and equip volunteers in educational methods to guide and support 4-H member projects in science, technology, engineering, and math (STEM), including animal sciences, environmental education, robotics, and agriculture, as well as the arts, entrepreneurship, career development, leadership, nutrition, healthy living, and citizenship. Assess and identify opportunities for volunteers to serve in management and leadership roles; then recruit, train, and use volunteers in those roles. Ensure the volunteer screening process is implemented and up to date and oversee all aspects of 4-H program risk management as directed by Louisiana 4-H Headquarters and local policies. Develop program delivery strategies that include the use of deliberately focused virtual platforms. Employ up to 25% virtual programming as appropriate within parish technology resources and stakeholder needs. Encourage and support health equity programming and systems for youth as resources are available. Use a needs assessment to target programs focused on youth, reflecting the parish’s diverse population and the unique educational needs of St. James Parish. Collaborate and develop strategic partnerships with parish and governmental departments, local businesses, and social service agencies to provide diverse and innovative educational opportunities for positive youth development. Use resourcefulness, creativity, enthusiasm, and innovativeness to strengthen current educational programs while reviewing and implementing new policies, maintaining enrollments and records, assessing risks, communicating effectively across social media platforms, managing the program’s financial resources, and creating educational materials. Seek and manage financial resources to support 4-H programming and ensure all financial policies are followed as instructed by LSU AgCenter and 4-H Foundation guidelines. Follow all LSU AgCenter policies and best practices regarding affirmative action, program development, program evaluation, and reporting. Develop and implement a communication plan for 4-H program participants, families, volunteers, and stakeholders using effective and contemporary approaches, including current social media. Write content for various media sources (e.g., newspapers, radio, newsletters, web, social media) to promote programs, report on programs, and educate the public. Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Experience in livestock production and working with youth on 4-H livestock projects. Demonstrated organizational skills. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to use social media in a variety of formats. Comfort presenting in front of small and large crowds. Experience establishing solid partnerships. Highly self-motivated. Innovative audience engagement and development. Demonstrated skills in partnership development and project management. Experience creating lesson plans, developing instructional materials, and applying teaching methods appropriate for the audience. Experience managing volunteers. Experience working in multicultural settings and coursework/training on multicultural topics. Qualification Requirements: A baccalaureate degree in education, vocational education, agricultural sciences, family and consumer sciences/human ecology, biological or social sciences, recreation and leisure studies or closely related areas. Must have an undergraduate degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 2.5 (all GPA requirements based on a 4.0 system) and a 3.0 for graduate work attempted, if any, or master’s degree with an overall grade-point average of at least 3.0 or a current grade-point average of at least 3.0 on at least 12 hours of graduate credit. The applicant must demonstrate effective oral and written communication skills. A master’s degree in a field listed above is desired. Experience in recruiting, training and supervising volunteers and experience in teaching and applying principles of leadership development to both youth and adults is also desired.  Knowledge of public relations and the ability to cope with change are highly desirable characteristics.  Ability to work with and through others is essential as is the ability to function with minimum supervision.  Salary and Benefits:   Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Conditions of Employment:  A personal automobile and appropriate insurance coverage is required (travel allowance provided).  Satisfactory completion of one specific graduate level extension course (3 credit hours) is required in year two or three of employment, prior to promotion eligibility to associate agent.  Additionally, a faculty member who does not have a related master’s degree must complete an additional 12 hours of related graduate level coursework in order to be promoted to associate agent and such promotion must occur in the first seven years of employment.  An exception is that additional agent experience may be substituted for 12 hours of coursework, but not for the required course.  Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline:  September 19, 2026 , or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Qualified candidates must apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU   (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching file(s) containing a curriculum vita, a letter of application, official university transcripts, and two letters of reference. Questions about the online application system should be directed to the HRM Office at 225/578-0324. (Paper, faxed, or emailed application materials will not be accepted.)  In lieu of attaching the letters of reference, they may be sent directly to: Lauren Faust Southeast Regional 4-H Coordinator 479 F. Edward Hebert Blvd. Belle Chasse, LA 70037 Email: LFaust@agcenter.lsu.edu   Phone: 504-934-6975 Web site:  www.lsuagcenter.com The Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and applications will be accepted without regard to race, religion, color, sex, national origin, age, or disability. Information on Equal Employment can be obtained from the EEO and Civil Rights Coordinator, 103 J. Norman Efferson Hall, LSU AgCenter, Baton Rouge, LA 70803. Phone 225.578.2258.  It is the policy of the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service to employ only United States citizens or aliens lawfully authorized to work in the United States. The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Assistant/Associate Extension Agent (4-H Youth Development)     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-Aquaculture-Greenhouse/Research-Associate-Specialist_R00119078": {
      "title": "Research Associate Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate Specialist     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG PL2 - SRNR - Renewable Natural Resources (Kaelyn Jorden Fogelman (00294270))     Work Location: 0101 Aquaculture Greenhouse     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: (This is a grant-funded, non-tenure track position through 08/31/2027.  Funding must be available for any continuation of appointment. Work Location: Aquaculture Research Station, School of Renewable Natural Resources, LSU AgCenter, Baton Rouge, Louisiana Position Description: The LSU AgCenter Aquaculture Research Station is seeking a Research Associate to assist with diverse field and lab work as part of a research program focused on commercial crawfish production. Applicants should have an undergraduate degree (BA, BS) in biology, natural resource ecology management, fisheries, or aquaculture or related field or lab experience aquaculture or aquatic animal husbandry, preferably with invertebrates. The ideal candidate will be experienced in farm equipment operation (tractor, bush hogging), driving and trailering, collecting field (soil, water quality, crayfish) data, and aquaculture pond management. The successful candidate will be involved in several on-going projects involving crawfish pond management, burrowing ecology, reproduction, catchability, behavior, and stress tolerance. The candidate will also be expected to maintain lab and field equipment including equipment, facilities, and infrastructure maintenance at the Aquaculture Research Station. The position involves supporting and working with graduate students, as well as state, federal and non-governmental organization collaborators. Travel to field sites, including overnight stays, and occasional weekend work may be required. Qualification Requirements: A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in biology, natural resource ecology management, fisheries, or aquaculture.  A master’s degree is desired.  Preference will be given to applicants with a degree in an aquaculture or aquatic science or a related field.  Applicant must possess experience in some, or preferably all, of the following (1) experience working in the field, on a farm, aquaculture lab, or commercial aquaculture operation, operating a tractor, and collecting field and laboratory data; (2) ability to work extended days outside during hot and cold days; (3) ability to work independently, create work plans, meet deadlines and collaborate; (4) experience and knowledge of crawfish/crayfish biology and ecology. LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications.  If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (La RS 42:36). Salary and Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with education and experience.  The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline: September 2, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Dr. Kaelyn Fogelman School of Renewable Natural Resources | Aquaculture Research Station LSU AgCenter Baton Rouge, LA 70803-6202 Tel.: (225) 578-4131; Fax: (225) 578-4144; Email: kfogelman@agcenter.lsu.edu   Website: www.lsuagcenter.com The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Research Associate Specialist     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1138-Ruffin-G-Pleasant-Hall/Financial-Aid-Coordinator--Loan-Processing---OBBBA-Compliance_R00119032": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Coordinator/ Loan Processing & OBBBA Compliance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Financial Aid Coordinator/ Loan Processing & OBBBA Compliance     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - EM - Rec - FAS - FA - Operations (Brandi Jones Martin (00003169))     Work Location: 1138 Ruffin G. Pleasant Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The Financial Aid Coordinator of Loan Processing & One Big Beautiful Bill Act (OBBBA) Compliance within Louisiana State University’s Office of Financial Aid & Scholars will play a key collaborative role in advancing the university and meeting the student access objectives. The individual, with general oversight from the Senior Assistant Director of Financial Aid, is responsible for administering, monitoring, and supporting federal student loan processes associated with OBBBA related regulatory and operational requirements. This position ensures accurate loan origination, reconciliation, compliance, and student support while serving as a key source for implementing and maintaining new loan processes. Responsibilities include managing Schedule of Reductions (SOR), resolving loan rejects and discrepancies in the Common Origination and Disbursement (COD) system related to Workday integration and processing issues, and supporting additional OBBBA related financial aid initiatives and compliance requirements. Loan Processing & Administration (20%) Process federal student loan records in accordance with institutional policies and federal regulations. Review, originate, adjust, and reconcile loan awards and disbursements. Monitor loan processing workflows to ensure timely and accurate delivery of aid. Assist with implementation and ongoing management of new loan programs and requirements resulting from OBBBA.   Schedule of Reductions (SOR) Management (20%) Review and process Schedule of Reductions (SOR) transactions. Ensure reductions are accurately reflected in institutional and federal systems. Investigate and resolve discrepancies affecting loan balances and student accounts. Maintain documentation and audit trails for all SOR-related activity.   Common Origination and Disbursement (COD) & Workday Exception Resolution (20%) Monitor and resolve loan rejects, warnings, and edit failures in COD. Research and correct data discrepancies between Workday and COD. Coordinate with Information Technology, Student Accounts, and Financial Aid staff to resolve system integration issues. Track recurring errors and recommend process improvements to reduce future rejects.   Reporting & Process Improvement (20%) Generate and analyze reports related to loan processing, COD rejects, SOR activity, and compliance metrics. Identify trends and recommend corrective actions to improve operational efficiency. Participate in testing, validation, and implementation of Workday updates and financial aid system enhancements. Assist with development and documentation of standard operating procedures.   Student & Campus Support (10%) Accurately interpret and communicate financial aid policies, eligibility requirements, and procedures to ensure students and families fully understand their options and responsibilities. Deliver timely, responsive, student-centered service by addressing concerns efficiently and professionally. Develop communications related to new loan processes and regulatory changes.   Special projects as assigned (10%) Including, but not limited to assigned committees and outreach projects.  Represent LSU and the Office of Enrollment Management & Student Success at professional functions and recruiting events.   Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Meets eligibility to obtain National Student Loan Database System access and must not be in default on a student loan. Our ideal candidate possesses the following qualities: Strong team orientation, effective interpersonal skills, and superior written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated commitment to data-driven decision-making, including effective analytical skills and proven results in achieving objectives and goals. Knowledge of federal financial aid regulations and compliance requirements. Ability to interpret regulatory guidance and translate requirements into operational procedures. Strong attention to detail and data accuracy. Ability to work collaboratively across departments. Demonstrated customer service skills when working with students and families. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information appropriately. As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The location of this position is LSU-BR and is not eligible for remote work. To be considered, qualified candidates will submit a complete application which includes a cover letter explaining their specific interest in the position and how their skills and experiences prepare them for success in this role, a resume, and three professional references. Please provide resume and transcripts, if applicable. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Brandi Martin at brandij@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Communication, Confidentiality, Critical Thinking, Customer-Focused, Decision Making, Policy Knowledge, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 17, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Athletic-Director---Internal-Operations_R00119010-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director - Internal Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Athletic Director - Internal Operations     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUA Chancellor - Athletics (Tyler Scott Unsicker (00071869))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: General Description: The Assistant Athletic Director - Internal Affairs reports to the Director of Athletics and is responsible for assisting in the operations of the department, carrying out all activities necessary to accomplish all its’ objectives within the guidelines of the NAIA, Red River Athletic Conference (RRAC) and Louisiana State University of Alexandria. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the front line of communication for the department, including assisting coaches with work day software, travel and budgeting Oversee and manage all budgets for each sport and administration Complete all requisitions on behalf of department and act as liaison between athletics and the accounting office. Prepare deposits for all Athletics revenues, including ticket sales, fundraisers and all other monies Work with Faculty Athletic Representative on student-athlete NAIA compliance certification Assist Foundation accountant to reconcile vendor invoices, account statements and sponsorship fulfillment Keep records of all signing letters and grant-in-aid agreements between players and coaches Serve as the Title IX Coordinator for the department Annual Reports such as EADA and the NAIA’s ROA Year-End Report Act as point of contact for visiting teams and officials for home events. Update visitor’s guide annually and provide copies to all visiting teams Act as event administrator for assigned athletic events at home and occasionally on the road Oversee all aspects of athletic event ticketing (pre-event sales and setup, event sales, post-event reconciliations and deposits) Direct gameday management at all LSUA home events including overseeing gameday workers and interns for event setup, game responsibilities, and breakdown Help with all operations of conferences and national tournaments hosted by LSUA Write and apply for annual grants with national and local foundations Perform other job-related duties as assigned Required Minimum Qualifications Valid driver license A background check will be required of the successful applicant Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree 2-3 years’ experience in athletic administration *IT IS A CLASS A MISDEMEANOR TO MISREPRESENT ACADEMIC CREDENTIALS     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Instructions: Please attach a Resume/CV, a cover letter, 3 references and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts and a background check will be required upon hire.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 18, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0102-Student-Recreation-Complex/Coordinator-of-Fitness-Operations_R00118910": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Fitness Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Coordinator of Fitness Operations     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - H&WB - URec - PO - Fitness and Wellness (Irma L. Nieves-Torres (00081765))     Work Location: 0102 Student Recreation Complex     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: COORDINATOR OF FITNESS OPERATIONS Reporting to the Assistant Director of Fitness, the Coordinator of Fitness Operations assists in the organization and administration of fitness, supervision of fitness assistant staff/personal trainers, and management of equipment & resources. Through ensuring the fitness floors are well maintained and operated, the Coordinator develops a welcoming environment that fosters a sense of community when utilizing the UREC.    GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES FOR THIS POSITION INCLUDE: Support the supervision of student staff who manage the fitness floors Train and supervise students who work as Fitness Assistants and/or Personal Trainers Provide direct support for members who participate in our Personal Training program Familiarity with the best practices as it relates to fitness and wellness that align with our mission OPPORTUNITIES FOR LEADERSHIP: Enhance the student and member experience Nearly 30,000 distinct LSU students and members utilize the UREC at least once a year. This position has a leadership role in establishing consistent, high-quality experiences for how members engage within our fitness programs and services. Through ensuring the fitness floors are well maintained and operated, the coordinator develops a welcoming environment that fosters a sense of community when utilizing the UREC.  Optimize student staff experience Actively engages in the recruitment, interviewing, hiring, and scheduling of new Fitness Assistants and Personal Trainers. Further, meets regularly with student employees and conducts evaluations. Commit and support a culture that embraces and encourages an environment dedicated to student success.   ATTRIBUTES OF THE SUCCESSFUL CANDIDATE: Ability to supervise and guide with clarity the student staff to execute the vision and culture for the Fitness Operation. Understand and prioritize tasks with a sense of urgency. Or something along those lines knowing there will be tasks and deadlines, etc. Driven to enhance the user experience in the fitness area by observing and discerning patterns and behaviors of participants. Is familiar with best and innovative fitness and wellness practices. The successful candidate will be part of the ideation process for programs. When addressed with concerns or questions related to fitness operations, will work to find creative solutions while considering current conditions and policies. Build/ establish healthy and professional relationships with peers across the department. Stay curious and eager to learn. ABOUT THE DIVISION OF STUDENT AFFAIRS PRIORITIES: Three priorities guide our work in the Division of Student Aﬀairs. Foremost, we maintain a commitment to quality which is rooted in the belief that LSU students deserve our best eﬀort. Every interaction we have with students should communicate care, relevance, polish, and attention to detail. We work to ensure every space, place, and staﬀ-to-student interaction communicates a sense of home to students. Finally, we design programs, services, events, and experiences with everyone in mind.   RESPONSIBILITIES EXPLAINED: Direct Student Support (40%) Guide and direct student members as well as student staff on the proper usage of fitness equipment. Translate department efforts, initiatives, and goals to students through interactions at programs, services, events, and experiences. Serve as the liaison between (fitness staff) students and the leadership in the unit. Responsible for developing trainings that ensure Fitness student employees are knowledgeable about UREC policy and procedures related to ensuring a safe environment in all our fitness spaces.  Quality Control (25%)  Ensures every aspect of [programmatic/administrative/financial/facility/etc] outputs including administrative tasks, implementation, and overall design exudes a high degree of quality.Embraces and executes a belief for continuous improvement and applies to elevate the level of all services, events, programs, and experiences in department.   Program Support (20%) Responsible for operations of fitness programs, services, events, and/or experiences. Provides input on overall expenditures, experiences and services within fitness. Oversees the daily execution of the personal training program.   Administrative Support (10%)  Support the day-to-day fitness operations through administrative management while working with UREC business administration to ensure policies are being followed and updated when necessary. Provides feedback regarding programs and experiences by personally using UREC. Contributes to the work environment by developing and maintaining positive relationships that support a culture of teamwork and cooperation.  Other Duties as Assigned (5%)  Other duties as assigned by the Executive Director, Associate Director of Programs or Assistant Director of Fitness. This includes but is not limited to efforts that support broad division/institution efforts including at least 40 hours per year spent helping divisional initiatives such as Move-In Day, Welcome Week, Family Weekend, Career Expo, Disability Services Finals Testing, other special projects etc.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree in Health Promotion/Education, Nutrition, Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or related field Related experience LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s Degree in Health Promotion/Education, Nutrition, Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Higher Education, Business, Public Administration, or related field 2 years professional work experience in collegiate recreation, fitness facility, and or corporate fitness   DESIRED CERTIFICATIONS/LICENSES: National Commission for Certifying Agencies (NCCA) accredited personal training certification. Examples are but not limited to; Academy of Applied Personal Training (AAPTE), American College of Sports Medicine (ACSM), American Council on Exercise (ACE), and/or International Fitness Professionals Association (IFPA)   SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS: Ability and willingness to work evening and weekend hours. We support, when appropriate, the ability to have a flexible work schedule.  Due to the position’s physical requirements, a pre-employment physical examination will be required per FASOP: HR-04.   As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Applications will be accepted online on the LSU Careers website. The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and continue to accept applications and nominations until the position is filled. However, to assure the fullest consideration, candidates are encouraged to submit completed applications by August 28, 2026. Requested application materials include a letter of interest; curriculum vitae or resume; and the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Irma Nieves-Torres at irmant@lsu.edu or 225-578-1154.     Skills Needed: Adaptability, Collaboration, Communication, Customer Service, Data Analysis, Problem Solving, Project Management, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 15, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0112-Thomas-D-Boyd-Hall/Coordinator---Registrar_R00118907": {
      "title": "Coordinator - Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Coordinator - Registrar     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - EM - CS - Registrar - Ops - CCM - Operations (Capri Marie Mandella Alvarez (00004750))     Work Location: 0112 Thomas D. Boyd Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The Coordinator in the Curricula & Course Management Division is responsible for coordinating the course section build for sections with special requirements. The Coordinator will also manage student and faculty accommodations, publish and maintain the \"Building a Course Offering\" training guide, and monitor faculty assignments. Must have an extensive knowledge of university policies, procedures, and practices and be able to respond to a myriad of questions, problems, and situations dealing with curricular and course scheduling issues. Also, this person will assist with the planning of the course offerings each semester as well as assisting individuals campus-wide with Workday Student and 25Live. Job Responsibilities Responsible for the scheduling of 200+ general purpose classrooms for general meetings, organizational meetings, final examinations, orientation programs, Supplemental Instruction Leader session, Leisure Courses, Biology Boot Camps, 4H, ACT Testing, School of Banking, etc. For all outside agencies, must work with the Department of Facility Services to complete a campus use agreement and coordinate a reservation. Responsible for all University-approved organizations' classroom reservations. Serves as primary room scheduler for events held on campus. (20%) Responsible for the scheduling of 200+ general purpose classrooms for institutional space. Utilizes scheduling software to assign classes to classrooms while maximizing utilization. Coordinates room assignments for faculty who teach courses back-to-back. Serves as primary room scheduler for classroom instruction. (20%) Responsible for manually assigning classes and events based on special requirements. Special requirements include but are not limited to the following: disabled faculty and student needs; special needs of departments, individual faculty members, or organizations; demands for large (80-capacity and above) classrooms; and working with academic departments on specific course section needs. (15%) Responsible for publishing and maintaining the “Building a Course Offering” training guide. Responsible for updating publication as processes/software changes. Assists the campus community on the University's student information system and associated software and applications. (10%) Responsible for ensuring that faculty are accurately assigned to teach all courses. This process must be completed before the 14th class day each semester. All grades (midterm/interim and final) are submitted by the faculty via Moodle/Workday Student. Faculty assignments must be complete and accurate to ensure that faculty members have access to their grade sheets. Works directly with the Office of Budget and Planning to ensure faculty assignment data is available for the production of reports required by the Board of Regents and to ensure that proper compensation is made to the teaching faculty. (10%) Responsible for training the campus community on the use of Workday Student, including, but not limited to, faculty assignments and section creation. Also assists with training the campus community on room scheduling/reservation software. This will be a continuous process that requires outreach and strong interpersonal communication skills. (10%) In coordination with the Assistant Registrar, assists with special projects related to the Workday Student implementation, including faculty assignment reports, eligibility rules for courses, academic requirements for degree programs, etc. Plays a pivotal role in the creation, implementation, and rollout of the Extend App, which will allow on-campus departments to make course section changes in Workday Student. (10%) Supervises and trains student assistants, coordinates their schedules, assigns and reviews their work, and reviews time sheets. Other related duties as assigned by supervisor. (5%) Additional Requirements FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related matter, they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Ability to learn and quickly adapt to new software environments as introduced.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Capri Alvarez at capri@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 15, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
