    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101A-Eunice-Library/Health-Science-Academic-Advisor_R00118769": {
      "title": "Health Science Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Health Science Academic Advisor     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUE AA - Library & SSS - Student Success Center (Amy Lemaire (00053242))     Work Location: 0101A Eunice Library     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: The Health Sciences Academic Advisor reports to the Assistant Director of Advising and is chiefly responsible for providing guidance and support for all students majoring in pre-allied health programs at Louisiana State University at Eunice. The purpose of this position is to support these students holistically by ensuring that best practices in student advising, career and academic coaching are followed, and working as a part of a supportive team in the Integrated Learning Center. Job Responsibilities: 70% Advising - Service pre-allied health majors in the following ways: assist students in choosing the appropriate program and/or major and scheduling of courses; recommend courses of action for students seeking academic guidance; maintain student advising records; and uphold the policies and procedures of the University as related to advisory duties.  25% COACHING - Service these students in the following ways: assist in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; work with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivate students to take ownership of their academic success; assist students with preparations for effective job searching including feedback on resumes and strategizing for a successful job interview.  5% Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree 2 years' experience in admissions, advising, retention, and/or teaching in higher education is preferred. Salary: $30,000.00-$40,000.00     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Academic Advisor     Skills Needed: Academic Advising, Active Listening, Communication, Critical Thinking, Curriculum Coordination, Data Entry, Detail-Oriented, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 14, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!    Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUE is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSUE Human Resources Management Office at 337-550-1222 or emailed at hr@lsue.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-Red-River-Admin-Building-New/Research-Associate-Specialist_R00116785": {
      "title": "Research Associate Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate Specialist     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG PL3 - Northwest - Red River Research Station (William F Waltman (00013528))     Work Location: 0101 Red River Admin. Building-New     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: Work Location: Red River Research Station, Bossier City, La. 71112  Position Description : The LSU AgCenter is seeking a Research Associate to support applied research and extension programming at the Red River Research Station (Bossier City, LA). This position will be divided approximately equally between row crop cultivar testing and general research station operations and support.  In the area of row crop cultivar testing, the successful candidate will assist in planning, establishing, and managing row crop variety trials. Responsibilities include preparing research plots through layout and field mapping, collecting and maintaining accurate research data, and performing basic statistical analysis to assist with interpretation of results. The position also supports research activities conducted in field, greenhouse, and laboratory settings and assists with harvest operations, data summaries, and reporting.  In support of research station operations and extension activities, the individual will collect and record daily weather station data and assist with general field operations such as planting, spraying, and harvesting both row crops and specialty plots, including homesteader vegetable gardens. The role includes mixing and applying agricultural chemicals in accordance with label requirements, maintaining station grounds through mowing and general upkeep, and supporting operations at the Pecan Research Station and associated facilities. The employee will also assist with the preparation and execution of field days, demonstrations, and other outreach events.  The research associate will work as part of the station farm crew under the supervision of the farm manager and is expected to prioritize and complete assigned tasks efficiently while adapting to changing needs and seasonal demands. This position will support a wide range of research, extension, and operational needs.  This position requires a strong work ethic, attention to detail, and the ability to work effectively in field environments under varying conditions.  Housing is available if the successful candidate is offered the position. Qualification Requirements : Candidates should have a bachelor's degree in agriculture, plant science, biology or a related field. A working knowledge of agricultural systems is required. Applicants must be willing and able to perform physical work outdoors. Candidate with an MS degree is desired.  Applicants with a degree in another agricultural or basic science field will be considered qualifying provided they possess significant work experience in agricultural systems.  LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications. If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (La RS 42:36).  Salary and Benefits : Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process.  Application Deadline: August 28, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified.  Application Procedure: Apply online at https://lsu.wdl.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters on line, they may be sent directly to:  Dr. Ronald Strahan  Northwest Regional Director  LSU AgCenter  262 Research Station Drive  Bossier City LA 71112  Phone : 318-741-7430  E-mail: rstrahan@agcenter.lsu.edu   Website: www.lsuagcenter.com   The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and pr vides equal opportunities in programs and employment.      Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Research Associate Specialist     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0111-Madison-B-Sturgis-New-Agronomy-Bldg/Research-Associate-Specialist_R00118742": {
      "title": "Research Associate Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate Specialist     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG PL1 - SPESS - Plant Environmental and Soil Sciences (Niranjan Baisakh (00005139))     Work Location: 0111 Madison B. Sturgis (New Agronomy Bldg)     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: (This is a grant-funded, non-tenure track position for one year.  Funding must be available for any continuation of appointment. Work Location:   School of Plant, Environmental, and Soil Sciences, Louisiana State University Agricultural Center, Baton Rouge, Louisiana Position Description: The Sugarcane Genetics Laboratory of the School of Plant, Environmental, and Soil Sciences is seeking a Research Associate (RA) to conduct computational genetic studies to improve desirable agronomic traits in sugarcane. The researcher will use contemporary bioinformatics and quantitative genetics tools to facilitate genomics-assisted breeding in sugarcane. The incumbent will be expected to work in the greenhouse and field setting, as needed . Qualification Requirements: A B.S. or M.S. degree in Plant Breeding, Genetics, or related field. Candidates experienced with handling high-throughput sequence, genotypic and phenotypic datasets using Python and/or R will be preferred. Applicants must be motivated to work independently as well as in a team environment. Good communication skills are a requirement. LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications.  If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (La RS 42:36). Salary and Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with education and experience.  The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline: September 1, 2026 or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Dr. Niranjan Baisakh School of Plant, Environmental and Soil Sciences LSU AgCenter 104 Madison B Sturgis Hall, Baton Rouge, LA 70803 Phone : 225-578-1300 Fax : 225-578-1403 E-mail: nbaisakh@agcenter.lsu.edu   Website: www.lsuagcenter.com The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions:     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/3261-Patrick-F-Taylor-Hall/Adjunct-Instructor---Mechanical-Engineering_R00118736-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Adjunct Instructor - Mechanical Engineering     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Engineering - School of Mechanical and Industrial Engineering (Dimitris E Nikitopoulos (00006339))     Work Location: 3261 Patrick F. Taylor Hall     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Teach a Mechanical Engineering course as assigned by the ME UG Program Co-Director - Academic Affairs & Curriculum and/or MIE Department Chair. Job Responsibilities: 100% Teach Mechanical Engineering courses (Technical Electives or Core). Minimum qualifications: Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field; 5 years of industry experience     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions regarding pay or the status of your application please reach out to Dr. Dimitris Nikitopoulos at medimi@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): February 10, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-Life-Sciences-Building/Instructor_R00118737": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM Science - BioS - Molecular Biology - Gene Expression (David Donze (00009160))     Work Location: 0101 Life Sciences Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: This individual will be responsible for development of a hybrid online/in person Introductory Biology laboratory course (BIOL 1212) and a completely online Human Physiology course (BIOL 2160) and teaching the BIOL 2160 course during the 2026/27 AY. After the 2026/27 AY, this individual will teach the online BIOL 2160 course and up to two Introductory Biology Program courses each semester or other courses as needed. This individual will provide service in support of the Introductory Biology Program or Department of Biological Sciences as needed. Duties: 50% Teach online BIOL 2160 during one term each semester and up to two Introductory Biology Program courses each semester. 35% Develop an online Human Physiology course (BIOL 2160) and a hybrid online/in person laboratory course (BIOL 1212) during the initial year of appointment. 10% Provide service in support of the Introductory Biology Program and Department of Biological Sciences as needed. This may include providing help with required program assessment each semester or developing additional online courses. 5% Additional duties as deemed necessary by the Associate Chair of Introductory Biology, Associate Chair of Undergraduate Studies, or the Department Chair to fit the changing needs of a growing department. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Microbiology or related field. Three years experience with standard laboratory techniques used in biology laboratories. Experience teaching at the college level. This can include experience as a graduate teaching assistant. Experience teaching online courses. Strong training in biology, experience with multimedia or other modern instructional technology or both; familiarity with practices of active learning and inquiry-based learning. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Microbiology or related field with experience with standard laboratory techniques used in biology laboratories. Experience teaching at the college level. This can include experience as a graduate teaching assistant. Experience teaching online courses. Strong training in biology, experience with multimedia or other modern instructional technology or both; familiarity with practices of active learning and inquiry-based learning.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please submit a current cv and contact information of 3 references. An official transcript showing highest degree obtained will be needed prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the position, please contact Lori Bond at lbond3@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 11, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0201-Fred-C-Frey-Computing-Services-Building/Enterprise-Resource-Planning--ERP--Analyst-1--2--or-3--Financial-Aid_R00116792-1": {
      "title": "Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) Analyst 1, 2, or 3- Financial Aid",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) Analyst 1, 2, or 3- Financial Aid     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM FA - ITS - DA - SS - Student Financial and Administrative (Crystal Murphy (00051640))     Work Location: 0201 Fred C. Frey Computing Services Building     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The purpose of the ERP Analyst is to work with end users, product owners, developers and business stakeholders to elicit, analyze, communicate, and validate business, functional or reporting requirements, and business processes. Prepares and/or maintains detailed documentation pertaining to configurations, systems operations, and requirements.  Achieves and maintains subject matter expertise relevant to the functional areas of Financial Aid, included but not limited to, Attendance Plans, ISIR processing, Cost of Attendance, Packaging, Award Disbursement, etc within Workday Student. Works with product teams and product managers to implement changes and enhancements to applications. An ERP Analyst 2 will be required to perform additional duties with more autonomy and less required supervision and consultation with superiors.  Examples include being assigned as lead analyst on various projects, enhancement initiatives, and software implementations and representing the department with software vendors. An ERP Analyst 2 will also be expected to provide more consulting services to business users, leveraging advanced critical thinking skills. An ERP Analyst 3 will be required to perform additional duties with more autonomy and less required supervision and consultation with superiors than an ERP Analyst 2.  Will be expected to be experts in their respective functional areas and provide consulting services to business users with minimal to no management direct oversight. Additional examples include serving as technical lead on various projects, creating and maintaining module roadmaps and assuming responsibility that priorities are established and executed, becoming an expert on Workday Reporting and learning SAS Enterprise Guide for advanced reporting needs, assuming responsibility of manual and automated testing efforts for assigned functional areas, and mentoring junior analysts in Workday business process, reporting, and security configuration.  Job Responsibilities: ERP Analyst 1- Support:   Knowledge of business processes and technologies for assigned product line.  Works with product owners, product teams, and other ITS teams to troubleshoot, analyze, gather requirements, and propose resolutions. Communicates potential impact of solutions.  Executes solutions.  Tests independently and in collaboration with product owners. (30%) Consulting/Enhancing: Works with product owners, product teams, product managers, and vendors to understand business needs and vendor product roadmaps.  Documents requirements into functional and technical specifications using a variety of business analytic techniques.  Recommends solutions to product owners. Works with product team to implement and test enhancements based on University product roadmap priorities.  Coordinates with other ITS teams to implement solutions and to communicate solutions to appropriate parties. (25%) Reporting: Works with product team and product owners to define and document reporting needs and creates reports within applications and/or external reporting systems.  Coordinates with other ITS teams to implement solutions and to communicate solutions to appropriate parties. (20%) Testing: Uses automated testing tool when available  Maintains and enhances testing scripts, executes on schedule, troubleshoots results, and works with product line to recommend enhancements to business processes. (15%) Other duties as assigned. (10%) ERP Analyst 2- Support:   Knowledge of business processes and technologies for assigned product line.  Works with product owners, product teams, and other ITS teams to troubleshoot, analyze, gather requirements, and propose resolutions. Communicates potential impact of solutions.  Executes solutions.  Tests independently and in collaboration with product owners. Will be expected to work autonomously with other ITS teams, requiring less input and advisement from supervisor. (30%) Consulting/Enhancing: Works with product owners, product teams, product managers, and vendors to understand business needs and vendor product roadmaps.  Documents requirements into functional and technical specifications using a variety of business analytic techniques.  Recommends solutions to product owners. Works with product team to implement and test enhancements based on University product roadmap priorities.  Coordinates with other ITS teams to implement solutions and to communicate solutions to appropriate parties. Will be expected to manage some enhancements from beginning to end with less need for supervisor consultation. Will be assigned as primary departmental representative on software solution implementations. (30%) Reporting: Works with product team and product owners to define and document reporting needs and creates reports within applications and/or external reporting systems.  Coordinates with other ITS teams to implement solutions and to communicate solutions to appropriate parties. Will be responsible for seeking out opportunities to enhance business processes or solve problems through reporting solutions, thus acquiring an advanced report-developing skill set. (15%) Testing: Uses automated testing tool when available  Maintains and enhances testing scripts, executes on schedule, troubleshoots results, and works with product line to recommend enhancements to business processes.  Will be responsible for working directly with software vendor of testing tool to solve problems and convey needs of the department. (15%) Other duties as assigned. (10%) ERP Analyst 3- Support:  Maintain expert knowledge of business processes and technologies for assigned product line modules.  Works with product owners, product teams, and other ITS teams to troubleshoot, analyze, gather requirements, and propose resolutions. Communicates potential impact of solutions.  Executes solutions.  Tests independently and in collaboration with product owners. Will be expected to work autonomously with other ITS teams, often requiring little to no advisement from supervisor. (30%) Consulting/Enhancing: Works with product owners, product teams, product managers, and vendors to understand business needs and vendor product roadmaps.  Documents requirements into functional and technical specifications using a variety of business analytic techniques.  Recommends solutions to product owners. Creates and maintains module roadmaps and ensures that priorities are established and executed. Will be expected to manage some enhancements from beginning to end with little to no supervisor consultation. Will be assigned as technical lead on software solution implementations. (25%) Reporting: Works with product team and product owners to define and document reporting needs, recommends reporting solutions that solve business problems and enhance efficiencies, and creates reports within applications and/or external reporting systems.  Must achieve expert level of knowledge on Workday reporting.  Utilizes other reporting tools such as SAS Enterprise guide for advanced, multi-source reporting. Will be responsible for seeking out opportunities to enhance business processes or solve problems through reporting solutions, thus acquiring an advanced report-developing skill set. (25%) Testing: Responsible for overseeing manual and automated use cases for assigned functional areas.  Maintains and enhances testing scripts, executes on schedule, troubleshoots results, and works with product line to recommend enhancements to business processes.  Will be responsible for working directly with software vendor of testing tool to solve problems and convey needs of the department. (10%) Other duties as assigned. (10%) Minimum Qualifications: ERP Analyst 1- Bachelor's degree in a technology or busiess related field. 1 year of experience. ERP Analyst 2- Bachelor's degree in a technology or business related field. 2 years of experience. ERP Analyst 3- Bachelor's degree in a a technology or business related field. 3 years of experience. +LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: ERP Analyst 1- Master's Degree in computer science, information systems, engineering, or related.  1 year knowledge of financial aid processes, experience supporting student information systems (SIS), or ERP platforms in a higher education environment. ERP Analyst 2- Master's Degree in computer science, information systems, engineering, or related.  3+ years knowledge of financial aid processes, experience supporting student information systems (SIS), or ERP platforms in a higher education environment. ERP Analyst 3- Master's Degree in computer science, information systems, engineering, or related.  5+ years knowledge of financial aid processes, experience supporting student information systems (SIS), or ERP platforms in a higher education environment. Additional Information: The ERP Analyst position is a hybrid position and requires the employee to be continuously available and maintain an acceptable, appropriate level of access to LSU infrastructure/systems. It is the employee’s responsibility to sustain a proper connection to LSU that allows the ERP Analyst to perform work-related duties when working remotely.  As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire. Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Mary Bordelon at mbordelon@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 6, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0124-William-P-Johnston-Hall---Office/Disability-Services-Lead-Access-Coordinator_R00118701": {
      "title": "Disability Services Lead Access Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Disability Services Lead Access Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - H&WB - DS - Advising (Taylor Kechelle Ballom (00044514))     Work Location: 0124 William P. Johnston Hall - Office     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Reporting to the Assistant Director for Access, the Lead Access Coordinator provides case management guidance to the Access Coordinator team while overseeing services for specialized student populations. This position is also a shared service position for LSU Online, for which the Lead Access Coordinator will maintain an LSU Online caseload and serve as the staff liaison. This position assesses disability documentation, determines appropriate accommodations, coordinates special programs, and collaborates with campus partners to ensure consistent, high-quality disability services and student support.   GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES FOR THIS POSITION INCLUDE   Serve as the primary case manager and liaison for shared services between LSU Online and Disability Services. Serve as case manager for designated specialized student populations. Advise students with disabilities regarding their rights and responsibilities under the ADA, Section 504, and any related university policies and/or procedures. Analyze and interpret disability related documentation to determine eligibility for services and accommodations for students with disabilities.   Assist in the development, implementation, and assessment of appropriate academic support services and accommodations under ADA, Section 504, and any related university policies and/or procedures. OPPORTUNITIES FOR LEADERSHIP    Enhance Support for LSU Online The number of students enrolled in LSU Online registered with Disability Services has grown exponentially in the past few years. As the primary case manager for the shared services between Disability Services and LSU Online, the Lead Access Coordinator will need to quickly determine what is working well and where improvements can be made in the partnership in serving these online students.  Strengthen Support for Specialized Student Populations The Lead Access Coordinator has an opportunity to advance support for specialized student populations by strengthening collaborative partnerships, enhancing accommodation practices, and identifying innovative strategies that improve access and student success across specialized programs including the Academic Center for Student Athletes, LSU Eunice (LSUE) Bridge Program, Pre-Scholars (PSA), Student Support Services for Disabilities (SSS-D), and Veterinary Medicine.   Enhance Customer Service through Individual Student Connections Each individual interaction between a student and a staff member is an opportunity to impact an individual student. By championing a culture of exceptional customer service, the Access Coordinator can improve student satisfaction, solidifying relationships with students and campus partners, and contribute to increased student engagement, persistence, and overall success. ATTRIBUTES OF THE SUCCESSFUL CANDIDATE   Demonstrates a knowledge of disability-related issues, especially the provision of accommodations, and how various disabilities contribute to an educational setting.  Committed to advocating for students and supporting institutional and divisional priorities and initiatives, specifically a commitment to quality, communicating a sense of home, and designing programs, services, events, and experiences with everyone in mind. Does not start with “no” when addressing student concerns or requests, but instead works to find innovative ways to solve problems and meet the needs of students with disabilities.  Possesses the ability to navigate complex systems and provide ideas on how to mitigate challenges students may face within these structures. Collaborates well with others across campus to solve problems and mitigate barriers that prevent students with disabilities from realizing their educational goals. Willingness to admit to and learn from mistakes and help others through mistakes they make in a way that fosters positive personal and team growth. Can communicate with clarity, direction, and conviction in person, in written communication, and in virtual spaces.   ABOUT THE DIVISION OF STUDENT AFFAIRS PRIORITIES    Three priorities guide our work in the Division of Student Affairs. Foremost, we maintain a commitment to quality which is rooted in the belief that LSU students deserve our best effort. Every interaction we have with students should communicate care, relevance, polish, and attention to detail. We work to ensure every space, place, and staff-to-student interaction communicates a sense of home to students. Finally, we design programs, services, events, and experiences with everyone in mind .  RESPONSIBILITIES   Direct Student Support - 40% Serve as the primary case manager and liaison for shared services between LSU Online and Disability Services. Coordinate business and student service functions across both departments to ensure seamless, consistent, and accessible support for LSU Online students with disabilities. Manage student accommodation cases from initial request through implementation, including reviewing documentation, conducting intake meetings, determining appropriate accommodations, and coordinating access needs with students, faculty, and staff.   Specialized Student Populations - 40% Serve as case manager for designated specialized student populations requiring advanced knowledge of disability accommodations, university processes, and collaborative support. Coordinate accommodations and auxiliary services for populations including, but not limited to, the Academic Center for Student Athletes, LSU Eunice (LSUE) Bridge Program, Pre-Scholars (PSA), Student Support Services for Disabilities (SSS-D), and Veterinary Medicine. Collaborate with academic and campus partners to facilitate access across special programs.   Program Support - 15% Lead programming efforts for specialized student populations, including neurodivergent initiatives and designated neurodivergent spaces. Provide consultation on case management and overall professional development for Access Coordinators, with support from the Assistant Director for Access. Collaborate with departmental staff and campus partners to develop educational programs, workshops, and outreach opportunities. Maintain knowledge of accommodations and best practices for students who are Deaf/Hard of Hearing and Blind/Visually Impaired, and provide consultation and support in the absence of specialized case managers.   Other Duties as Assigned - 5% This includes, but is not limited to, efforts that support broad divisional and institutional goals, such as at least 40 hours per year spent supporting divisional initiatives, including Move-in Day, Welcome Week, Family Weekend, and Career Expo.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS   Master’s degree in a related field from an accredited institution OR Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 2 years of related experience. Experience providing services to individuals in a high pace environment. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description.   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Rehabilitation Counseling, Social Work, Counseling, or directly related field.  Experience working in higher education. Experience working with adolescents and/or adults with disabilities.  Experience reading and interpreting disability related documentation for students.   SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS    Ability and willingness to work some evening and weekend hours.   This position and/or position's responsibilities require work directly with minors. Finger printing and National Sex Offender Registry check required per FASOP HR-04.  As with all LSU employees, this position, due to its title and/or responsibilities, has an obligation to assist students in obtaining necessary services. Should a student appear to need or seek assistance with emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related issues, they should be referred to the appropriate service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee, outside of the rights contained in FERPA, ADA, and Section 504, should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.    APPLICATIONS    Applications will be accepted online on the LSU Careers website. Please direct all nominations and inquiries for the position to Taylor Ballom at 225-578-4913. The department will begin reviewing applications immediately and continue to accept applications and nominations until the position is filled. However, in order to assure the fullest consideration, candidates are encouraged to have complete applications submitted by August 28, 2026 .  Requested application materials include a letter of interest; curriculum vitae or resume; and the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications.  An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Requested application materials include a letter of interest; curriculum vitae or resume; and the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Taylor Ballom at 225-578-4913.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 13, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 11, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0404-Life-Sciences-Building/Postdoctoral-Researcher_R00118620": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Postdoctoral Researcher     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG PL1 - DE - Entomology (Michael J Stout (00006216))     Work Location: 0404 Life Sciences Building     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: (This is a grant-funded, non-tenure track position through 09/30/2027. Funding must be available for any continuation of appointment.) Work Location: Department of Entomology, Baton Rouge, LA 70803 Position Description: The individual will be expected to perform a variety of duties as an post-doctoral associate in the Department of Entomology in coordination with the USDA-ARS Honey Bee Breeding, Genetics and Physiology Research Laboratory (HBBGPRL).  These duties will include conducting research related to honey bee cell culture and viruses, including developing pipelines for primary cell culture testing and viral clones; assisting with outreach and extension; sampling honey bee colonies; and collecting and computerizing research data. Additional duties will be concordant with expertise and may include conducting basic and advanced science laboratory techniques, such as established molecular and organismal biology methods (e.g. DNA and RNA extractions, ecotoxicology assays), microscopy, and managing research honey bee colonies. The individual will be expected to design experiments in relation to project objectives and be able to troubleshoot and refine methodologies as appropriate. Current projects would require the successful applicant to coordinate work as part of a team of extension technicians, field technicians, and researchers at the USDA-ARS HBBGPRL, beekeepers, and related units in joint tasks when deemed necessary. Qualification Requirements:   A minimum of a PhD in the entomology, biology, microbiology and immunology, virology, genetics or related fields and prior postdoctoral research experience. If the candidate possesses sufficient relevant experience with honey bees, then the field of degree could be outside of those listed. Preference will be given to applicants with prior experience working with honey bees in laboratory and field settings and the beekeeping community, and specifically with regard to honey bee cell culturing and virology.  Preference will also be given to candidates with additional training in basic sciences like molecular biology, entomology, microscopy, and/or field work.  Salary and Benefits: Salary will be commensurate with education and experience.  The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System.  Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available: Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline: August 28, 2026 or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Michael Stout Entomology LSU AgCenter 404 Life Sciences Building Phone :225-578-1634 E-mail: mstout@agcenter.lsu.edu   Website: www.lsuagcenter.com The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions:     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1002U-Energy-Coast-and-Environment-Building/Coordinator_R00118617": {
      "title": "Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM CCE - Oceanography and Coastal Sciences (Kanchan Maiti (00007816))     Work Location: 1002U Energy, Coast, and Environment Building     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: This Coordinator position will provide administrative support to faculty and staff in the Department of Oceanography & Coastal Sciences. This position will be responsible for creating travel and expense reports, maintaining supplies, assisting with functions and events in the college and other related duties. Most importantly, this position is expected to provide excellent customer service to faculty, staff, students and visitors to the department by assisting with assigned duties and related issues that arise. Job Responsibilities: 40% Manage the travel function for the Department of Oceanography & Coastal Sciences to include processing and tracking approvals and reimbursements, providing assistance and training for staff and students on guidelines and procedures, and assisting visitors to the department with accommodations and reimbursements. Also, provide assistance for class field trips, including all required university approvals, reservations, etc. 30% Provide administrative support for faculty, research staff and students by assisting with LaCarte purchases when needed and reconciling charges. Coordinator will monitor charges for the department to ensure expense reports are processed timely and work with employees to resolve issues that arise. 10% Orders/maintains departmental office supplies, manages the mail room and copier, providing assistance when needed. 10% Assist with functions for the college and academic programs, such as orientation, receptions, student events, commencement, etc. 5% Serve as backup in the absence of other coordinators in the department as well as within the College. 5% Other duties as needed Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree with administrative experience. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply--a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: At least 2 years of administrative experience Competencies: Demonstrated effective customer service skills. Proficient Ability to prioritize, organize and perform multiple assignments. Proficient Ability to effectively problem solve and identify appropriate options for resolving issues. Proficient Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff and students. Proficient     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references including name, title, phone number and email address. A copy of your transcript (s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, official transcripts are required prior to hire (if applicable). If your degree was earned outside the US, a credential evaluation will be required. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check and credit check. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Sharon Butler at sbutler@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Communication, Compliance Awareness, Customer Service, Data Entry, Detail-Oriented, Expense Reconciliations, Purchasing, Travel Itineraries     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 8, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1134-Ruffin-G-Pleasant-Hall/Scholarship-Counselor_R00118612": {
      "title": "Scholarship Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Scholarship Counselor     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - EM - Rec - FAS - Scholarships - Award Management (Madison Grace Lingo (00066964) (Private))     Work Location: 1134 Ruffin G. Pleasant Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The scholarship counselor position within Louisiana State University’s Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships will play a key collaborative role in advancing the University and meeting the student enrollment objectives.  The individual, with general oversight from the Assistant Director, will be responsible for maintaining scholarship communication with current and prospective students and families.      Customer Service for Scholarships Unit (30%) Responsible for primary customer service assistance to prospective and continuing students, parents and departmental contacts. This includes resolving problems and providing support associated with the administration of scholarship programs via phone, email or in person interactions. Represents the office as assigned and presents scholarship and financial aid information at orientation sessions or other presentation opportunities for student and parent groups. Acts as liaison between our office and faculty/staff, students and the public to provide information and resources regarding scholarship activities and programs. Must have strong communication and interpersonal skills. Assists with departmental communication to colleges regarding scholarship aid packages and supporting departments in their scholarship awarding process.  Act as the primary liaison for the Enrollment Management call center as it relates to scholarship matters. Provides ongoing training to call center students for the scholarships unit. Scholarship Counseling (30%) Counsels and advises prospective and enrolled students in all matters pertaining to university, state, federal and donor scholarship programs. The employee must be accurate in describing scholarship policies, criteria and procedures. Must be responsive to students’ concerns and needs by providing excellent customer service. Scholarships Operations: (30%) Supports colleges awarding departmental scholarships which includes the responsibility of making decisions in releasing disbursement to students. Responsible for the initial review of all documents submitted by departments for the purpose of establishing scholarship programs and program rules in the SAE system. Coordinates with Sponsored program accounting, LSU Foundation and Bursar operations to establish new scholarships for university administration.  Assists with the administration of University scholarships including departmental, Foundation, and academic awards. Reviews, approves, and enters award information for various scholarships to individual student records in the appropriate database. Supports selection and processing of awards administered by Financial aid and Scholarships. Maintains all files for scholarships programs and assures audit efficiency.  Maintains accuracy of the Scholarships unit policy and procedures manual. Responsible for processing reports and the maintenance of accuracy in all records. Manages daily operations for assigned scholarships programs. Assist with institutional aid math process for the A&M campus.  This includes matching students with institutional scholarships to foundation scholarships, as well as working with all departments on campus to offer a centralized swap process.    Special projects as assigned (10%) Including, but not limited to assigned committees and outreach projects.  Represent LSU and the Office of Enrollment Management at professional functions and recruiting events.  Represents LSU and EMSS at orientation events.   Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in student services setting preferably in higher education.  Bachelor’s degree in Public Relations, Communications, Marketing, or Business-related field. Our ideal candidate possesses the following qualities: Strong team orientation, effective interpersonal skills, and superior written and verbal communication skills with demonstrated ability to build and steward relationships Demonstrated commitment to data-driven decision-making, including effective analytical skills and proven results in achieving objectives and goals. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail and accuracy. Proficient computer skills, particularly word processing, spreadsheets, and database management. Ability to complete multiple assignments within provided time constraints with minimal supervision. Self-starter who works well independently, but who also thrives in a team environment, sharing ideas and working collaboratively.   Special Qualifications: As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality.       Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: The location of this position is LSU-BR and is not eligible for remote work. To be considered, qualified candidates will submit a complete application which includes a cover letter explaining their specific interest in the position and how their skills and experiences prepare them for success in this role, a resume, and three professional references. Please provide resume and transcripts, if applicable. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Madison Lingo at Madison.Lingo@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Communication, Confidentiality, Critical Thinking, Customer-Focused, Decision Making, Policy Knowledge, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 10, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Innovation-Park-Bldg-8000/SBDC-Accounting-Coordinator_R00118610": {
      "title": "SBDC Accounting Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: SBDC Accounting Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM ORED - Small Business Development Center (Bryan L. Greenwood (00009600))     Work Location: Innovation Park Bldg 8000     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: The Louisiana Small Business Development Center Network (LSBDC) is the largest technical assistance provider to small businesses in Louisiana. The position will assist with the financial oversight of the LSBDC network and perform the day-to-day accounting transactions required of all LSBDC Network contracts and grants. Duties include but are not limited to budget preparation and review, processing monthly invoices, reconciling financial reports, maintaining supporting documentation, and processing journal entries and budget transfers. Job Responsibilities : Financial Administration - This position will assist with the financial oversight of the LSBDC Network and perform the day-to-day accounting transactions required for all the LSBDC contracts and grants. Duties include but are not limited to budget preparation, budget review, processing monthly invoices from subcontractors, reconciling financial reports to funding agencies, maintaining supporting documentation, and assisting with audits and financial reviews. Assist with preparing the LSBDC Network’s budget and program narrative in response to the annual SBA SBDC NOFO. Assist with the coordination of the annual sub-award agreements with sub-recipients. Monitors the LSBDC Network and sub-awards budget vs. actual and remaining balance activities. Assist with preparing the LSBDC Network’s quarterly financial and programmatic narrative reports. Assist with the development, maintenance, and implementation of the LSBDC Network financial and programmatic policies and procedures. Will coordinate with LSU Office of Sponsored Programs, Sponsored Program Accounting, and Procurement Services as required. (45%) Workday / Accounting Transactions - Maintains knowledge of the LSU Workday system, GeauxGrants, and other systems related to the financial activities of the LSBDC Network’s contracts and grants. Familiar with and follow all LSU financial policies and procedures. Reviews fiscal documents, balances and reconciles subsidiary accounting records, and collects data for budget projections and/or requests for release of funds. Assembles, verifies, and corrects data as needed. Prepares non-routine fiscal reports. Processes journal entries and online budget transfers and journal vouchers as necessary. Assist with P-card purchases and approvals, P-card reconciliation, purchase requisitions, and direct pay requests. Assists with travel requests from LSBDC Lead Center staff to ensure travel costs are within the budget and all prior approvals have been obtained from SBA. Compiles financial, accounting, or auditing reports on matters such as cash receipts, expenditures, accounts payable and receivable, and payroll. (45%) Miscellaneous Duties - Assists with other LSBDC Network projects as required. Attends national, regional, and state meetings and trainings as required. Develop and provide specific information, reports, and/or special services as requested or required by the SBA/SBDC Administrators, the SBA Business Development Specialist, and the LSBDC State Director. Support area, state, and federal research projects concerning small businesses and disseminate results to the community. Other duties as assigned. (10%) Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply--a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications : Master's degree in accounting or MBA. 1-5 years of accounting, finance, or business. Understanding of University policies and procedures.  Knowledge of LSU Workday System. Physical Demands: Physical ability and eye-hand coordination necessary to use a computer terminal, copier, telephone, and other standard office equipment; ability to sit in the same position for extended periods (5.5+ hours a day) at a time using continuous hand motions when entering data into the computer system. Additional Information: LSU seeks to employ qualified, fiscally responsible individuals in sensitive positions within the university. Therefore, all candidates and temporary staff who are selected for employment at Louisiana State University for a position that regularly engages in financial matters including handling credit cards, cash, grant funds, or other university funds must undergo a credit check per FASOP HR04. Competencies: Knowledge of accounting principles and contract and grant activities.  Knowledge and application of various computer programs, including but not limited to Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint), and Adobe Acrobat. Excellent oral and written communication skills.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide cover letter, resume and three (3) professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire (if applicable). Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities this position shall be subject to pre-employment screenings as required by LSU FASOP HR-04. For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Bryan Greenwood at bgreenwood@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 10, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Teacher---Children-s-Center_R00118565": {
      "title": "Assistant Teacher - Children's Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Teacher - Children's Center     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUA FA - ChildCtr - Daycare (Sarah Grace Corley (00066261))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: LSUA Children's Center Job Description Job Title: Assistant Teacher - Children's Center Position Description: Supervise and ensure the safety and well-being of the children at all times, being alert for needs and/or problems of the children as individuals and as a group. Know at all times how many children are in your care Know the names and ages of all children in your care at any given time Report to the director any special needs or problems of individual children Report to the director any cases of suspected child abuse or neglect Assist assigned Teacher in any way possible, which may include, but is not limited to: Planning curriculum with lead teacher Implementing daily program for class Preparing bulletin boards and other visuals with children’s art or lesson theme materials Changing diapers, helping student potty, and applying any medications Plating, dispersing, and helping feed students’ breakfast, lunch, and snack Keeping classroom clean, neat, and orderly Vacuuming and mopping classrooms and cleaning restrooms Communicating with parents daily about needs and activities of the child Documenting daily activities, any incidents, and any other necessary information Attend in-service workshops to complete at least 12 hours of continuing education hours each licensing year and as the director sees necessary Assume temporary responsibilities of a teacher in case of their absence Be familiar with all center policies and procedures, as well as early childhood licensing regulations Attend staff meetings, evaluations, parent conferences, team-teaching meetings, and school family functions Assist with other duties as needed or as assigned by the teacher and/or director Required Qualifications: Must be 18 years or older Must be able to pass a Child Care Background Check Must be able to obtain Pediatric First Aid/CPR licensure Previous experience in childcare preferred     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at 318-473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu. Please attach all transcripts or certificates to your application for proof of education and training.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0305-AR-Choppin-Hall---Chemistry/Postdoctoral-Scholar_R00118315": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Postdoctoral Scholar     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAM Science - Chem - Physical Infrared (Daniel Kuroda (00002539))     Work Location: 0305 A.R. Choppin Hall - Chemistry     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: The Postdoctoral Scholar will investigate molecular structure and mechanisms giving rise to macroscopic properties of electrolytes in the bulk, characterize electrolytes through spectroscopic methods (IR ultrafast spectroscopy) and electrochemical (EIS and Cyclic voltammetry) to name a few and collaborate with theoreticians to obtain molecular insights into the experiments. Duties 60% Perform research in the lab ranging from material preparation, characterization, and modeling, develop projects and propose new ideas. 30% Write manuscripts and support proposal writing and reports on various projects 10% Mentor students and participate in collaborations Min qualifications: PhD in chemistry or related field Job Competencies Must be able to plan and execute experiments, work alone or with other members of the group, and possess strong scientific writing skills.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide CV and names and contact details for at least three references. A copy of your transcript(s) should be attached to your application (if available); however, original transcripts are required prior to hire. For questions regarding the status of your application or more details of the position, please contact Professor Daniel Kuroda at dkuroda@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 12, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 10, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): N     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
