    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/French-House/Instructor---Part-Time_R00118297": {
      "title": "Instructor - Part-Time",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor - Part-Time     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM AA - HC - Instruction (Drew Lamonica Arms (00003093))     Work Location: French House     Pay Grade:     Job Description: This part-time instructor will focus on teaching one introductory course worth three credit hours in the Ogden Honors College. Job Responsibilities Teach an introductory course worth three credit hours in the Ogden Honors College. (100%) Additional Information FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related matter, they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. Experience teaching and/or developing introductory courses in Honors     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns 