    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Professor-of-Finance_R00118217": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Finance     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Business Administration (Rafael Ernesto Romero Moreno Sr. (00008021))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: College of Business Department of Accounting & Finance Full-Time, 9-Month Finance Assistant Professor Position Purpose: The College of Business at Louisiana State University of Alexandria invites applications for a full-time, Assistant Professor of Finance. We are seeking an educator who is committed to teaching excellence, student success, and the mission of an institution that values innovation, engagement, and service to Central Louisiana. This is a nine-month position. This 9-month, teaching-focused instructor role carries a 12-credit hour course load per semester (4 courses) during the fall and spring terms. Summer teachings optional but highly encouraged. Responsibilities: Teach 12 credit hours per semester (fall and spring) in Finance, Economics, Accounting, and related areas of business aligned with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Develop and deliver high-quality, student-centered instruction in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Participate in curriculum planning, program review, and development of applied learning opportunities, including internships, case competitions, and community-based projects. Maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline that aligns with ACBSP expectations. Support ACBSP accreditation by contributing to assessment, documentation, and continuous improvement of academic programs. Support student recruitment, retention, outreach initiatives, and alumni engagement efforts. Support Command Your Career and other career development programs designed to prepare students for success in the workforce. Engage in service to the department, College, University, and profession, including committee work, faculty governance, and involvement in business-community partnerships throughout Central Louisiana. Facilitate workshops in collaboration with Continuing Education, the Small Business Development Center (SBDC) and other key stakeholders to support regional business growth and student learning. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Finance or a closely related field with at least 18 graduate hours in Finance. Preferred Qualifications: Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or DBA) in Finance from a regionally accredited institution. Additional specialty certifications such as CFA, CPA, CFP, and FRM are valued. Documented record of excellence in teaching, as demonstrated through student evaluations, teaching awards, or peer reviews. Experience in course and curriculum design, particularly in support of accreditation or continuous improvement processes (preferably ACBSP). Proven record of working effectively as part of a team- partnering with colleagues, staff, and community stakeholders to strengthen programs and support student success. Application Requirements: Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the instructor position Curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references Note: Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, a writing sample, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Instructions: Please attach a Resume/CV, a cover letter, 3 references and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Please attach all transcripts to your application. A background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at (318) 473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 5, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Student-Health-Center-Cl-Infirmary-Building/Patient-Access-Coordinator_R00118170-1": {
      "title": "Patient Access Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Patient Access Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - SA - H&WB - SHC - Ops - Fin - Patient Access (Vickie Dedwylder Hendrix (00006679))     Work Location: Student Health Center (C&l Infirmary) Building     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: The Patient Access Coordinator functions as the initial contact for all incoming patients to the Student Health Center (SHC), including students, spouses, employees (for worker's compensation injuries), campus visitors, and others participating in special camps and programs. The Coordinator is a member of the multi-disciplinary team in the Medical Clinics, including general medicine, gynecology and specialty care. The Coordinator supports both the check-in process, including scheduling and health records, and the check-out process, including accounts receivable. Should have a deep appreciation for a collaborative care model, partnering with all areas of the SHC, and be committed to advancing the divisional priorities, and cultivating a working relationship with Our Lady of the Lake Health. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES 40% - Schedule, reschedule, cancel and confirm in-person and telehealth appointments and manage provider schedules in multiple clinics. Greet and direct patients and visitors in a friendly, prompt, and helpful manner. Maintain accuracy of patient demographics, contact information, insurance information and filing status by verifying this information at each patient encounter upon check-in. Ensure required/applicable forms are presented, explained and completed correctly to finalize check-in process. Maintain patient confidentiality and a working knowledge of all relevant policies and procedures, including HIPAA and the SHC eligibility policy. Answer general inquiries related to the SHC routing the inquiry to the appropriate unit, as needed. 40% - Collect and review all patient insurance information needed to complete the benefit verification process. Upon check-in, initiate patient tracking in the Electronic Health Records System. Accurately collect and post co-pays and other appropriate fees at check-in. Accurately post patient payments by recording cash, checks and credit card transactions and provide receipts to patients. Respond to patient inquires regarding basic insurance questions. Perform daily cash reconciliation and reporting of individual till. 15% - Review forms and records for accuracy and scan to appropriate health record when needed; manage requests to release Protected Health Information (PHI), verifying identity, confirming multiple unique identifiers, and releasing information exactly as specified. Monitor incoming faxes and assign to appropriate staff, when appropriate. Send outgoing faxes (i.e. referrals, refill requests, etc.) to external providers as requested. Serve as backup for merging duplicate health records and run necessary daily reports in absence of Patient Access Manager. Check out patients and complete the patient tracking in the Electronic Health Records System. 5% - Other Duties. Performs other duties as assigned by the Executive Director. This includes but is not limited to efforts that support broad division/institution efforts including engaging in in-service opportunities for the division, and other special projects. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree Two years of health care office experience. General administrative and clerical procedures. Working knowledge of an electronic clinic management/ health record, healthcare and insurance terminology and procedures. ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS/EXPECTATIONS Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to drug/alcohol testing in accordance with University Policy Statement 67. This position has access to/directly handles cash. Financial history/credit check required per FASOP HR-04. In accordance with University Policy Statement 18, this position is considered essential and may be required to report or stay on campus in the event of an emergency or closure. May be required to work occasional nights and weekends.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Requested application materials include a letter of interest or cover letter; resume or curriculum vitae; and the names, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of at least three professional references. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Kelsi Taylor at ktay126@lsu.edu or 225-578-2308.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Adaptability, Confidentiality, Customer Service, Data Entry, Detail-Oriented, Task Organization, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 5, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): December 3, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/United-Plaza-XII/Coordinator-of-Academic-Area-4_R00118239-1": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Academic Area 4",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Coordinator of Academic Area 4     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM Online - CE - CCR - PD - Online Programs & Partnerships (Michelle Theriot Carbo (00010442))     Work Location: United Plaza XII     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: Coordinates non-credit continuing online education programs for participants from business, industry, government, professional organizations, and the general adult population. Manages large content and employee partnerships. Job Responsibilities: Handles all program logistics including customer service, scheduling, registrations, instructors, course materials, technology tools, and reporting. Ability to manage large scale projects. 40% Makes all fiscal arrangements for programs, including budgeting, salary negotiation, and registration fees. Assist in contract negotiations and executing contracts. 20% Implements non-credit continuing education programs for participants from business, industry, government, professional organizations, the general adult population. Assists in promotion of courses and certificates. 20% Evaluates programs and identifies ways to improve upon instruction, content and facilitation of future program offerings. Assists in program and course development. 15% Other duties as assigned. 5% Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with 3 years of experience LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Additional Requirements: Operation Essential Personnel - This position may be asked to work during an official closure, but who is otherwise not required to report to the physical campus during a closure and whose absence does not present a risk to the safety, resources, and well-being of the campus per FASOP HR-01. Additional Information: This position may require more than 40 hours per week including nights and weekends.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, (3) professional references, and transcripts. Official transcripts are required prior to hire, if needed. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Michelle Carbo at mcarbo@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 5, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): August 19, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
