    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0102-Music-School-Building/Cordell-and-Ava-Haymon-Endowed-Chair-of-Music-Therapy---Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Music_R00110758": {
      "title": "Cordell and Ava Haymon Endowed Chair of Music Therapy & Associate or Full Professor of Music",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Cordell and Ava Haymon Endowed Chair of Music Therapy & Associate or Full Professor of Music     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM CMDA - School of Music (James L Byo (00010414))     Work Location: 0102 Music School Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Louisiana State University invites applications for the position of the Cordell and Ava Haymon Endowed Chair of Music Therapy, an endowed, tenured faculty appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership for LSU's rapidly growing Music Therapy program within the School of Music in the College of Music & Dramatic Arts (CMDA).This endowed position offers a rare opportunity to lead the first music therapy degree program established at a public university in Louisiana and to shape the future of music therapy education, research, and clinical practice across the state and the Gulf South. Established through the generosity of the Haymon family, whose multigenerational commitment has been instrumental in advancing music therapy at LSU, the endowed chair provides significant annual resources to support innovative research, instructional excellence, clinical partnerships, faculty and student development, and strategic program growth. LSU welcomed its inaugural Bachelor of Music Therapy cohort in Fall 2023. With a strong undergraduate curriculum now established, the program is poised for its next phase of growth, including expanded enrollment, transformative clinical partnerships, externally funded research, and the development of graduate education opportunities. Situated within a Carnegie R1 research university, the Chair will play a central role in defining a long-term vision for the program while expanding access to high-quality music therapy education and services in a region where such opportunities remain limited. The Chair reports to the Director of the School of Music and will collaborate extensively across LSU's expanding research and healthcare enterprise, including LSU Health New Orleans, LSU Health Shreveport, the LSU AgCenter, the Pennington Biomedical Research Center, and partners throughout the healthcare, education, and community sectors. These collaborations create exceptional opportunities to advance interdisciplinary research and clinical innovation in areas such as cancer care, behavioral health, rehabilitation, integrative medicine, survivorship, symptom management, and healthcare equity. Located in a state internationally recognized for its rich and diverse musical heritage, LSU provides a distinctive environment where music serves as both a defining cultural force and a powerful vehicle for health, healing, and community engagement. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to build a nationally recognized program that advances scholarship, transforms clinical practice, and strengthens the role of music therapy in improving health and well-being throughout Louisiana, the Gulf South, and beyond. Job Responsibilities: Provide visionary leadership for LSU's Music Therapy program, including strategic planning, program development, faculty leadership, accreditation, and oversight of clinical education and operations. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in music therapy while mentoring students, supervising clinical training, and ensuring excellence in professional preparation. Lead a nationally recognized program of scholarship by advancing innovative, externally funded research and maintaining a distinguished national and international reputation in music therapy. Cultivate interdisciplinary partnerships across LSU's health, research, and clinical enterprise to expand music therapy research, clinical practice, and community engagement. Develop and sustain clinical affiliations with healthcare systems, community organizations, and regional partners to enhance experiential learning and expand access to music therapy services. Recruit, mentor, and support faculty and students in fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and high-achieving academic environment. Provide leadership in university governance and professional service , contributing to departmental, college, university, and national initiatives that advance the field of music therapy. Represent LSU and the Music Therapy program through professional organizations, public engagement, and partnerships that elevate the university's leadership in music therapy education, research, and clinical innovation. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate (Ph.D., DMA, or equivalent terminal degree) in Music Therapy or a closely related discipline with a demonstrated focus on music therapy. Board Certification in Music Therapy (MT-BC) or equivalent profesional credential. Eligibility for appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated excellence in university-level teaching. Evidence of mastery of professional music therapy competencies and advanced clinical practice. Experience developing clinical partnerships in medical, educational, behavioral health or community settings. Record of scholarly achievement, including peer-reviewed publications and other evidence of sustained research activity. Demonstrated ability to mentor student scholarship. Preferred Qualifications: Establish national or international reputation in music therapy research, clinical practice, education or leadership. Experience working with a research-intensive university environment. Experience pursuing federal funding opportunities, including NIH or related agencies. Experience supervising music therapy clinical training programs and overseeing internship or practicum experiences. Record of interdisciplinary collaboration involving healthcare, psychology, education, neuroscience, rehabilitation, public health or related fields. Leadership in local, regional, national, or international professional organizations. Leadership in program development, enrollment growth, accreditation or strategic planning. LSU's College of Music & Dramatic Arts comprises two schools, Music and Theatre & Film. It is a performing arts community that trains, cultivates, prepares, and rewards excellent artists, educators, scholars, and performers, fostering passion for the arts, collaboration, and the creation of new works. We engage with our community, heightening our collective ability to communicate with expressive power and purpose. The LSU School of Music stands as one of the nation's most comprehensive music programs and serves as a premier cultural arts center for the state of Louisiana. Nestled within the College of Music & Dramatic Arts at Louisiana State University in Baton Rouge, the School has cultivated a rich tradition of musical excellence for nearly a century — earning its initial accreditation from the National Association of Schools of Music (NASM) in 1931, a distinction it has held and renewed ever since, with its most recent comprehensive review completed in 2024. With a vibrant community of nearly 500 music majors, students find themselves immersed in a tight-knit, artistically driven environment where world-class instruction meets Louisiana's uniquely rich cultural heritage. The School offers a remarkable breadth of degree options across every level of study — from undergraduate degrees in Music Performance, Music Education, Music Therapy, and Music Composition to graduate programs including the Master of Music, Doctor of Musical Arts, and PhD in Music. Students learn from an acclaimed faculty of renowned scholars, stellar performers, and inspiring teachers with active international careers, supplemented by a world-renowned network of visiting artists at the forefront of their fields. Graduate students in particular benefit from a hands-on, 21st-century curriculum that emphasizes flexibility, artistic expression, communication, and technology — preparing them not just to perform, but to discover, create, and lead in a rapidly evolving musical landscape.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Review of applications begins on September 14, 2026. To receive full consideration, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, contact information for three references, teaching philosophy (one page), and summary of research program with links to two most influential publications (one page). Teaching videos may be requested at a later date. Official transcripts are required prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Joseph Dunbar at jdunbar@lsu.edu or Lauren Hensel at lfoster1@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): January 30, 2027    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Professor-of-Management_R00118063": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Management     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Business Administration (Rafael Ernesto Romero Moreno Sr. (00008021))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: College of Business  Department of Management and Marketing  Full-Time, 9-Month, Assistant Professor of Management Purpose: The College of Business at Louisiana State University of Alexandria invites applications for a full-time, Assistant Professor of Management. We are seeking an educator who is committed to teaching excellence, student success, and the mission of an institution that values innovation, engagement, and service to Central Louisiana. This is a nine-month position. This 9-month, teaching-focused instructor role carries a 12-credit hour course load per semester (4 courses) during the fall and spring terms. Summer teaching is optional but highly encouraged. Responsibilities: Teach 12 credit hours per semester (fall and spring) in Management, and related areas of business aligned with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Develop and deliver high-quality, student-centered instruction in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Participate in curriculum planning, program review, and development of applied learning opportunities, including internships, case competitions, and community-based projects. Maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline that aligns with ACBSP expectations. Support ACBSP accreditation by contributing to assessment, documentation, and continuous improvement of academic programs. Support student recruitment, retention, outreach initiatives, and alumni engagement efforts. Support Command Your Career and other career development programs designed to prepare students for success in the workforce. Engage in service to the department, College, University, and profession, including committee work, faculty governance, and involvement in business-community partnerships throughout Central Louisiana. Facilitate workshops in collaboration with Continuing Education, the Small Business Development Center (SBDC) and other key stakeholders to support regional business growth and student learning. Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or DBA) in Management from a regionally accredited institution. Documented record of excellence in teaching, as demonstrated through student evaluations, teaching awards, or peer reviews. Experience in course and curriculum design, particularly in support of accreditation or continuous improvement processes (preferably ACBSP). Proven record of working effectively as part of a team; partnering with colleagues, staff, and community stakeholders to strengthen programs and support student success. Application Requirements: Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the instructor position Curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references Note: Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, a writing sample, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Requirements: • Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the instructor position • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial transcripts • Names and contact information for three professional references Note: Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, a writing sample, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired. Background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at 318-473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: August 3, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Veterinary-Medicine/Assistant-Professor-of-Anatomy_R00118014": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Anatomy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Anatomy     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM VetMed - School of Comparative Biomedical Sciences (Alexander Murashov (00082114))     Work Location: Veterinary Medicine     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: The Anatomy Assistant Professor (Clinical track) participates in the delivery of lecture and laboratory material (gross- and micro-anatomy) for the Form & Function courses to first year veterinary students in the veterinary professional curriculum; assists with the preparation of all teaching materials related to the assigned teaching responsibilities; conducts scholarly activities; mentors professional and graduate students and contributes service at the department, school, and university levels. Job Responsibilities: 60% - The assistant professor participates in the delivery of lecture material and the laboratory anatomy courses to first year veterinary students in the veterinary professional curriculum. 25% -The assistant professor assists with the preparation of all teaching materials related to the assigned teaching responsibilities. These duties include doing prosections, embalming, and maintaining specimen collection, and performing other duties as assigned 10% -The assistant professor mentors professional and graduate students and contributes service at the department, school, and university level. 5% - The assistant professor conducts scholarly activities. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements: DVM or equivalent (Applicants with a Ph.D. in a related field are encouraged to apply.) Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. and 1+ years of teaching experience in gross anatomy laboratory/lecture settings Special and Physical Qualifications: Safety and Security Sensitive Job - Safety and security-sensitive positions are defined as those positions where any form of substance abuse may affect University activities through unsafe work behavior/performance or error in judgment; or where substance abuse could jeopardize the safety and well-being of employees, other personnel, or the general public, or cause significant damage to University property. This includes positions requiring firearms, access to controlled substances, handling hazardous material, operating heavy equipment or machinery, etc. These positions are subject to drug screens per PS-67/FASOP HR-04. FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health related matter they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Requires standing, sitting, walking, bending, reaching (above shoulder), reaching (below shoulder), vision (near sight), vision (far sight), crawling, twisting, pushing/pulling, climbing, squatting, lifting more than 50 pounds, and lifting less than 50 pounds.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. Please provide your CV/resume and three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if applicable). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. Alexander Murashov at amurashov@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 31, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): October 31, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating