    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/William-B-Hatcher-Hall/Coordinator-of-International-Student-Success_R00117036": {
      "title": "Coordinator of International Student Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Coordinator of International Student Success     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - OGE - International Student Engagement (Daniela Chu-Rodriguez (00076514))     Work Location: William B. Hatcher Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: At Louisiana State University, we believe in being a magnet for global talent. With nearly 2,000 international students representing 107 countries – including our largest populations from Bangladesh and India – our goal is to provide a gold standard of service that reflects our deep commitment to excellence. To help us achieve this, we are looking for a dedicated Coordinator of International Student Success to join the Office of Global Engagement. This is a unique, dual-focused position that sits at the heart of our international community. You will split your energy equally between International Student Services (ISS) and the Global Community Center (GCC), ensuring our students have both the immigration and compliance support and the vibrant social home they need to thrive. Position reports directly to the Director of International Student Engagement with a dotted line of supervision to the Director of International Student Services. Job Responsibilities Immigration Compliance and Support (50%) Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO), maintaining compliance with federal immigration laws. Provide basic immigration advising to all international students, primarily via email communications. Manage the ISS email inbox to ensure the office stays up to date on the workflow and student needs. Coordinate all advising appointments between the ISS staff and students, including the setup, use, and configuration of scheduling software. Schedule and organize meetings and track projects. Manage ISS logistics, including programming such as immigration workshops. Assist with technology needs to streamline the international student experience. Perform general administrative support duties and maintain office records. International Student Engagement (50%) Assist in the planning and implementation of programs throughout the calendar year, including international orientation, night and weekend events. Assist in overseeing daily GCC operations, including space rentals, catering logistics, facility upkeep, and GCC initiatives. Contribute to the supervision and coordination of student staff, providing guidance and team oversight. Work alongside the Coordinator of International Student Engagement to represent the Global Community Center and provide student services at campus events, outreach initiatives, and tabling opportunities. Assist with the upkeep of and responses to emails in the GCC email account, including responding to general inquiries and referring students to resources. Other duties as assigned. Additional Information This position requires evening, holiday, and weekend hours. The Coordinator must be available for early morning and/or evening programs and special circumstances that may arise. The Coordinator must be eligible to drive as needed on official University business. Scheduling will be coordinated by the supervising Director(s). This position will support both units in a flexible manner, depending on busy seasons, deadlines, staffing needs, etc., as directed by the supervising Director(s). This position requires a valid driver's license, will require an MVR, and is subject to drug screens per PM-33/PS-67/FASOP HR-04.   As mandated by federal regulations, U.S. Citizenship or Lawful Permanent Residence is required to be a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO) for approval to access the Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) and thereby perform the duties of this position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and 1 year of experience working with students in a university setting. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Minimum Licenses/Certifications Valid Driver's License     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Daniela Chu-Rodriguez at drodriguez@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Adaptability, Campus Operations, Customer Service, Ethics, Program Support, Student Advocacy, Task Organization     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 15, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 4, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Administration/Assistant-Vice-President-of-Communications-Content_R00117250": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President of Communications Content",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Vice President of Communications Content     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM OCUR - Office of Communications (Meg Casper Sunstrom (00327313) (Inherited))     Work Location: University Administration     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: Strategizes for and directs LSU's overall global public relations and communications efforts with the university leadership team; promotes and publicizes LSU and the LSU System at the local, state, national and international levels; works to enhance LSU's reputation through communications and public relations; strategizes for and develops crisis communications for LSU; directs the writing department within the LSU Marketing & Communications Office. Responsibilities: 40%: Coordinate and create content for multiple communications platforms using writers, videographers, graphic designers, social media specialists and media relations team. Content should promote and amplify LSU’s flagship campus as well as the System with a focus on audiences including students, alumni, faculty/researchers, donors, policy makers and the general public. 30%: Works directly with the flagship Chancellor/Provost in coordination with Enrollment Management Staff to identify recruitment strategies and the communications materials need to support those efforts annually. 20%: Oversee the Campus Communicators group, organize and plan meetings to ensure LSU flagship and system priorities/messaging are understood and amplified towards common goals. Establish and socialize campus communicator responsibilities for content creation and support of their direct supervisors while clarifying Marketing & Communication’s oversight/approval roles as well as shared assets that are available for use. 10%: Crisis Planning: Serve as a member of LSU’s Emergency Operations Center Core Committee, which works year-round to plan for/prevent crisis on campus. Attend crisis training and planning exercises. Provides periodic updates of crisis materials to staff. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree with 10 years of experience LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree with 12 plus years of proven experience in crisis communication, proficient knowledge of AP writing style, proven verbal and written communication skills, proven ability to manage a large number of employees, problem-solving skills, experience in issues management, experience in ghostwriting and with social media. Additional Requirements: This position may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach CV/resume, cover letter, and the names of three professional references. A copy of your transcripts may be attached to your application (if available). However, official transcripts are required prior to hire. Please attach all documents under the “Resume/CV” section of your application. Attachments are limited to five. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Meg Sunstrom at msunst1@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 11, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0101-William-B-Hatcher-Hall/Operations-Coordinator_R00117027": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Operations Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - OGE - Business Operations (Jennifer L Kennison (00012282))     Work Location: 0101 William B. Hatcher Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The Operations Coordinator is a key member of the Office of Global Engagement Administrative unit at Louisiana State University. The Coordinator will serve the University community and partners through exceptional service, relationship building, and administrative support. This position reports directly to the Associate Director of Finance and Operations for the Office of Global Engagement. The Coordinator will facilitate positive working relationships both internally and externally. This is an excellent opportunity to support international and domestic students, faculty, staff, suppliers, and partners with the goal of advancing internationalization. To be a successful member of the operations team, the Coordinator will contribute to and participate in improving the experience of the international community at LSU. This is a public-facing position not currently eligible for remote work. The standard University hours of operation are 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM CST, Monday - Friday. Job Responsibilities Front Desk Administration (40%): Receive and direct students, faculty, staff, scholars, parents, visitors, and guests. Assist individuals and groups in-person, by phone, email, and video conference. Foster positive working relationships inside and outside of the Office of Global Engagement team. Act as a resource, being willing to solve problems independently or collaboratively as needed. Coordinate internal and external communications. Manage general inquiries, mail, and specialized correspondence. Act courteously and professionally at all times. Maintain a professional appearance. Be understanding and considerate of academic, personal, professional, cultural, and family concerns. Actively work to increase one’s cultural competence. Handle sensitive information in a confidential and trustworthy manner. Exercise discretion and independent judgment. Receive and distribute highly sensitive documents. Log incoming and outgoing documentation properly. Ensure individuals and groups successfully connect with the resources needed in a timely manner. Ensure efficient operations and the positive presentation of Hatcher Hall spaces. Prepare regular reports to be distributed to the Office of Global Engagement leadership team, informing them of trends, challenges, opportunities, and needs identified through tracking data related to interactions and requests at the front desk. Administrative Support (30%): Assist with the planning of Global Engagement programming and initiatives as directed. Support engagement by utilizing software and web-based programs to schedule meetings, appointments, conference calls, advising sessions, and video conferences. Draft, format, organize, update, and distribute materials to appropriate parties as needed. Assist Global Engagement team members with administrative tasks, including but not limited to ordering/ locating/organizing supplies, preparing for programming and events, and addressing team needs in a timely manner to avoid disruption to workflows. Business Operations (30%): As a member of the Business Operations team, process financial reconciliation tasks in support of Global Engagement staff, Study Abroad faculty, staff, and students, etc. Process requisitions, deposits, internal charges, and small-dollar purchases on behalf of the Office of Global Engagement. Develop and maintain operational processes and workflows to ensure resources are used efficiently. Support relevant annual cycles and requirements, including but not limited to inventory, fiscal year-end, study abroad accounting, scholarships, orientations, unit strategic planning, etc. Additional Requirements FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related matter, they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in any field and 1 year of experience in a professional setting, including experience managing documents and digital files. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business, Accounting, International Business, International Studies, or a related field. Specific Experience: Professional, educational, and/or volunteer experience with student, international, and/or multicultural populations. Experience traveling, studying, and/or living abroad.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Jennifer Kennison at jkennison@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Active Listening, Adaptability, Campus Operations, Customer Service, Ethics, Program Support, Student Advocacy, Task Organization     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 14, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 4, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
