    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0203-David-F-Boyd-Hall/Office-Coordinator_R00117104": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Office Coordinator     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM FA - Office of Administration (Ashley Scott Territo (00008605))     Work Location: 0203 David F. Boyd Hall     Pay Grade: Professional Hourly     Job Description: Job Summary: The Office Coordinator supports the mission and function of the full range of Staff Senate at the LSU A&M campus as well as administrative support for Finance and Administration. Finance and Administration's primary responsibility is the stewardship and enhancement of the University’s financial, physical and human resources. LSU Staff Senate promotes and protects the welfare of the LSU staff by representing the interest of and the issues impacting all staff members. It is comprised of duly elected representatives from the University staff and serves as a recognized voice of the LSU staff. This includes but is not limited to event planning and logistics, social media, meeting facilitation and support, website and email management, procurement, budgetary tasks, and other special projects. The position supports the members of the Staff Senate, members and chairpersons of standing committees, members and chairpersons of ad hoc committees, and members of liaison assignments. The position provides a smooth transition between executive officers, committee chairpersons, and other newly elected or appointed Senators. This position creates efficiency and consistency in Staff Senate and Finance and Administration. The position functionally reports to the Manager of Operations and is supervised by the Manager of Operations and Staff Senate President. Occasional travel and attendance for Staff-Senate sponsored events may be required. Job Responsibilities: 20%- Finance and Administration Support- Serves as the HR Analyst for several units (B&P, HRM and Risk Management) ensuring accuracy of Workday transactions and compliance with civil service and university polices. Provide office support for F&A operations including but not limited to scheduling meetings, answering phones, processing mail etc. Assist with processing forms, LSU Ring Program, Summer youth Programs and special project requests for Finance and Administration or assigned by the supervisor. 25%- Staff Senate Governance & Operations Schedules, organizes, and facilitates all Staff Senate, Executive Committee, and committee meetings. Confirms meeting locations and virtual platforms; operates and oversees audio, video, and recording equipment. Prepares, posts, and distributes meeting agendas and supporting materials in compliance with the Staff Senate Constitution and Bylaws. Attends meetings and records, transcribes, and distributes official minutes, attendance records, and supporting documentation. Maintains and has a working knowledge of the Staff Senate Constitution, Bylaws, Operating Procedures, public meeting requirements, and parliamentary procedures. Drafts presentations and supporting materials for Staff Senate leadership. Assists with elections, appointments, and onboarding of new senators. 20%- Staff Senate Administrative Support Serves as the primary administrative liaison for the Staff Senate. Supplies direct administrative and project support to the Staff Senate President, Executive Committee, Committee Chairs, and Staff Senators. Provides support with scheduling, agenda development, and documentation deadlines. Maintains and updates governing documents, including Mission Statement, Constitution, Bylaws, resolutions, and committee charges. Maintains Senator rosters, committee membership lists, and term records. Manages the Staff Senate calendar, documents, and digital files. At the direction of Staff Senate leadership, facilitates special projects and initiatives. Researches staff-related governance and policy issues; prepares briefing materials and reports. Maintains rosters of Staff Senators and committees, including descriptions, leadership roles, and meeting schedules. Coordinates special projects as assigned by the Staff Senate President. 15%- Events & Programmatic Support Plans, coordinates, and supports Staff Senate events, programs, and university functions. Manages event logistics and on-site coordination for Staff Senate initiatives and campus engagement activities. Assists with the development and execution of staff-focused programs, recognition initiatives, and professional development opportunities. Coordinates forums, presentations, and engagement activities that support communication and collaboration across the university community. Provides operational and administrative support for Staff Senate-sponsored events and special initiatives. Other duties as assigned. 10%- Communications & Engagement Manages communication among Staff Senate, university leadership, and staff, as authorized by the Staff Senate President and Executive Committee. Drafts and distributes newsletters, announcements, and campus updates. Manages the Staff Senate email, internal communications, distribution lists, and inquiries about Staff Senate activities and processes. Maintains all Staff Senate website content. Creates and manages content for Staff Senate social media accounts. Creates marketing and promotional materials supporting Staff Senate initiatives, events and policies. Designs, distributes, and analyzes Staff Senate surveys and prepares summary reports. 10%- Budget & Finance Administration Procures supplies, equipment, and services in accordance with university policies. Completes University required forms prior to purchasing items that require special permissions. Collects funds from senators for Staff Senate Gift Fund. Processes payments, reimbursements, deposits, and internal financial transactions in a timely manner. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with some related experience. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply. A degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application, please contact Ashley Territo at 225-578-4342 or aterrito@lsu.edu.     Skills Needed: Administrative Support, Communication, Customer Service, Data Entry, Detail-Oriented, Microsoft Office, Task Organization, Time Management     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 6, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0102-Agricultural-Chemistry-For-Telecom-Use/Research-Associate-Specialist_R00117044": {
      "title": "Research Associate Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate Specialist     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAG Vice Presidents Office - Department of Agricultural Chemistry (David Allen Wall (00000072))     Work Location: 0102 Agricultural Chemistry (For Telecom Use)     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: Work Location: Department of Agricultural Chemistry, Louisiana State University Agricultural Center, Baton Rouge, LA 70803 Position Description: Responsible for performing basic and intermediate chemical laboratory work which involves the qualitative and quantitative chemical analysis of various samples including, feed, fertilizer, water, soil, plant and animal tissues for a variety of analytes. Some analyses will require the use of sophisticated instrumentation, including gas and liquid chromatography, inductively coupled plasma-optical emission spectrometer, nitrogen combustion analyzer, and other analytical instrumentation. Performing basic and intermediate laboratory tasks required for operation of laboratory including sample preparation, preventative and routine maintenance of analytical equipment, preparation of solutions and reagents, purchase of required reagents and supplies and normal laboratory housekeeping duties. Perform work in accordance with modern analytical chemical laboratory methods and procedures, such as those approved by AAFCO, AAPFCO, AOAC, FDA, USDA, and EPA as well as SOPs used by the laboratory. Other duties as assigned. Qualification Requirements : B.S. in chemistry, biochemistry, environmental science or an agricultural science related field. Course work or experience in chemistry or laboratory analysis and a strong background in analytical chemistry are preferred. Familiarity with the handling of feed, fertilizer, pesticides or other agricultural inputs and laboratory quality assurance and quality control are desirable. LSU and the AgCenter are dedicated to fostering an environment where our employees feel appreciated for their skills and individual qualifications. If a candidate does not meet the minimum qualifications listed but has other qualifications or substantial experience related to the key responsibilities, we encourage them to apply (La RS 42:36). Salary and Benefits : Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Current benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some child care and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year, typically includes a week off at Christmas), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment. Date Available : Upon completion of the selection process. Application Deadline : July 22, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified. Application Procedure : Apply online at https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU  (or through Workday for internal applicants) by attaching files containing a letter of application, curriculum vita, official university transcripts, and three letters of reference. Paper, faxed or e-mailed application materials will not be accepted, except that in lieu of attaching the reference letters online, they may be sent directly to: Dr. Ted Gauthier, Department Head Agricultural Chemistry Department Agricultural Chemistry Building – LSU 4159 Highland Rd, Room 102 Baton Rouge, LA 70803 Email: TGauthier@agcenter.lsu.edu   Telephone: 225/353/9545 Website: www.lsuagcenter.com The LSU Agricultural Center is a statewide campus of the LSU System and provides equal opportunities in programs and employment.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Research Associate Specialist     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 8, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - The LSU AgCenter has an attractive benefits package with a wide variety of benefit options. Benefits offered include retirement, multiple medical insurance options, supplemental insurances (dental, life, long-term disability, accident, vision, long-term care, etc.), Tax Saver Flexible Benefits Plan (saves tax dollars on some childcare and medical expenses), university holidays (14 per year), generous annual (vacation) and sick leave benefits, Employee Assistance Program, and possible educational leave and tuition exemption for coursework at campuses of the LSU System. Specific benefits depend on job category, percent effort and length of employment.      Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     About the LSU Agricultural Center: The LSU AgCenter , is one of eight campuses within the broader LSU enterprise (LSU System). The LSU AgCenter includes the Louisiana Agricultural Experiment Station, which conducts agricultural-based research, and the Louisiana Cooperative Extension Service, which extends the knowledge derived from research to the people of the state. The AgCenter is headquartered in Baton Rouge and has 12 “on campus” academic departments and five regions which are made up of 15 branch research stations and an extension office in each parish.  For more information, visit the AgCenter’s website at www.lsuagcenter.com .        The LSU Agricultural Center is an Equal Opportunity Employer. HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU AgCenter Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-2258 or emailed HRMHelp@agcenter.lsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0501-Moran-Family-Ctr-for-Athletic-Admin/Assistant-Director----Broadcast-Operations_R00116968": {
      "title": "Assistant Director -  Broadcast Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Director - Broadcast Operations     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM Athletics - Ops - MP - Broadcast Operations (Lee Andrew Scioneaux (00009804))     Work Location: 0501 Moran Family Ctr for Athletic Admin     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The Core Values of LSU Athletics define who we are and what we do. They are: Excellence, Integrity, Authenticity, Perseverance, Respect, Fairness, Growth, and Service. They are the support system that sustains our success. These values work together, constantly collaborating and combining to secure our future and drive our unending work to create transformational change – for our student-athletes, for our athletics community, and for the millions across the world who know and love these three letters. Forever LSU. The Assistant Director - Broadcast Operations advances the mission and values of the LSU Athletics Department by delivering the LSU Tigers brand through compelling, informative, and entertaining broadcast and in-venue productions. This position contributes to the execution and continued growth of SEC Network+, ESPN digital/linear broadcasts, and in-venue video board shows. 45% Serve as a key contributor to both network broadcasts and in-venue productions for assigned LSU events. Coordinate live production elements, ensuring a high-quality final product. Operate and maintain familiarity with broadcast equipment, including switchers, replay systems, graphics, cameras, communications, and signal routing. Assist the engineering team with upkeep and functionality of control room and venue equipment. 30% Support the development and management of production graphics and workflows. This includes creating graphic elements, building rundowns, and integrating video and statistical content into live productions. Contribute to technical execution and step into various production roles as needed during events. 20% Provide leadership and support to student workers and freelance crew during productions. Assist in training and development across production roles, helping to improve consistency and execution. Take ownership of assigned areas on gameday and contribute to efficient crew operations . 5% Advances and supports LSU and Athletics Department initiatives through participation in educational and developmental opportunities, as well as engagement in a culture consistent with the values of LSU and its Athletics Department; works collaboratively with the Office of Communications and University Relations and adheres to established standards; other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree with two years of experience in a live sports or broadcast production environment. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with live event production and familiarity with ESPN or similar network workflows preferred.   Special or Physical Requirements: Ability to work extended hours, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Working knowledge of live production environments and broadcast workflows required. Experience with Ross XPression, replay systems, and control room equipment preferred. Must demonstrate the ability to work under tight deadlines, manage multiple responsibilities, and contribute in a fast-paced environment. Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with students, staff, freelance crew, and external partners are essential.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire. Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary range, please contact Lee Scioneaux at scioneaux@lsu.edu     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 8, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 5, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/2800-BEC-North-Undergrad-Pavilion/Assistant---Associate---Full-Professor_R00117021": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant / Associate / Full Professor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUAM COB - School of Accounting (Dana Hollie (00008223))     Work Location: 2800 BEC North Undergrad Pavilion     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: Perform scholarly research with the expectation of publication in top accounting journals, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels; serve on dissertation committees; provide service to the University and also to the profession. We are particularly interested in scholars with research and teaching interests in financial accounting, auditing, taxation, and managerial accounting. Full Professor with tenure will be considered for the Thomas Daigre Endowed Chair of Business Administration. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: 50% - Teach undergraduate and graduate classes in the Department of Accounting 50% - Perform scholarly research with the expectation of publication in top accounting; serve on dissertation committees; provide service to the University and to the profession. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education Level: PhD in Accounting or related field Assistant Professor applicants must have PhD in Acct. or related field; (ABD candidates considered but degree must be conferred by 08/14/27) Associate Professor applicants must have a PhD in Accounting or related field and hold the title of Assistant or Associate Professor at another university Full Professor applicants must possess a PhD in Accounting or related field and hold the title of Associate Professor or Full Professor at 