    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/2214G-Patrick-F-Taylor-Hall/Assistant-Dean-of-Strategy-and-Communications_R00116203": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Strategy and Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Dean of Strategy and Communications     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM College of Engineering (Vicki Colvin (00089820))     Work Location: 2214G Patrick F. Taylor Hall     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: This role ensures alignment with the College's strategic direction while addressing wide-ranging audiences with available resources. The Assistant Dean identifies, manages, and reduces risks, provides the Dean with executive communications support, assists College deans and department chairs through coaching and strategic conversations, and works closely with LSU communication leaders to meet the university’s public affairs goals. The Assistant Dean serves as the primary advisor to College leadership on messaging, public speaking, and stakeholder engagement, ensuring that communications drive progress for the College and LSU. This leader will be both a strategist and advisor and a hands-on contributor who can write and edit a variety of materials, from memos to messaging, communications plans to press pitches. With exceptional judgment and discretion, a pro-active, data-driven approach, and a strong command of communications platforms such as Cision and Meltwater, the Assistant Dean is instrumental in building the reputation of the College and meeting its goals for improving education, research, and service to Louisiana.   30% Strategic Planning and Execution: Establish and drive a multi-channel communications strategy for the College that reflects the priorities of the College’s academic and research leaders and aligns with university strategy. This will include both internal and external audiences and channels. Serve as a key member of the Dean’s administrative team, contributing to college planning and advising leaders on communications. Lead communications projects with significant potential to drive progress toward College goals, including impact reporting, major program announcements, and alumni and donor engagement. Continuously review audiences, messaging, and outreach with an eye toward effectiveness and efficiency. 30% Team Management and Development: Supervise a team of communication professionals, providing tailored support, direction, and mentorship. Model and build a culture of collaboration, curiosity, and excellence and a positive, pro-active, problem-solving mindset. Actively and consistently encourage each team member’s learning and growth, and equip them with the resources they need, in order to meet high performance standards, build morale, and maintain consistency in communications efforts. Review employee performance, oversee professional development, and build and manage a team budget. 20% Collaboration and Partnerships: Work closely with College deans, department heads, faculty, and staff to align communication efforts with institutional priorities and initiatives. Establish strong ties with cross-sector partners inside and outside of the university, including the LSU communications team members, LSU Foundation staff, industry partners, and government agencies to strengthen the College’s expanding public and private partnerships. 10% Support for Leadership: Provide coaching and support to academic leaders and spokespeople to develop clear and concise messaging that aligns with the College's strategy. Develop impactful talking points that convey leadership’s strategic priorities, fostering connection and trust among stakeholders. 10%Support College Leadership:  Provide coaching and support to academic leaders and spokespeople to develop clear and concise messaging that aligns with the College's strategy. Develop talking points, issues briefs, and project plans that convey priorities, foster connection, and build trust among stakeholders. Lead all communications efforts for the Dean, collaborating with the Dean’s Executive Assistant and other members of the communications team. 10% Analyze Performance and Measure Impact: Identify, collect, and analyze metrics and qualitative data such as surveys and focus groups to evaluate the impact of communication strategies and demonstrate return on investment. Continuously monitor and adopt new and effective tools, such as AI applications and new content management or design platforms, that improve the work of the team. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree and 7 years of related experience. LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply--a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Additional Information: Due to the nature of the position and/or responsibilities, in times of emergencies and/or University closures, this position is considered essential. It may be required to assist the Office of Communications and University Relations on necessary communications matters in times of crisis, including potentially working in LSUs Emergency Operations Center during those times.      Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide resume, cover letter and 3 professional references. For questions regarding the status or pay for the position, please reach out to Jessica Waters at jessicawaters@lsu.edu.     Posting Date: June 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 30, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/William-B-Hatcher-Hall/Study-Abroad-Advisor_R00110639": {
      "title": "Study Abroad Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Study Abroad Advisor     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM AA - OGE - Programs Abroad (Shelly Royer-Fremaux (00284961))     Work Location: William B. Hatcher Hall     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The Study Abroad Advisor is responsible for recruiting and advising study abroad students from assigned colleges for semester and summer Study Abroad programs, including but not limited to exchanges, direct enroll, and affiliate partners.  This position supports the students throughout the Study Abroad process from initial inquiry to returnee stage. The position works with students to collect and organize LSU Study Abroad required documentation, manage tracking mechanisms, maintain required documents, forms, and processes, etc. Salary Range:  $42,960-$51,553 Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications within the posted range. Job Responsibilities Advising Duties & Responsibilities (60%): Advises students from assigned college(s) throughout the process on study abroad program opportunities and requirements, administers acceptance decisions, and promotes the program through outreach to the university community. Advising may include information about major/minor/elective requirements, financial aid, scholarships, credit transfer, and other topics. Maintains expert understanding of University policies pertaining to academic programs abroad. Responds to inquiries from students, parents, faculty, and others regarding program policies, procedures, and requirements, making referrals as appropriate. Advises on the Benjamin A Gilman, Boren, Critical Language Scholarship, Study Abroad scholarships, and other scholarship opportunities. Maintains accurate applicant data, runs reports, and manages website information through the Terra Dotta application site. Maintains effective relationships with academic and administrative departments, as well as overseas partners and program providers. Acts as liaison between the overseas partner/program provider and students for education abroad and exchange purposes. Programming Operations (30%) Develops and executes a marketing and recruitment plan, but not limited to, bi-annual Education Abroad fairs, information sessions, pre-departure orientation, and re-entry sessions.   Facilitates student pre-departure orientation for faculty-led and semester-long students in collaboration with team members Identifies special projects and partners with the Director of Study Abroad to further the goals of the Study Abroad Office. Professional Development (10%) Ensures program quality and continual self-development through self-directed learning, professional development, and appropriate site visits. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Requirements FERPA - As with all LSU employees, due to this position title and/or responsibilities, this position has an obligation to assist students in the acquisition of necessary services. Should a student appear in need of or seek assistance with issues of an emotional, behavioral, or mental health-related matter, they should be referred to the proper service within the Student Health Center. In situations where the student creates an impression that they are a danger to themselves or others, the advisor should immediately contact the Care Team, the Dean of Students, or the appropriate law enforcement agency. The employee outside of those rights contained within FERPA should create no impression of client or patient confidentiality. Additional Information Ability to work occasional nights and/or weekends as required.  Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree Specific Experience: Proficiency with Terra Dotta software. Experience studying, living, or working abroad. Experience with education abroad and/or academic advising. Familiar with developing and implementing marketing plans across multiple platforms. Job Competencies The ideal candidate will possess the following competencies: Highly proficient in Microsoft Office products, including Excel, PowerPoint, and Word. ( Advanced) Demonstrate excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. (Proficient) Ability to problem solve, organize, and complete multiple tasks simultaneously with close attention to detail. (Proficient) Ability to work effectively independently and within groups (Proficient)     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Shelly Royer-Fremaux at sroyer4@lsu.edu.     Posting Date: June 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 30, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/3325-Patrick-F-Taylor-Hall/Research-Associate-5_R00115862": {
      "title": "Research Associate 5",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Research Associate 5     Position Type: Other Academic     Department: LSUAM Engineering - School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Shuangqing Wei (00007502))     Work Location: 3325 Patrick F. Taylor Hall     Pay Grade:     Job Description: The Research Associate 5 candidate for the Electrical and Computer Engineering department will manage, oversee, and design engineering simulations, experiments and/or tests and collect data to ensure data integrity/control. Conduct research to identify solutions for data-driven modeling, communications, and networking of distributed maritime operations undertaken by both surface and underwater marine vehicles.  Provides direct management support in initiating and developing contacts with grant/contract agencies and sources and in developing funding sources. 60% Conduct research on modeling, communications, networking, and machine learning techniques for distributed maritime operations undertaken by both surface and underwater marine vehicles. Design algorithmic and software tools for decision making, communications, networking, and intelligent autonomous operations. Maintain currency of knowledge regarding relevant state-of-the-art technologies, equipment, systems, and machine learning methods. 35% Manage and supervise graduate students and coordinate research activities within the project task groups. Support the development of research proposals and oversee the preparation of monthly and quarterly reports associated with the task groups led under the project. Manage and coordinate project roles, research tasks, and technical deliverables. 5% Other duties as assigned.  Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in mechanical, electrical, or computer engineering, computer science, or robotics and 2 years of related experience as a research assistant in an area relevant to this position. Degree Substitute: Ph.D in related field. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D in mechanical, electrical, or computer engineering, computer science, or robotics and 4 years of related experience. This position is not eligible for sponsorship.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please attach three professional references and a copy of transcripts when applying. Official Transcripts required prior to hire. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Shuangqing Wei at swei@lsu.edu. This position is considered a research or research-related support position and must undergo screenings per RS 17.     Posting Date: May 28, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): November 24, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
