    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-Science-And-Technology-Building/Physical-Therapy-Assistant-Program-Director_R00115763": {
      "title": "Physical Therapy Assistant Program Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Physical Therapy Assistant Program Director     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUE AA - Health Sciences Business Technology (Kristie Broussard (00056048))     Work Location: Health Science And Technology Building     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The PTA Program Director serves as the academic and administrative leader responsible for ensuring the program meets CAPTE accreditation standards. Their primary purpose is to develop, maintain, and enhance a high-quality educational program that prepares students to become competent, ethical, and licensed physical therapist assistants. Job Responsibilities: 50% Organize and assure program effectiveness; conduct on-going program review and assessment; evaluate outcome measurements and effectiveness of the program; timely and periodic communication with officers of CAPTE as needed (substantive changes, annual report, etc); keep the Dean of the Division of Health Sciences and Business Technology apprised of problems pertaining to the overall operation of the Program. 15% Participate in continued development and budget planning; accept committee assignments, either departmental or university, and contribute to the welfare of the institution; assist in the recruitment of qualified students and faculty. 10% Provide leadership for PTA faculty and students by developing and participating in activities that promote the image and involvement of the PTA profession. 10% Conduct regular meetings with faculty and with communities of interest while maintaining documentation; evaluate all PTA faculty members on a regular basis. 10% In cooperation with the DCE/ACCE, the Program Director shall ensure that non-clinical units of instruction are properly coordinated and that all students receive didactic and laboratory instruction sufficient to ensure adequate background for entry into practice. Maintain academic records on all students enrolled in the clinical phase of the Program; assure that appropriate and relevant student, faculty, and clinical agency evaluations and surveys are developed and utilized. 5% Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Master's Degree Minimum of five years, full-time, post licensure experience that includes a minimum of three years of full-time clinical experience. Experience in classroom, lab, or clinical teaching experience Experience in administration, management, and leadership. (clinic experience acceptable) Professional development or education in educational theory and methodology, instructional design, student evaluation, and outcome assessment. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D Preferred: Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Eight years, full-time, post licensure experience that includes a minimum of five years of full-time clinical experience. Experience in classroom, lab, or clinical teaching experience Experience in administration, management, and leadership. (clinic experience acceptable) Professional development or education in educational theory and methodology, instructional design, student evaluation, and outcome assessment. Salary Range: $70,000.00-$85,000.00     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: 60 contact hours of professional development or education comprising exclusively and comprehensively the four content areas of: education theory and methodology, instructional design, student evaluation and outcome assessment or ABPTRFE Faculty (non-clinical) Residency program completion.     Posting Date: May 21, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!    Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUE is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSUE Human Resources Management Office at 337-550-1222 or emailed at hr@lsue.edu ."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0340-Fred-C-Frey-Computing-Services-Building/AI-Architect_R00115650": {
      "title": "AI Architect",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: AI Architect     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM FA - ITS - TA - RETS - HPC - User Services (Le Yan (00011962))     Work Location: 0340 Fred C. Frey Computing Services Building     Pay Grade: Professional     Job Description: The AI Architect will lead the design, implementation, and ongoing development of ITS AI infrastructure and services in support of LSU’s research, teaching, and operational needs. Work closely with researchers, faculty, staff, and campus partners to assess requirements, develop AI solutions, and deploy AI tools and services. Job Responsibilities: Consultation and collaboration: Engage with researchers and department heads to assess AI-related needs and offer tailored guidance and support. Identify opportunities where AI technologies can improve research, teaching, service delivery, or operational efficiency. Collaborate with researchers to assist with developing and maintaining AI services, including data acquisition, preprocessing, model training, and deployment. Research, evaluate, and recommend AI services models that meet business objectives and performance requirements. Work with customers and stakeholders to understand their AI requirements and provide guidance on how AI can be used to improve institutional goals. (35%) Technical support: Design, deploy, and support AI computing environments across on-premises, cloud, and hybrid infrastructure. Research, recommend, and implement AI tools and applications, and serve as a primary technical liaison for supported platforms and services. Assist researchers and campus users with setup, configuration, and troubleshooting of AI computing environments, including HPC systems, cloud services, containers, and specialized software. Collaborate with the HPC team and other ITS units on shared infrastructure and service delivery. (35%) Data management: Support the effective use of secure, cloud, on-premises, and open computing and storage environments for AI workloads. Advise users on data handling, storage, movement, and operational considerations related to AI workflows. Help ensure AI services are reliable, maintainable, and aligned with institutional practices for security, access, and sustainability. (20%) Service Development and Continuous Improvement: Stay current with emerging AI technologies, platforms, and practices relevant to higher education and research computing. Contribute to service planning, documentation, and technical decision-making for ITS AI offerings. Help define and improve processes, standards, and support models for AI services as the program matures. Perform other duties as assigned. (10%) Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree with 3 years IT experience with a variety of technologies including AI infrastructure/architecture, managing compute and storage, networking, using and recommending applications, researching solutions for customer use.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with a variety of researchers.  Demonstrated ability to work independently, manage multiple projects, and meet deadlines. +LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or a related field. 5 years experience upporting AI/ML, HPC, GPU-enabled computing, or research computing services in higher education, research, or enterprise environments. Familiarity with AI/ML frameworks, containers, APIs, model deployment workflows, and related tooling. Experience with both on-premises and cloud-based infrastructure for AI or advanced computing workloads. Experience providing consultation, training, or technical guidance to researchers or other advanced users. Familiarity with data security, access controls, and operational considerations for sensitive or regulated workloads. Additional Requirements: ​ This position may be required to report to campus in times of emergency and/or closure per PS-18. ​     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required prior to hire. Please provide three professional references including name, title, phone number and e-mail address. An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Mary Bordelon at mbordelon@lsu.edu     Posting Date: May 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 16, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N): Y     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
