    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/1079-Digital-Media-Center/Postdoctoral-Researcher_R00115639-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Postdoctoral Researcher     Position Type: Professional / Unclassified     Department: LSUAM ORED - CCT - Software Development (Hartmut Kaiser (00001446))     Work Location: 1079 Digital Media Center     Pay Grade: Other Academic     Job Description: We seek a postdoctoral associate to develop and prototype frameworks that integrate quantum computing resources with high performance computing (HPC) systems. The project will focus on extending the C++ based HPX runtime (hpx.stellar-group.org) to orchestrate hybrid quantum classical and quantum-simulation workloads, enabling scalable quantum accelerated algorithms for scientific and engineering applications. The position offers a strong interdisciplinary environment, opportunities for collaborative publications, and the chance to build an independent research profile at the computational–physics interface. Job Responsibilities: Research and Development: Design and implement HPX extensions that schedule quantum kernels on remote quantum processors alongside classical tasks. Develop C++ libraries and APIs that expose quantum circuit execution, error mitigation, and data movement. Benchmark hybrid workloads. (65%) Collaboration: Work with faculty, students, and external partners on interdisciplinary initiatives aimed at applications in quantum computing; contribute to joint problem-solving and co-mentorship of graduate students. (20%) Dissemination: Prepare manuscripts for peer-reviewed publications, technical reports, and presentations at national/international conferences. (10%) Other duties as assigned. (5%) Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D in Computer Science, Physics, Electrical Engineering, or related field. Expert level C++ (C++17/20) and experience with parallel runtime systems, preferably HPX. Also, Hands on experience with quantum programming frameworks (Qiskit, Cirq, or similar) and understanding of quantum algorithms.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and three (3) professional references including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. Please attach ALL required documents under the \"Resume/CV\" section of your application. A copy of your transcript(s) may be attached to your application (if available). However, original transcripts are required before hiring. Due to the nature of the position and/or position responsibilities, this position shall be subject to pre-employment screenings in accordance with University Policy as required and RS:17 screenings (https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?p=y&d=1297548). For questions or concerns about updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Dr. Hartmut Kaiser at hkaiser@lsu.edu.     Posting Date: May 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 16, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/0222-AT-Prescott-Hall/Virtual---Research-Mentor_R00115572": {
      "title": "Virtual - Research Mentor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Virtual - Research Mentor     Position Type: Non-Employee Wages as Earned (Fixed Term)     Department: LSUAM AA - APSS - CainCtr - Business Management - WAEs (Katilyn Simpson Hebert (00067718))     Work Location: 0222 A.T. Prescott Hall     Pay Grade:     Job Description: Research mentors plan 3-4 potential mathematics research projects accessible to high school students. At the start of Math Circle, they present their proposals, and will ultimately be assigned to two groups of 2-4 students each. For the rest of the program, they are responsible for virtually supervising these students and guiding them through their research project, as well as aiding them in preparing their presentation at the end of the program. Job Responsibilities Plan 3-4 potential mathematics research projects accessible to high school students. (50%) Virtually supervise selected students through projects. (25%) Administer final project presentation. (25%) Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree LSU values skills, experience, and expertise. Candidates who have relevant experience in key job responsibilities are encouraged to apply— a degree is not required as long as the candidate meets the required years of experience specified in the job description.     Additional Job Description: Special Instructions: Please provide a resume and three professional references, including name, title, phone number, and e-mail address. For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact Katilyn Hebert at ksimps10@lsu.edu.     Posting Date: May 19, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): September 15, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     All candidates must have valid U.S. work authorization at the time of hire and maintain that valid work authorization throughout employment. Changes in laws, regulations, or government policies may impact the university’s ability to employ individuals in certain positions.     HCM Contact Information: For questions or concerns related to updating your application with attachments (e.g., resumes, RS:17 documents), date of birth, or reactivating applications, please contact the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 225-578-8200 or email HR@lsu.edu .  For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or salary ranges, please contact the department using the information provided in the Special Instructions section of this job posting."
